study_a;54;ctrl_a_0054;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.851863+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"It Sounds Like Your Body Is Holding Onto A Deep Need To Protect You, Even As Your Heart Longs For Connection. That Tension Between Missing Who You Were And Feeling Stuck In This New Reality Must Be So Heavy. Maybe There’s Space To Gently Explore What Touch Feels Safe Now—even Something Small, Like A Warm Drink In Your Hands Or A Soft Blanket—to Slowly Rebuild Trust With Your Own Senses. You Don’t Have To Force The Old Gestures; Healing Might Look Like Discovering New Ways To Feel Grounded And Present. Your Care For Others Still Exists—it’s Just Learning To Coexist With The Parts Of You That Needed To Step In To Keep You Safe. What Does Your Body Seem To Ask For In Those Moments When Closeness Feels Hard?";11388
