study_a;85;ctrl_a_0085;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.864489+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Really Tough To Feel Stuck In This Cycle Of Frustration—both With The Arguments And With Being Hard On Yourself. When Emotions Run High, It’s Natural To Feel Overwhelmed Or Like You’re Not Being Heard. Could We Explore Ways To Slow Things Down In Those Moments, So You Have Space To Reconnect With What *you* Need? Sometimes Writing Down Thoughts Beforehand Or Taking A Pause Mid-conversation Can Help Untangle The Pressure To Respond Quickly. How Does That Land With You?;470
study_a;86;ctrl_a_0086;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.865116+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like This Pursuit Has Held Deep Meaning For You, And Perhaps Some Frustration Too—feeling Like There’s A State Of Being Just Out Of Reach. What If We Gently Explore What *your* Relationship With Consciousness Feels Like Now, Not As Something To Attain, But As Something To Notice Unfolding Within You?;2581
study_a;87;ctrl_a_0087;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.865633+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Takes Real Courage To Share When It Feels Uncomfortable—thank You For Trusting This Space, Even When It’s Hard. It Makes Sense To Protect Yourself By Avoiding Tough Feelings, Especially When Life *looks* Okay But Doesn’t *feel* Okay. What If We Gently Explored What Happens When Those Emotions Stay Unspoken? You’re Not Alone Here—we’ll Move At Your Pace.;3115
study_a;88;ctrl_a_0088;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.866095+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It’s Powerful That You’re Letting Yourself Name This Anger And Feel It Fully, Without Judgment. Sometimes Just Naming It—letting It Take Up Space—is Its Own Kind Of Healing. You Don’t Have To “fix” It Or Act On It. You’re Honoring Your Truth, And That In Itself Is A Step. I’m Here To Hold That Space With You, Whenever You Need.;5296
study_a;89;ctrl_a_0089;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.866433+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;I Hear How Heavy This Feels—like The Color Has Drained From Things That Once Mattered. Let’s Sit With This Together. Would You Be Open To Gently Exploring What Happens In Your Mind And Body When You Try To Engage With Even Small Moments Of Your Day? Sometimes, Tracing Those Patterns Can Reveal Steps Toward Reconnecting With What Brings Light. You’re Not Alone In This.;10477
study_a;90;ctrl_a_0090;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.866967+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;That Sounds Like Such A Profound Struggle—carrying That Weight Through Every Small Step. It Takes Real Courage To Keep Moving When Even The Basics Feel Impossible. The Shame Makes Sense, But So Does The Pride: You’re Showing Up For Yourself Even When It’s This Hard. Maybe There’s Space To Hold Both Feelings Gently, Without Letting One Drown Out The Other. What If Exhaustion Isn’t A Sign Of Failure, But Proof Of How Fiercely You’re Trying? You’re Not Just “dragging” Yourself—you’re *persisting*. That Matters.;10541
study_a;91;ctrl_a_0091;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.867506+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Carrying So Much Weight Right Now—this Exhaustion And Loneliness Are Real, And I Want You To Know They Matter. When You Say “nothing Changes,” I Wonder What It Might Look Like To Pause And Honor How Hard You’ve Been Pushing, Even When It Feels Thankless. Sometimes, When We’re Running In Place, It’s Because Part Of Us Needs To Be Heard, Not Pushed Harder. Could We Explore What *you* Need In This Moment, Without Comparing It To Others’ Journeys? You Don’t Have To Figure It All Out Alone—we Can Sit With This Together, One Step At A Time.;13839
study_a;92;ctrl_a_0092;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.868071+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like This Relationship Left You Questioning Your Own Vibrancy In Ways Your Friendships Don’t—almost Like Parts Of You Dimmed When You Were Together, Even If You Can’t Pinpoint Why. That Mismatch Between How You Feel Around Others Versus How You Felt With Him Must Be So Confusing. When Someone’s Presence Makes Us Doubt Our Worth, It Often Says More About The Connection Than About Us. Maybe Exploring What Felt Different With Him—the Moments You Held Back, Or The Ways You Were Received—could Help Untangle Why His Opinion Weighs So Heavily Now. You Deserve Relationships That Make You Feel *more* Like Yourself, Not Less. Your Friends Clearly See And Value Your Light. What If This Isn’t About Being “boring,” But About Learning To Trust The Version Of You They Reflect—the One Who’s Already Enough?;4906
study_a;93;ctrl_a_0093;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.868642+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"I’m So Sorry You’re Carrying This Weight. It Makes Sense To Feel Terrified When Stability Slips Away Like This. Let’s Pause For A Moment—what’s One Small Step That Feels Possible Today? Maybe Calling A Local Shelter Or Outreach Program? You Don’t Have To Face This Alone; There Are People Who Want To Help. We Can Figure This Out Together, One Breath At A Time.";12247
study_a;94;ctrl_a_0094;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.869129+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like That Mix Of Humor And Genuine Worry Is Keeping You Up At Night—both The Laughable Moments And The Underlying Stress About Doing Right By Your Pup. It Makes Sense To Feel That Tension. Could It Help To Explore What This Situation Brings Up For *you*? Not Just The Googling, But The Care Behind It—the Part Of You That Wants To Get This Right. Sometimes Our Pets Mirror Our Own Need For Patience, Both With Them And Ourselves. What If Curiosity, Not Worry, Guided Those Late-night Searches? You’re Clearly Dedicated—how Might That Dedication Feel Lighter?;18145
study_a;95;ctrl_a_0095;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.869693+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"Your Heart Is Wrestling With So Much—wanting Connection But Needing Protection. That Shutdown Response Makes Sense If Being Near Him Stirs Old Wounds. It’s Okay To Honor Both Your Longing *and* Your Boundaries. Healing Isn’t About Rushing To Forgive; It’s About Giving Yourself Space To Feel Safe First. What Would Feel Gentle To *you* Right Now?";15224
study_a;96;ctrl_a_0096;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.870166+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It’s Completely Understandable To Feel Both Thrilled And Uneasy About Such A Big Step. This Role Matters Deeply To You, And That Care Is Why You Want To Do Well. Those “what Ifs” Can Feel Heavy, But They’re Often Stories We Tell Ourselves When We’re Stretching Beyond What’s Familiar. What Would It Look Like To Gently Challenge Those Doubts? For Example: What Evidence Do You Have That You *are* Ready, Even In Small Ways? How Might You Lean Into The Excitement While Making Space For The Learning Curve? You’re Not Alone In This Transition—what Support Do You Think Would Help You Feel Steadier?;13462
study_a;97;ctrl_a_0097;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.870793+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;Your Dedication To Finding A Connection That Aligns With Your Values Isn’t Asking Too Much—it’s Honoring What Matters Deeply To You. That Longing For Someone Who Truly Understands Your Commitment Might Feel Isolating Now, But It Also Shows How Clearly You Know Your Heart. When We Hold Space For What Feels Authentic, Even When It’s Hard, We Create Room For Relationships That Can Grow In Depth Over Time. What Would It Look Like To Nurture Patience With Yourself While Staying Open To Moments Of Connection, Even Small Ones, That Reflect Pieces Of What You Value? Sometimes The People Who “fit” Enter Our Lives In Unexpected Ways When We Least Anticipate It. You’re Not Alone In Wanting More Than Surface-level Bonds—that’s A Human Need. How Does It Feel To Consider That Your Standards, While Specific, Might Actually Guide You Toward What You Deserve Rather Than Limit You?;11274
study_a;98;ctrl_a_0098;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.871390+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like These Shifts Between Such Intense Energy And Subsequent Exhaustion Are Really Confusing And Draining For You. It’s Understandable To Feel Concerned, Especially When Actions Like Spending Affect Parts Of Your Life. Could We Explore What These Moments Feel Like In Your Body And Thoughts, And How They Connect To What’s Happening Around Or Within You? Sometimes Tracking When They Arise—even Without Obvious Triggers—can Help Us Notice Subtle Patterns. Would You Feel Open To Gently Observing These Shifts Together, So We Can Find Ways To Ground And Care For You Through Both The Highs And Lows? You’re Not Alone In Figuring This Out.;93
study_a;99;ctrl_a_0099;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.871869+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It’s So Human To Feel Both Relief And Guilt—like Your Heart Is Split Between Caring For Yourself And Worrying About Their Feelings. That Tension Can Be Exhausting. What If, For A Moment, You Let The Relief Guide You? It Might Be Telling You Something Important About What You Needed. The Guilt Doesn’t Erase That Truth. When The Doubts Creep In, Could You Try To Hold Space For *both* Feelings—honoring Your Need To Breathe While Gently Asking, “Did I Act From Hurt, Or From Care For Us Both?” Sometimes The Answer Reveals More Kindness Than Guilt Lets You See.;16789
study_a;100;ctrl_a_0100;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.872214+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It’s Powerful That You Recognize The Need To Nurture Your Own Well-being First—that’s A Meaningful Step Toward Growth. What Does Advocating For Yourself Look Like Right Now? Maybe Starting Small, Like Honoring Your Limits Or Speaking Up About What You Need. When We Fill Our Own Cup, We’re Better Able To Pour Into Others. What Feels Most Vital To Prioritize Today?;1403
study_a;101;ctrl_a_0101;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.872697+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’ve Been A Steady Source Of Care And Support For Her During A Deeply Challenging Time. How Does It Feel To Reflect On That Experience Now? Do You Sense Any Lingering Emotions, Or Perhaps Ways That Period Still Shapes Your Relationship Today? I’m Here To Listen As You Unpack This.;1660
study_a;102;ctrl_a_0102;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.873096+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;I Hear How Heavy This Feels—like You’re Carrying A Weight That Never Lifts. It’s Exhausting To Keep Pushing When Hope Feels Out Of Reach. You’re Not Alone In This, Even If It Seems That Way Right Now. Would It Help To Unpack Some Of What’s Drowning You? Sometimes Naming The Waves Can Make Them Feel Smaller, And We Can Find Pockets Of Air Together.;11240
study_a;103;ctrl_a_0103;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.873621+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It’s So Hard To Carry This Worry From Afar—you Care Deeply, And That Love Matters. When She’s Ready, Maybe Ask What *feels* Helpful Right Now: Talking Through Grounding Steps (like Breath Or A Safe-room Checklist), Or Brainstorming Trusted People Nearby Who Could Stay With Her. You’re Already Helping By Holding Space For Her Pain—and Your Own. Let’s Explore Ways To Nurture Both.;14265
study_a;104;ctrl_a_0104;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.874077+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"It Sounds Like This Urgency Feels Heavy—like You’re Racing Against Time. That Fear Of ""what If"" Can Be Paralyzing. What If, Instead Of Needing To Do It ""right,"" You Gave Yourself Permission To Explore The Workbook In Small, Curious Steps? Even A Page Or A Sentence Could Be A Start. Mistakes Aren’t Failures—they’re Part Of Learning What Works For *you*. The Fact That You’re Reaching Out Shows How Much You Care About Your Growth. Let’s Honor That Courage First.";16410
study_a;105;ctrl_a_0105;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.874713+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It’s So Brave To Reach For Connection When You’ve Felt Alone—it Makes Sense To Feel Both Relief And Fear. Finding People Who “get It” Can Be Like Discovering Shelter In A Storm. It’s Okay To Hold Both Hope And Uncertainty Gently. What If, For Now, You Let This Space Remind You That Support Exists, Even When Doubts Arise? You’re Building Steps Toward Trust In Yourself, And That’s Worth Honoring.;11817
study_a;106;ctrl_a_0106;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.875275+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;Reaching Out When So Much Feels Uncertain Must Be Incredibly Vulnerable. That Heaviness In Your Chest Might Be Holding All The Unspoken Words And The Ache Of Those Missing Memories. What If You Began With Something Small, Like Writing Down One Thing You *do* Remember—or Even Just How Much You Wish You Could? You Don’t Have To Have All The Answers To Honor That Longing To Connect. The Silence Between You And His Brother Isn’t Yours To Carry Alone—maybe Sharing That Weight Could Soften It, Even Just A Little.;11889
study_a;107;ctrl_a_0107;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.875769+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Carrying So Much Weight, Even Amid These Huge Steps Forward. Sobriety And Success Don’t Always Quiet The Storm Inside, Do They? Let’s Slow Down And Explore What *you* Need To Feel Connected To Life Again—not Just What Others See Or Expect. What Small Thing, Even Just A Flicker, Still Matters To You? We Can Start There.;10661
study_a;108;ctrl_a_0108;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.876323+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like The Weight Of The World Feels Heavy On Your Shoulders Right Now—that’s So Understandable. When Those “what If” Thoughts Spiral At Night, Maybe We Could Explore Gently Untangling Them Together. What If We Tried Grounding Those Worries In The Present, Moment By Moment, And Noticed What Feels Within Your Control? Small Steps Can Create Space To Breathe Again. You’re Not Alone In This.;11109
study_a;109;ctrl_a_0109;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.876593+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It’s Brave To Reach Out For Support, And I’m Here To Help You Navigate This. Let’s Start By Understanding What Feels Most Pressing For You Now. We Can Explore Your Thoughts And Emotions Through Gentle, Open Conversations—like Untangling Threads To See Patterns Or Connections You Might Not Notice Alone. If You’d Like, We Could Also Try Small, Practical Steps To Help You Feel Grounded When Things Feel Unclear. Sometimes Looking At Challenges From Different Angles—like How They Show Up In Relationships, Daily Habits, Or Even Unspoken Expectations—can Reveal New Paths Forward. What Matters Most Is Creating A Space Where You Feel Safe To Experiment, Reflect, And Discover What Resonates For *you*. Would You Want To Share A Specific Situation Or Feeling You’d Like To Start With?;6569
study_a;110;ctrl_a_0110;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.876983+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"It Takes Courage To Carry Such A Shift In Perspective—to See Life Through Experiences Others Might Not Fully Grasp. That Distance You Feel Makes Sense; You’ve Walked Paths That Reshape How You Value Things, And It’s Lonely When That Isn’t Shared. You’re Not Wrong For Feeling Changed. Would It Help To Gently Explore What Parts Of This ""gap"" Feel Most Heavy? Maybe Through Stories Of What Matters To You Now, Or What You Wish Others Could Understand? Sometimes, Naming Those Unspoken Layers Can Soften The Weight, Even If Others Aren’t There Yet. I’m Here To Listen, Wherever You’d Like To Start.";4123
study_a;111;ctrl_a_0111;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.877489+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like That Situation Stirred Up Some Intense Feelings For You, Especially Since It’s Happened Before. Feeling Uncomfortable And Aggravated Makes Sense When Someone’s Actions Keep Crossing Into Your Space. Can You Share More About What Those Moments Felt Like In Your Body And Mind? Did Any Memories Or Older Worries Surface As It Happened? Sometimes Our Reactions In The Present Connect To Deeper Needs For Safety Or Respect. Let’s Explore How You Might Honor Those Feelings While Finding Ways To Feel Grounded Again. You’re Not Alone In This.;3645
study_a;112;ctrl_a_0112;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.877966+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;I’m So Sorry You’re Carrying This Weight—it Sounds Unbearable. When Stress Feels Like Fire In Your Mind, It’s Your Whole Body Screaming For Relief. Let’s Slow This Down Together. What If, For Now, You Focus On One Breath, One Task, Or Even One Hour At A Time? Overwhelm Shrinks When We Break It Into Pieces. Can We Explore What *needs* Your Attention Most Urgently, And What Might Wait? You’re Not Failing—you’re Surviving A Storm. Would It Feel Possible To Share This Load With Someone You Trust? You Don’t Have To White-knuckle Through Alone.;17243
study_a;113;ctrl_a_0113;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.878422+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"Your Pain Is So Deep And Real—it’s Okay To Feel This Heaviness. What Happened To You Matters, And Your Grief, Anger, And Guilt Are All Valid. Healing Isn’t About “moving On” But Finding Ways To Carry This With Care For Yourself. Could We Gently Explore How To Rebuild A Sense Of Safety In Your Body And Heart, Step By Step? You Don’t Have To Face The Hurt In Your Husband’s Eyes Alone—what If We Worked On Ways To Share This Burden Together, When You’re Ready? You’re Not Broken; You’re Surviving, And That Takes Courage.";15025
study_a;114;ctrl_a_0114;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.878815+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Asking For Recognition Of Your Capabilities And Worth, Which Is Completely Valid. Let’s Explore Ways To Express Your Need For Acknowledgment In Relationships Or Environments Where You Feel Overlooked. Would Practicing Assertive Communication Or Reflecting On Moments You Felt Respected Help Clarify What Changes Might Foster That Feeling? You Deserve To Feel Valued.;3435
study_a;115;ctrl_a_0115;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.879244+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;Your Mom’s Strength And Your Own Commitment To Generosity Speak Volumes About The Values You Hold Close. It Sounds Like Honoring That Part Of Yourself—giving Freely, Without Shrinking For Others’ Judgments—is Deeply Tied To Your Sense Of Integrity. How Does It Feel To Carry That Legacy Forward In Your Own Way?;1203
study_a;116;ctrl_a_0116;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.879657+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"It Sounds Like You’ve Been Carrying A Lot Since Losing Your Mom, And Maybe The Drinking Has Become A Way To Cope With That Weight—even If It Feels ""social"" On The Surface. Would It Help To Gently Explore How Your Relationship With Alcohol Has Shifted Since Her Passing, And What It Might Be Covering Up? You’re Not Alone In This; We Can Take It Step By Step.";1992
study_a;117;ctrl_a_0117;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.879986+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;This Uncertainty Can Feel So Heavy, Can’t It? Career Shifts Often Stir Up Deeper Questions About What Truly Matters To Us. If It Feels Right, We Could Gently Explore Moments In Your Past Work Or Life Where You Felt Energized Or Proud—not To Rush Toward Answers, But To Listen For Clues Your Experiences Might Be Sharing. How Does That Land?;170
study_a;118;ctrl_a_0118;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.880260+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"It’s Okay To Feel Uncertain—asking For Help Takes Courage. Let’s Slow Down And Explore What’s On Your Mind, One Step At A Time. I’ll Listen Without Judgment, And Together We Can Untangle These Feelings. You Don’t Have To Have Answers Right Now; Sometimes Just Naming What Feels Unclear Brings Relief.";2249
study_a;119;ctrl_a_0119;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.880646+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It’s Beautiful To Hear That Sense Of Lightness And Hope Emerging—like The Sun Breaking Through Clouds After A Storm. Hold That Feeling Gently, And If It Feels Right, Maybe Reflect On What Small Steps Or Shifts Helped That Weight Lift. Hope Can Be Fragile, But Even A Little Can Light The Way Forward. How Does This New Space Feel For You?;5687
study_a;120;ctrl_a_0120;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.881013+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’ve Carried So Much For Others, Perhaps Even Putting Their Needs Ahead Of Your Own For A Long Time. That Weight Can Feel Crushing When There’s No Space Left To Honor What *you* Need. What Would It Feel Like To Gently Ask Yourself: *“What Do I Truly Want To Carry, And What Might I Set Down?”* Sometimes, The Roles We’re Taught To Embrace Don’t Leave Room For Our Humanity—for Rest, For Imperfection, For Being Cared For, Too. You Deserve That Kindness.;471
study_a;121;ctrl_a_0121;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.881363+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;Your Feelings Make So Much Sense—being Overlooked In Such A Foundational Way Can Leave Deep Imprints. When Those Who Were Meant To Cherish Us Unconditionally Couldn’t Fully See Our Worth, It’s Natural To Question If We’re “enough.” That Ache Of Invisibility Is So Heavy To Carry. What If We Gently Explored How Those Old, Unspoken Messages Might Still Whisper In Your Choices Or Self-view Today? Sometimes Naming Those Quiet Hurts—and Grieving The Care You Deserved But Didn’t Receive—can Create Space To Rewrite The Story. You’ve Shown Such Strength In Trying To Earn Love, But Real Belonging Starts With Offering Yourself The Compassion They Couldn’t Give. What Would It Feel Like To Untangle Your Worth From Their Limitations?;7659
study_a;122;ctrl_a_0122;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.881756+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Carrying A Lot Of Weight Right Now—pressure From Outside And Uncertainty Within. Let’s Slow Down And Explore What Marriage Means *to You*. What Fears Come Up When You Imagine It? There’s No Rush To Meet Others’ Timelines—your Feelings Deserve Space And Care. How Does That Land?;8803
study_a;123;ctrl_a_0123;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.882163+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;That Sounds Really Overwhelming—like Your Emotions Are Suddenly Steering The Wheel, Even When You Want To Stay Grounded. It Takes So Much Strength To Carry That Frustration And Still Care About How It Affects Others. Would It Help To Explore What Might Be Beneath Those Waves? Sometimes Anger Is A Messenger—it Might Be Pointing To Unmet Needs, Old Hurts, Or Even Fear Of Losing Connection. What If We Gently Unpacked Those Moments Together, Looking For Patterns Or Triggers You Haven’t Noticed Yet? You’re Not Alone In This. Small Steps Toward Understanding Can Help You Feel More In Control Again.;13198
study_a;124;ctrl_a_0124;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.882581+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;I Can Hear How Heavy This Has Been For You—the Longing, The Strain With Hamid, The Weight Of Uncertainty. It’s So Human To Feel Grief And Fear When Something Deeply Wanted Feels Out Of Reach. Could We Explore Ways To Gently Reconnect With Hamid, Not To “fix” Things, But To Share This Ache Together? Sometimes Leaning Into Vulnerability, Even When It’s Scary, Can Soften The Distance. What Do You Think Might Help You Both Feel Seen And Held Right Now?;472
study_a;125;ctrl_a_0125;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.882956+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;I Hear How Heavy This Pain Feels, How It Wraps Around Every Part Of Your Day. You’re Carrying So Much Alone Right Now, And That Exhaustion Is Real. I Want You To Know This: Even When It Feels Impossible To See Light, Your Presence Matters. The Fact That You’re Sharing This Takes Courage, And I’m Here To Hold Space For All Of It. Let’s Slow Down And Breathe Together For A Moment. Could We Explore What Small Step Might Feel Manageable Today? Maybe Reaching Out To Someone You Trust, Even Just A Text, Or Naming One Thing That Feels Slightly Less Heavy? You Don’t Have To Figure This Out Alone—we Can Walk Through It, One Breath At A Time.;15409
study_a;126;ctrl_a_0126;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.883298+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;That’s Wonderful—you’ve Worked Hard In School And Have Such A Clear Passion For Baseball. What Do You Love Most About Playing? How Does It Feel When You Imagine Pursuing It After School? Let’s Explore How You Can Nurture Both Your Strengths And The Excitement You Have For This Next Step.;473
study_a;127;ctrl_a_0127;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.883842+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like This Shift In Your Routine Came With Some Urgency—like Part Of You Felt Pulled To Take Extra Care In A New Way. How Did It Feel, Physically And Emotionally, During Those Two Hours? And When You Spoke To Your Friend, Did Anything Come Up That Might’ve Nudged This Change? Sometimes Connections Between Conversations And Our Choices Aren’t Obvious At First. Let’s Explore What “being More Careful” Means To You Right Now—is It About Control, Safety, Or Something Else? I’m Here To Listen.;4513
