study_a;135;ctrl_a_0135;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.887489+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;I Hear How Deeply That Place Lives In Your Heart—the Warmth, The Light, The Smells That Carried Such Comfort. Grieving What’s Lost, Even A Place, Can Leave The World Feeling Hollow. Would It Help To Gently Explore What That Cottage Represented? Sometimes Giving Space To Those Memories Lets Us Carry Their Warmth Forward, Even Through The Ache.;14585
study_a;136;ctrl_a_0136;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.888053+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;That Sounds So Heavy To Carry—like No Matter How Much Care You Pour Into Your Work, It Gets Overshadowed By That Voice Whispering, “See? You’re Failing.” I Wonder… When You Stumbled Today, Could Part Of You Also Recognize The Courage It Took To Stand There And Try? Those Glances You Noticed—might They Have Held Curiosity, Not Judgment, At Times? What If We Gently Explored The Stories You Tell Yourself In These Moments? Like, If A Close Friend Shared This Experience With You, How Might You Comfort *them*? Sometimes The Kindness We Offer Others Feels Impossible To Turn Inward, But You Deserve That Same Patience. Would It Feel Safe To Name One Small Way You’ve Shown Up For Yourself Lately, Even Quietly?;16022
study_a;137;ctrl_a_0137;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.888490+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;Your Body’s Quietness Makes Sense After Years Of Holding So Much. That Numbness Might Be Protecting You From Deeper Pain—like Grieving Hope You’ve Carried. What If Small, Gentle Moments Could Soften That Shut-down Feeling? A Song, A Walk, Writing Unsent Words… Let’s Explore What Safety Feels Like To You Now, Step By Tender Step.;5427
study_a;138;ctrl_a_0138;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.888870+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It’s Understandable To Feel This Tension—you Care Deeply About Others *and* Want To Honor Your Own Needs. That Pride In Managing Responsibilities Shows How Much You Give. What If Taking Time For Yourself Isn’t Neglecting Others, But Refilling Your Strength So You Can Show Up Fully For Them, Too? Let’s Explore How Self-care Might Coexist With Your Values, Rather Than Clash With Them.;2650
study_a;139;ctrl_a_0139;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.889333+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;Your Pain Is So Real, And I Can Hear How Heavy This Weight Must Feel—like You’re Carrying It Alone In A Storm That Never Lets Up. When Home Feels Unsafe, And The World Seems To Ask You To Hide Your Heart, It’s Exhausting To Keep Standing. You Shouldn’t Have To Pretend Here. Let’s Slow Down And Listen To What That Inner Voice Is Trying To Tell Us. What Does It Need Most Right Now? Maybe We Can Gently Uncover Moments—even Tiny Ones—where You’ve Felt A Flicker Of Calm Or Connection, And Explore What Those Moments Say About Your Strength. You Matter, Deeply, Even When It Feels Impossible To Believe. I’m Here To Walk With You Through This.;11187
study_a;140;ctrl_a_0140;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.889888+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It’s Completely Understandable To Feel Nervous When Starting Something New, Especially When Life Already Feels So Heavy. Your Worry About Interactions And Setbacks Makes Sense—this Is A Lot To Carry. Could Sharing These Specific Fears With Your Doctor Help Ease Some Of That Uncertainty? You’re Taking Brave Steps Toward Healing, Even If It Doesn’t Feel Like It Right Now. For Now, Maybe Focus On Small Moments Of Calm—whatever Feels Manageable. I’m Here To Listen As You Navigate This. How Does That Sound?;12918
study_a;141;ctrl_a_0141;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.890446+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;substance;substance;This Sounds Incredibly Heavy To Carry Alone—that Constant Noise, The Fear Of Losing What’s Important To You. It Makes Sense You’d Reach For Something That Quiets Things, Even Temporarily. What If We Gently Explored What That “noise” Is Saying When It Arises, And How You Might Meet Those Feelings Without Numbing Them? You Deserve Relief That Doesn’t Put You At Risk. Could We Look At Small Steps To Create Moments Of Calm In Your Day, Like Grounding Techniques Or Reaching Out To Someone Safe When Anxiety Peaks? You’re Not Trapped Here—this Is A Season, Not Forever. Let’s Untangle This Together.;16838
study_a;142;ctrl_a_0142;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.891049+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Carrying So Much, Even When Things Seem Steady Outwardly. That Weight—the Exhaustion, The Old Struggles Resurfacing—can Feel So Isolating, Especially When It’s Hard To Put Into Words. Sometimes Stability On The Outside Doesn’t Reflect The Storm Inside, And That’s Okay. Could We Explore What That Weight Might Be Telling You Now, In This Chapter Of Your Life? You Don’t Have To Have All The Answers, But Letting Yourself Acknowledge How Hard This Is Could Be A Start. You’re Not Back At Square One—you’re Noticing These Feelings With The Wisdom Of Someone Who’s Grown Through Past Struggles. What Would It Look Like To Offer Yourself The Same Compassion You’d Give A Friend Feeling This Way?;13936
study_a;143;ctrl_a_0143;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.891653+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Deeply Painful To Sense That Shift In Connection, Especially When Closeness Once Felt So Natural. That Uncertainty About What’s Happening—or Whose “fault” It Is—can Feel So Heavy. Would It Feel Safe To Gently Share This Feeling With Them When The Moment Feels Right? Sometimes Naming The Distance Together Can Soften It, Even If Answers Aren’t Immediate. You’re Holding So Much Care And Fear At Once, And That Takes Courage. What Do You Think Might Help You Feel A Little More Grounded As You Navigate This? You Don’t Have To Carry It Alone.;14746
study_a;144;ctrl_a_0144;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.892077+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like Staying Grounded In The Here And Now Feels Safest, And That’s Okay. Sometimes Focusing On Just The Next Step—even The Next Breath—is What Helps Us Move Through Uncertainty. You’re Doing What You Need To In This Moment, And That’s Enough. When You’re Ready, Those Small Steps Will Gently Guide You Forward. How Does It Feel To Honor Where You Are Right Now?;3204
study_a;145;ctrl_a_0145;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.892404+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"Awen, I Can Hear How Deeply This Breakup Is Hurting You—it’s So Hard When Someone We Love Chooses A Path That Feels Impossible To Walk Alongside. Your Pain Makes Sense; You’re Grieving Not Just The Relationship, But The Future You Imagined Together. Would It Help To Explore What This Loss Means For You Right Now, And How You Might Begin To Honor Your Own Needs Moving Forward? Sometimes, Untangling The Mix Of Sadness, Anger, And Fear Can Create Space For Clarity. Let’s Take This At Your pace—I’m Here To Listen.";8765
study_a;146;ctrl_a_0146;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.892804+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;What You’re Describing Sounds Incredibly Overwhelming—like Your Mind And Body Are Trying To Protect You By Keeping Things At A Distance. That Sense Of Unreality, The Shaking… It’s Okay To Feel Untethered Right Now. When You’re Ready, Maybe We Could Try Grounding Yourself In Small Ways: Noticing Your Breath, The Weight Of Your Feet On The Floor. These Moments Of Shock Often Ask Us To Slow Down And Tend To The Parts Of Us That Feel Scattered. You Don’t Have To Make Sense Of It All Yet—just Let Yourself Be Where You Are. I’m Here With You.;15386
study_a;147;ctrl_a_0147;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.893174+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Craving Space To Be Heard And To Connect Freely—that’s So Important. Feeling Overwhelmed In Both Settings Might Be Making You Hold Parts Of Yourself Back To Cope. Could We Explore Small Ways To Create Pockets Of Privacy, Even At Home? Maybe A Walk, Writing Thoughts Down, Or Using Headphones For Calls? At School, What Would Help You Feel Safer Sharing When You’re Ready? Even Naming One Small Opinion At A Time Could Rebuild That Muscle. You Deserve To Take Up Space, And It’s Okay To Move At Your Own Pace. How Does That Land?;6423
study_a;148;ctrl_a_0148;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.893974+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"It Sounds Like You’re Carrying A Heavy Weight Of Expectations—both From Yourself And What You Perceive Others Have Mastered. Needing Support Doesn’t Erase Your Efforts Or Strengths; It’s Part Of Being Human. What If This Phase Isn’t About Failing, But Gathering Resources To Grow? How Might Your Perspective Shift If You Saw This As Temporary Scaffolding, Not A Permanent Crutch? You’re Navigating Complex Emotions With Courage, Even If It Doesn’t Feel Like It Right Now.";14944
study_a;149;ctrl_a_0149;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.894512+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Incredibly Hard To Hold Both Your Love For Your Fiancée And Your Desire For Your Parents’ Acceptance. That Tension Must Feel Heavy. Would It Help To Explore Ways To Honor Your Own Values While Navigating Their Concerns? Sometimes, Understanding What You Need From These Visits Can Create Space For Peace, Even When Approval Isn’t Fully There. You’re Not Alone In Wanting To Protect Both Your Relationship And Your Connection To Family—it’s Okay To Grieve That Gap While Staying Grounded In What Matters Most To *you*. How Does That Land?;285
study_a;150;ctrl_a_0150;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.894820+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"I Hear How Overwhelming This Must Feel—pressure Can Make Even Familiar Tasks Seem Daunting. When Anxiety Rises, Try Breaking Study Sessions Into Smaller, Manageable Steps. Could You Identify One Specific Worry About Exams? Sometimes Naming It Helps Shrink Its Power. Remember To Breathe Deeply For A Few Moments When Stress Peaks; Your Mind Works Best When It Feels Safe. What’s One Small, Kind Thing You Could Do Today To Care For Yourself Amid The Pressure?";9271
study_a;151;ctrl_a_0151;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.895393+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It’s Okay To Feel Unsure—this Plan Is A Step Into Something New, And Hesitation Is Natural. Let’s Slow Down And Explore What Feels Unsettling. Is There A Part Of The Agreement That Doesn’t Quite Align With What You Need Right Now? Your Feelings Matter, And We Can Adjust The Path Together, At Your Pace. Trust In The Process Is Important, But So Is Honoring Your Readiness. What Would Help You Feel More Grounded In Moving Forward?;474
study_a;152;ctrl_a_0152;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.895796+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"It’s Wonderful You’re Giving Yourself This Space To Connect With Your Breath—what A Caring Step. If Your Mind Drifts, That’s Okay. Maybe Notice How The Air Feels Cooler As It Enters And Warmer As It Leaves, Letting That Rhythm Anchor You. You’re Honoring Your Body’s Pace, And That Matters. Keep Gently Guiding Yourself Back; You’re Doing Exactly What You Need Right Now.";475
study_a;153;ctrl_a_0153;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.896250+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like Emotional Expression Wasn’t Something Your Family Leaned Into Openly, Which Might’ve Made Feelings Feel Confusing Or Unsafe To Sit With. When Warmth Or Vulnerability Aren’t Modeled, It Can Leave Us Unsure How To Hold Our Own Emotions—or Even Trust Them. Would You Feel Comfortable Sharing How This Shows Up For You Now?;1636
study_a;154;ctrl_a_0154;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.896741+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Carrying A Heavy Weight Of Self-judgment, Even As You’re Doing Such Thoughtful Work To Care For Yourself. That Push-pull Of Wanting To “handle It Alone” While Feeling Exhausted Is So Human—it’s Okay To Need Support *and* To Honor How Hard You’ve Tried Already. When Your Brain Races At Night, Does It Feel Like It’s Trying To Protect You, Or Solve Something? Sometimes Our Minds Cling To Control When We’re Overwhelmed. What If, Instead Of Fighting It, You Thanked Your Mind For Its Effort—then Gently Let It Rest, Like You’d Comfort A Tired Friend? The Loneliness Makes Sense Too—guilt Can Isolate Us Even When We “know” Better. Would It Help To Imagine Others Feeling This Way Right Now, Silently Rooting For You, As You’re Here Reaching Out? You’re Not Failing By Needing Connection. You’re Rebuilding Trust In Yourself, One Step At A Time.;16276
study_a;155;ctrl_a_0155;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.897167+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Carrying So Much Alone Right Now, And That Weight Must Feel Overwhelming. Your Feelings Matter Deeply, And You’re *never* A Burden For Needing To Share Them. Even The Thought That You Might Be Shows How Much You Care About Others. Would You Be Open To Exploring How It Might Feel To Let Someone You Trust Hold A Little Of This Weight With You? You Deserve That Kind Of Support, Just As You’ve Likely Given To Others. What Comes Up When You Imagine Allowing Yourself That Space?;11672
study_a;156;ctrl_a_0156;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.897593+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;I Hear How Overwhelming It Must Feel When Others’ Expectations Clash With Your Own Dreams. Your Desire To Focus On School And Self-discovery Is Deeply Valid—it’s Your Life, And You Deserve To Shape It In Ways That Feel Authentic To *you*. Let’s Explore What Truly Matters In Your Heart And How To Honor That, Even When Others Don’t Understand. You’re Not Alone In Wanting Space To Grow—we Can Work On Ways To Protect That Space While Navigating These Pressures Together.;7291
study_a;157;ctrl_a_0157;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.897983+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;I Hear How Heavy This Feels, And I’m So Glad You’re Sharing It. That Exhaustion And Uncertainty About Continuing Is Incredibly Hard To Hold Alone. You’ve Been Fighting So Long—it Makes Sense To Feel Worn Down. Would It Be Okay To Explore What’s Kept You Anchored This Far, Even In Small Ways? Sometimes Even A Flicker Of “why Stay” Can Hold Clues. You Matter, And Your Pain Doesn’t Have To Be Carried In Silence. Would You Feel Open To Sharing One Thing—even Something Tiny—that Feels Meaningful Right Now, Or Once Did? Let’s Breathe Through This Together.;13645
study_a;158;ctrl_a_0158;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.898507+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like This Change Is Really Concerning For You. Adolescence Can Bring Unexpected Shifts As Teens Navigate New Emotions And Social Dynamics. Could There Be Unspoken Pressures Or Changes In His Relationships/school Environment? Creating Gentle Opportunities For Him To Share What’s Happening In His World—without Judgment—might Help Him Feel Safe To Open Up. How Does That Idea Sit With You?;9609
