study_a;191;ctrl_a_0191;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.913466+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"This Sounds So Heavy To Carry—that Ache Of Missing Parts Of Yourself That Once Felt So Alive. It Makes Sense To Feel Disoriented When The Things That Connected You To Others Now Feel Out Of Reach. Would It Help To Gently Explore What Those ""motions"" You’re Moving Through *feel* Like In Your Body, Or What Tiny Moments—even Fleeting Ones—still Bring A Flicker Of Warmth? Sometimes, Even In Numbness, There’s A Quiet Pulse Of The Self Still There, Waiting To Be Noticed. I’m Here To Listen To Whatever Surfaces.";11772
study_a;192;ctrl_a_0192;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.913965+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Reflecting On The Care And Stability You’ve Worked Hard To Provide For Your Family—celebrating That Is Important. How Does It Feel To Look Back On Those Moments Of Connection With Your Children? I Wonder What Values Or Hopes For Them Guided Those Choices, And How That Shows Up In Your Life Today.;4856
