study_a;254;ctrl_a_0254;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.940438+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;That Immediate Surge Of Fear Must Feel So Overwhelming, Even When Part Of You Knows It Doesn’t Align With What’s Real. It’s Like Your Mind Is Trying To Protect You, But The Alarm Bells Ring Too Loudly. Could We Gently Explore What Happens *before* That Reaction Takes Over? Sometimes, Slowing Down The Moment Between The Trigger And The Fear—even Just A Breath—can Create A Tiny Space To Remind Yourself Of The Deeper Truth You Carry. What Do You Think Might Help You Feel Grounded When That Wave Starts To Rise? You’re Not Alone In This.;487
