study_a;282;ctrl_a_0282;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.951846+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"What You’re Experiencing Sounds Incredibly Overwhelming—your Body Reacting So Intensely Must Feel Frightening And Disorienting. It’s Okay To Honor That Fear Instead Of Fighting It; It’s Trying To Protect You, Even If It’s Not Serving You Right Now. Let’s Explore What Happens In Those Moments. What Thoughts Or Memories Surface When You Think About Driving? Sometimes Slowing Down To Understand Those Patterns Can Soften Their Grip. And When Your Husband Encourages “pushing Through,” I Wonder How It Might Feel To Share With Him What You Truly Need In Those Vulnerable Moments—maybe Reassurance, Patience, Or Just Sitting Together In The Discomfort Without Pressure. You’re Not A Burden; You’re Navigating Something Deeply Challenging, And That Takes Courage, Even If It Doesn’t Feel Like It Yet. Small Steps, Like Sitting In The Car Without Starting It, Might Help Rebuild Trust In Yourself. How Does That Sound?";18035
