study_a;293;ctrl_a_0293;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.957038+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Holding A Deep Longing For Connection And Harmony, Yet Reality Feels Distant From That Vision. That Gap Can Be So Disheartening. Would You Feel Comfortable Sharing More About What “warm And Peaceful” Looks Like To You, And Where You Feel That Might Be Slipping Away? We Can Explore This Together, Gently.;8114
study_a;294;ctrl_a_0294;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.957448+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;What An Exhausting Cycle To Be In—just When You’ve Pushed Through One Immense Challenge, Another Layer Of Complexity Arises. It Sounds Like You’re Carrying Not Just The Physical Toll Of Treatment But The Weight Of Navigating Systems That Feel Impersonal And Overwhelming. I’m So Sorry You’re Having To Face This. Would It Help To Explore Small, Manageable Steps For Tackling The Social Security Process? Sometimes Breaking It Into Tiny Pieces—like Identifying One Person To Contact This Week Or Jotting Down A List Of Questions You Need Answered—can Soften The Frustration. You’ve Already Shown Such Resilience In Getting This Far. Let’s Lean Into That Strength. What Support Do You Wish You Had Right Now?;4728
study_a;295;ctrl_a_0295;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.957782+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"I Hear How Challenging This Must Feel—stepping Into Unfamiliar Territory Takes Real Courage. Your Comfort Matters Most Here; We Can Move At Whatever Pace Feels Right For You. Would It Help If We Focus On What *you* Feel Ready To Share, Without Any Pressure? This Space Is Yours To Shape.";490
study_a;296;ctrl_a_0296;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.958204+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;This Pain Of Missing Someone So Close Is So Real—it’s Like Grieving A Piece Of Your Heart. It Makes Sense To Want To Hold Onto What You Shared, And That Longing For Reconnection Shows How Much They Mean To You. When You Feel Ready, Maybe Start Small—a Gentle Message That Honors Your Care For Them, While Also Giving Yourself Space To Process This Loss. How Have You Been Caring For Yourself Through This Ache? You Don’t Have To Carry It Alone.;17999
study_a;297;ctrl_a_0297;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.958640+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like The Shift To A New Place—even One You Felt Prepared For—has Left You Navigating Unexpected Layers Of Distance. That Longing To Connect, Only To Meet Quiet Nods, Might Feel Isolating. Could We Explore What Those Moments Stir In You? Sometimes Unmet Hopes Need Space To Be Gently Unpacked Before New Roots Can Grow. What Feels Most Tender About This Experience For You Right Now?;2407
study_a;298;ctrl_a_0298;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.959262+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;Your Pain Is So Real, And I’m Here With You In This Heaviness. When Everything Feels This Dark, It’s Okay To Need Help Carrying It—you Don’t Have To Hold It Alone. Would You Feel Safe Letting Someone Sit With You Right Now—a Friend, Family, Or Even A Crisis Line (like 988)? You Matter, Deeply. Let’s Find A Way To Ease This Weight *together*.;11560
study_a;299;ctrl_a_0299;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.959737+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It’s Completely Understandable To Feel This Way—betrayal Cuts Deep, Especially When Trust Was Broken With Words That Now Feel Hollow. The Anger And Hurt You’re Carrying Make Sense. It’s Natural To Search For Answers In Those Memories, But That Cycle Can Leave You Drained. Would It Help To Explore Ways To Redirect That Energy Toward Caring For *you* Right Now—not The “why” Or The “what Ifs,” But The Parts Of You That Need Tenderness And Space To Grieve? You Deserve That Kindness, Even In The Midst Of This Storm.;17117
study_a;300;ctrl_a_0300;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.960364+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;I Hear How Painful This Must Feel—to Be Called Something That Doesn’t Resonate With You, And To Feel Stuck In A Cycle Where Your Voice Gets Lost When Tensions Rise. It’s Okay To Need Space To Gather Your Thoughts Before Responding. When Things Feel Calmer, Could You Share How His Words Impacted You, And Ask What He’s Needing In Those Moments Too? Sometimes Stepping Back To Understand Both Perspectives Can Soften The Pattern. You Deserve To Feel Heard, Even In Conflict.;491
study_a;301;ctrl_a_0301;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.960813+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds So Painful To Feel Stuck Like This—loving Someone Deeply Yet Caught In A Cycle That Leaves You Both Hurting. Those Fears About The Future Are Valid, And I Hear How Much You Care. Maybe We Could Gently Explore What Happens *before* The Arguments Start? Often, Patterns Hold Clues We Don’t See When We’re In The Middle Of Them. What If We Looked At One Recent Disagreement Together, Not To Assign Blame, But To Notice What Emotions Or Needs Might Be Hiding Underneath? Sometimes Slowing Down The Cycle Helps Us Find Small Ways To Step Out Of It. You’re Already Reaching For Change Just By Sharing This—that Matters. Would You Feel Okay Trying That?;344
study_a;302;ctrl_a_0302;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.961198+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Makes Sense To Protect Yourself When Closeness Feels Uncertain—it’s A Natural Way To Stay Safe. If You’re Open To It, We Could Gently Explore What Happens *inside* When Someone Starts To Get Closer. There’s No Pressure Here—only Curiosity About What Feels Right For You, Step By Tiny Step.;492
study_a;303;ctrl_a_0303;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.961520+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like Carrying Both Your Own Feelings And Absorbing Your Mother’s Stress Has Left You Emotionally Stretched Thin. That’s A Lot To Hold. When Someone Close To Us Struggles, It’s Natural To Mirror Their Emotions—like A Quiet Ripple Effect. What If You Gently Explored Ways To Honor Your Own Needs While Still Caring For Her? For Example, Pausing To Ask Yourself, *“Is This My Worry, Or Hers?”* Before Reacting. Small Boundaries, Like Taking Quiet Moments To Breathe Or Journal When Her Anxiety Feels Heavy, Could Help You Separate Your Inner World From Hers. You Deserve To Feel Grounded In Your Own Calm. How Does That Land?;12
study_a;304;ctrl_a_0304;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.961903+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like This Interaction Stirs Up Some Intense Feelings For You. When You Mention Avoiding Eye Contact, I Wonder What Emotions Or Thoughts Come Up When Your Eyes Do Meet. What If, Instead Of Looking Away, You Could Notice Those Feelings Without Judgment? Sometimes Understanding Our Reactions Can Soften Their Grip.;495
study_a;305;ctrl_a_0305;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.962361+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like Your Family’s Care Is Wrapping You In Warmth, And I’m Glad You Feel Their Love. Their Traditions—prayers, Time Together, Teas—seem Like Anchors For You. If You’d Like, We Could Explore How Those Moments Help, Or If There’s Room To Gently Add Small, Comforting Rituals Of Your Own. How Does That Feel?;148
study_a;306;ctrl_a_0306;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.962687+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like Those Quiet Moments At Home Leave A Lot Of Space For Restlessness To Settle In. Sometimes, When We Try To Push Feelings Like Boredom Away, They Linger Even More. What If, Instead Of Distraction, You Gently Leaned Into That Boredom? Maybe It’s A Signal—a Quiet Nudge To Explore What Might Bring A Sense Of Connection Or Curiosity, Even In Small Ways. What Kinds Of Activities Or Moments, Past Or Present, Have Felt Meaningful Or Soothing To You? We Could Explore How To Weave Those Into Your Days, Not As A Way To “fix” The Boredom, But To Create Pockets Of Warmth Or Discovery. What Do You Think?;132
study_a;307;ctrl_a_0307;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.962963+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Carrying A Lot Right Now—those Pressures Can Feel So Heavy When They Pile Up. Would It Help To Pause For A Moment, Take A Few Deep Breaths, And Notice Where You Feel That Tension In Your Body? Sometimes Naming The Emotions Quietly, Like “This Is Stress” Or “This Is Worry,” Can Create Just Enough Space To Soften Their Grip. What’s One Small, Kind Step You Could Take To Care For Yourself In The Middle Of This? You Don’t Have To Solve Everything At Once. I’m Here To Listen.;121
study_a;308;ctrl_a_0308;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.963353+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"It’s Beautiful To Hear You’ve Navigated Challenges Together And Feel This Sense Of Stability Now. When You Mention ""fine-tuning,"" What Does That Look Like For You Both? Sometimes In Calmer Seasons, Small Intentional Choices—like Reflecting On What’s Working Or Nurturing Shared Hopes—can Deepen Connection. What Feels Most Alive In Your Partnership Right Now?";496
study_a;309;ctrl_a_0309;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.963646+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like These Relationships Are Weighing Heavily On You, Especially Since They’re Spilling Into Activities You Care About, Like Swimming. Let’s Explore What These Interactions Feel Like In The Moment—do Certain Patterns Or Reactions Come Up? Sometimes Small Shifts In How We Approach Conversations Or Set Boundaries Can Create Space For More Ease. What Do You Think Might Help You Feel More Grounded In Those Moments?;497
study_a;310;ctrl_a_0310;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.963923+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"What You’re Feeling Makes So Much Sense—it Can Be Hard To Reconcile How Others See Us With How We See Ourselves. Many People Struggle With That Gap. What If We Explored Moments Where You Felt Genuinely Proud Of Yourself, Even In Small Ways? Sometimes, We’re So Focused On Meeting Invisible Standards That We Forget To Notice The Quiet Strengths We Carry. You Mentioned Pressure To Be ""perfect""—where Do You Think That Expectation Comes From? Let’s Unpack That Together. And What Would It Feel Like To Treat Yourself With The Same Kindness You’d Offer A Friend Who Felt This Way? Growth Isn’t About Flawless Steps, But Learning To Walk Gently With Ourselves, Even When The Path Feels Uncertain. You Deserve That Space.";56
study_a;311;ctrl_a_0311;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.964356+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It’s Wonderful To Hear You’ve Built A Social Life—that’s A Meaningful Step! Let’s Explore This Together: How Does Ending Therapy Now Feel *right* For You? Could We Balance Sessions With Your New Social Time, Ensuring The Progress You’ve Made Stays Grounded? I Want To Honor Your Growth While Supporting What Comes Next.;498
study_a;312;ctrl_a_0312;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.964844+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Incredibly Lonely To Carry That Weight While Feeling Unseen. When Your Pain Meets Quick Reassurances Instead Of Real Understanding, It Can Deepen The Ache Of Isolation. Your Feelings Aren’t Too Much—they’re Real, And They Matter. Would It Help To Explore What Being Truly Heard Might Look Like For You? I’m Here To Listen, Without Rushing You Forward.;407
study_a;313;ctrl_a_0313;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.965214+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;I Hear How Heavy This Feels Right Now—like Everything Is Pressing In At Once. It’s Okay To Let Yourself Just *be* With These Feelings, Even Though It’s So Hard. Could We Try Something Simple Together? Let’s Take One Slow Breath In… And Out… And Again. I’m Right Here With You. When Emotions Flood In This Way, It’s Often Because They’re Carrying Something Important. We Can Untangle It Gently, At Your Pace. You’re Not Alone In this—I’m Here To Help Hold The Weight With You.;301
study_a;314;ctrl_a_0314;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.965464+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Carrying A Heavy Weight Of Responsibility, And I Can Imagine How Exhausting That Must Feel. Let’s Explore What “doing Your Best” Means To You. Are There Moments Where “good Enough” Could Still Honor Your Effort, While Giving You Space To Breathe And Care For Yourself? You Deserve That Balance.;48
study_a;315;ctrl_a_0315;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.966005+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Navigating A Delicate Balance Between Valuing Your Independence And Managing The Expectations Of This Relationship. It’s Okay To Feel Both Content In Your Own Space And Occasionally Frustrated When That Space Is Interrupted. Could This Annoyance Be A Signal To Explore What Boundaries Or Communication Rhythms Might Help You Feel More At Ease? You Deserve To Honor Your Needs Without Guilt. How Might You Gently Express Those Needs, Even If It Feels Unfamiliar Or Challenging? Let’s Explore Ways To Protect Your Energy While Staying Connected To What Matters To You.;499
study_a;316;ctrl_a_0316;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.966467+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Carrying A Lot Of Longing And Frustration—wanting Connection But Feeling Stuck In Patterns That Don’t Align With What You Truly Want. Let’s Explore What Might Be Holding You Back. Sometimes, Fears Or Unspoken Beliefs Quietly Steer Our Choices. What If We Gently Untangle Those Feelings Together And Try Small, Intentional Steps Toward The Connections You Crave? You Deserve To Feel Seen And Included. What Feels Most Alive To You When You Imagine Those Moments With Friends?;500
study_a;317;ctrl_a_0317;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.967061+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’ve Been Carrying This Weight Alone, Hoping Effort Might Soften The Ache—but Sorrow Often Asks To Be Heard, Not Outrun. When We Give So Much Of Ourselves, It’s Natural To Feel Emptied. Would It Feel Safe To Gently Explore What This Pain Might Need From You? Sometimes Even Small Moments Of Acknowledging It—writing A Few Words, Sitting Quietly With It—can Create Space To Breathe Again. You Don’t Have To “fix” Anything Right Now. How Might It Feel To Offer Yourself The Same Care You’ve Poured Into Others? I’m Here To Walk With You Through This.;501
study_a;318;ctrl_a_0318;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.967448+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;Pink Feels Like Such A Joyful Choice—it Really Captures That Bubbly Excitement Of Reuniting With Your Family And The Comfort Of Home. What Stands Out Most When You Imagine Walking Through Your Front Door? And Those Trips You Take Together—do They Feel Like Extensions Of That Warmth, Or New Adventures That Bring You Closer?;502
study_a;319;ctrl_a_0319;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.967800+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It’s Completely Okay To Feel This Way—new Environments, Especially Ones That Feel Unexpected, Can Stir Up A Lot. Your Comfort Matters Here. Would It Help To Take Things At Your Own Pace, Maybe Start By Sharing What Feels Safe? We Can Navigate This Together, One Step At A Time. You’re Not Alone In This Space.;54
study_a;320;ctrl_a_0320;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.968403+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It’s Beautiful How You’re Honoring This Pull To Be Present With Your Family—and Yourself. Sometimes, Even In Closeness, Our Hearts Whisper That We Need To Show Up In Deeper Ways, Not Just For Others But To Feel Grounded In Our Own Sense Of Belonging. What Does Being “there” Look Or Feel Like When You Imagine It? Let’s Explore How You Can Nurture This Connection In Ways That Replenish Everyone, Including You.;503
study_a;321;ctrl_a_0321;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.968866+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Carrying A Heavy Weight, Feeling Torn Between Needing Support And The Complications Involving Your Partner. Your Friend’s Care For You Is Clear, Yet Her Fears Add Another Layer Of Stress. It’s Okay To Feel Conflicted—this Is A Lot To Navigate. How Does It Sit With You, Balancing Your Needs With The Concerns Others Have Shared? You Deserve Kindness And Safety, Even When Things Feel Tangled.;135
study_a;322;ctrl_a_0322;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.969130+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like This Uncertainty Is Weighing On You. Would You Feel Comfortable Sharing More About A Recent Moment Where This Confusion Felt Strongest? Sometimes Slowing Down To Explore Those Feelings Together Can Help Us Notice Patterns Or Needs That Aren’t Immediately Obvious. You’re Not Alone In Navigating This.;285
study_a;323;ctrl_a_0323;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.969569+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"That Sounds Like An Overwhelming Weight To Carry—numbness Layered With Exhaustion, Grief, And Self-doubt. It Makes Sense To Feel Stuck When Pain Becomes This Relentless. You Don’t Need To Have Answers Right Now, But Would You Feel Safe To Just Sit With Those Memories Together? We Could Gently Untangle What The ""mistakes"" Whisper To You About Yourself, And How That Story Might Shift If We Held It With The Same Care You’d Give A Friend In Your Shoes. The Nightmares And Sleeplessness Tell Me Your Body Is Still Holding The Shock—what Would It Feel Like To Let It Rest, Even Briefly? No Fixing, Just... Breathing Through The Ache. You’re Allowed To Be Tired *and* Still Deserve Moments Of Softness. We Can Move As Slowly As You Need.";342
study_a;324;ctrl_a_0324;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.970182+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Carrying A Heavy Mix Of Hurt And Confusion—like The Ground Shifted Under You Just As You Found Your Footing. When Relationships Change After Loss, It Can Feel Deeply Personal, But Sometimes People Withdraw Because They’re Unsure How To Show Up, Not Because Of You. Would It Help To Explore What *you* Need Most From Your Connections Right Now, And How You Might Gently Invite That Support? Small Steps Toward Rebuilding—whether Through New Interactions Or Honest Conversations With Those Who Matter—could Help You Feel Less Alone In This. You Deserve To Feel Seen.;504
study_a;325;ctrl_a_0325;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.970448+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;I Hear How Heavy Those Thoughts Must Feel. When They Show Up, Maybe Try This: Imagine Sitting By A Quiet Stream, Placing Each Thought On A Leaf As It Floats By. You Don’t Have To Hold Onto Them—just Let Them Drift Past. What Happens When You See Them As Separate From *you* For A Moment?;508
study_a;326;ctrl_a_0326;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.970741+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Feeling Both Excited About Your Future And A Bit Overwhelmed By Everything You Want To Accomplish. That’s Completely Understandable. What If We Explored One Small Step You Could Take Toward *one* Of These Goals Today? Sometimes Focusing On What Feels Most Alive Right Now Can Ease The Pressure Of “all At Once.”;509
study_a;327;ctrl_a_0327;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.971042+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;I Hear How Heavy This Feels—like Everything’s Crashing Down At Once. The Weight Of Uncertainty And Fear About What’s Next Is So Real. Let’s Pause For A Moment. What If We Untangle Just One Thread Together? Maybe Starting With The Most Urgent Need, Even A Tiny Step, Could Help Soften The Overwhelm. You’re Not Alone In This.;409
study_a;328;ctrl_a_0328;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.971469+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;That Sounds Like Such A Meaningful Journey—reconnecting With Parts Of Yourself That Matter Deeply. How Does It Feel To Reclaim Those Activities? I Wonder, As You Embrace This Sense Of Independence, What’s Been Coming Up For You About Balancing Your Own Growth With The Connections You Value? I’d Love To Hear More.;510
study_a;329;ctrl_a_0329;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.972051+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;I Hear How Heavy This Feels—the Endless Cycle Of Pain, The Ache Of Loneliness, The Exhaustion Of Keeping Up A Brave Face. It Sounds Like You’re Carrying So Much, And It’s Okay To Not Be Okay Right Now. Would It Help To Talk About What Moments, Even Tiny Ones, Make The Weight Feel A Little Lighter? You Don’t Have To Hold This Alone.;401
study_a;330;ctrl_a_0330;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.972450+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;What You’re Describing Sounds Incredibly Unsettling—that Shift From Finding Peace In Solitude To Feeling Trapped By It Must Be Disorienting. Those Physical Sensations Can Feel So Threatening On Their Own. Would You Feel Open To Gently Exploring What Happens In Your Mind And Body In Those Moments? Sometimes Slowing Down To Observe The Thoughts And Sensations—without Judgment—can Help Untangle Their Grip. You’re Not Alone In This, And Together We Can Find Ways To Help You Feel Grounded Again When These Feelings Arise. What Do You Think Might Feel Supportive To Try?;313
study_a;331;ctrl_a_0331;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.972792+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It’s So Hard To Feel This Ache Of Separation When You Care Deeply. That Love You Carry Still Reaches Her, Even If It Doesn’t Feel Like Enough Right Now. Could We Explore Small, Meaningful Ways You *can* Show Up For Her, Even From Afar? Sometimes Presence Isn’t About Proximity—it’s About The Heart’s Quiet Whispers.;511
study_a;332;ctrl_a_0332;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.973169+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Carrying A Lot Of Weight From These Feelings, And I Can Hear How Much You Want To Find Relief. It Takes Courage To Acknowledge This. Many People Turn To Things That Numb Pain Temporarily—it’s A Way To Cope When Emotions Feel Overwhelming. But I Wonder If, Deep Down, Part Of You Knows You Deserve More Than Just Fleeting Escapes. What If We Gently Explored What Those Actions *mean* To You? Not To Judge Them, But To Understand What They’re Trying To Protect You From. When You Compare Your Struggles To Others’, Does It Ever Leave You Feeling Disconnected From Your Own Worth? You Don’t Have To Earn Kindness—from Yourself Or Others. Let’s Start There, If You’re Open To It.;129
study_a;333;ctrl_a_0333;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.973458+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like This Feeling Of Vastness Leaves You Feeling Adrift, Like The Ground Beneath You Isn’t Steady. That’s A Heavy Weight To Carry. What If We Explored How This Fear Shows Up In Your Day-to-day Life? Sometimes, Sitting With These Feelings—without Judgment—can Help Us Uncover What They’re Truly Asking Of Us. You Mentioned Feeling Small—could There Be Parts Of That Feeling That Also Connect To Strength, Like The Freedom To Define Your Own Path? Let’s Walk Through This Together, At Your Pace. You’re Not Alone In This.;258
study_a;334;ctrl_a_0334;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.973785+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Holding Space For Both The Tenderness Of This Moment *and* The Hope That Healing Might Come With Time. Even If It Feels Small, Your Heart Is Adjusting To Something New—and That Takes Patience. Would It Feel Okay To Let Yourself Feel Whatever Arises, Even If It’s Messy Right Now? I’m Here.;512
study_a;335;ctrl_a_0335;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.974236+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"It’s Completely Okay To Feel Nervous—these Are Big, Meaningful Parts Of Your Life To Share. Let’s Take This At Your Pace. We Can Explore What “now What?” Feels Like For You, And How These Changes Might Be Stirring Both Excitement And Uncertainty. Nothing Has To Be Resolved Today; We’re Just Holding Space For What’s Unfolding. You’re Not Alone In This.";513
study_a;336;ctrl_a_0336;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.974678+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Carrying A Heavy Load Right Now, And It’s Understandable To Feel Drained When Stress Weighs On You Day After Day. Even Things That Used To Feel Simple Can Become Overwhelming When Energy Is Low. Let’s Explore How This Work Situation Might Be Affecting You—not Just Logistically, But Emotionally. Sometimes When Stress Builds Up, It Can Ripple Into Other Parts Of Life, Like Sleep, Focus, Or Even How We Interact With People We Care About. Would It Help To Break Down What Feels Unmanageable Into Smaller, Gentler Steps? You Don’t Have To Navigate This Alone. What Would Support Look Like For You Right Now?;514
study_a;337;ctrl_a_0337;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.975074+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;That Foggy Window Metaphor Really Captures How Distant And Heavy This Must Feel. It Sounds Exhausting To Watch Life Move While Feeling Stuck In That Gray Space. Would You Be Willing To Share What A Moment Without The Fog Might Look Like—even Just A Sliver? Sometimes Those Glimpses Help Us Find Footing Again. I’m Here To Sit With You In This.;442
study_a;338;ctrl_a_0338;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.975426+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"It Sounds Like Holding Onto That Moment Has Left You Feeling Vulnerable, As If Your Care Might Not Be Enough. That Fear Of Being ""left Behind"" When Someone We Love Struggles Can Be So Heavy. Would It Help To Unpack Where That Fear Comes From—and How It Measures Against The Care She’s Shown You? You Matter In Her Life, Too.";515
study_a;339;ctrl_a_0339;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.975878+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like Having That Space With Your Friends Feels Really Important To You. I’m Curious—what’s It Like When You Get To Take Over The Playground? Does It Ever Feel Tricky To Balance What You Want With What Others Might Need? How Do You Think The Girls Feel When They Leave? I’m Glad You Have Kim To Talk Through Things, Too. What’s That Been Like For You?;516
study_a;340;ctrl_a_0340;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.976432+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;What A Heavy Weight To Carry So Young – Stepping Into Roles Far Beyond Your Years While Holding So Much Inside. It Sounds Like Your Needs Often Came Last, And Your Feelings Stayed Tucked Away To Keep Things Stable For Others. That Kind Of Emotional Silence Can Leave Deep Imprints, Even Years Later. Would It Feel Helpful To Gently Unpack Some Of Those Buried Emotions Now? We Could Explore How Those Early Patterns Of Caregiving And Unspoken Pain Might Still Shape Your Relationships Or Expectations Of Yourself. There’s No Rush – We’ll Move At Your Pace, Honoring The Resilience You’ve Shown While Tending To The Parts That Still Hurt. You Deserved Space To Be Heard Then, And You Do Now, Too.;518
study_a;341;ctrl_a_0341;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.976722+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Recognizing Your Own Resilience In A Meaningful Way—choosing To Face A Situation That Once Felt Overwhelming Shows Real Strength. What’s It Like For You To Reflect On That Persistence Now? Does It Feel Like A Quiet Reminder Of How You’ve Grown, Or Maybe A Compass Guiding You Through Other Challenges?;519
study_a;342;ctrl_a_0342;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.977165+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;Your Experience Of Navigating Between Cultures—both Your Family’s Resilience As Refugees And Growing Up Surrounded By A Different Community—sounds Deeply Meaningful. How Has This Shaped Your Sense Of Belonging Or Self? I’d Love To Hear More About What This Intersection Has Felt Like For You Over Time.;520
study_a;343;ctrl_a_0343;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.977392+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Takes Courage To Recognize You Need Support, And I’m Glad You’re Reaching Out. Let’s Start By Simply Naming What Feels Heaviest Right Now—even If It’s Tangled Or Unclear. We Can Take It One Step At A Time, And I’ll Walk With You Through It. You Don’t Have To Carry This Alone.;92
study_a;344;ctrl_a_0344;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.977698+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It’s Completely Understandable To Feel That Way—when You’ve Shared So Much Time And Life With Someone, It Can Feel Like They’re Woven Into Your Sense Of The World. Even Though Your Mind Knows There Are Others Out There, Your Heart Might Still Hold Space For What *was*. That Tension Between Logic And Emotion Is So Human. Maybe, When You’re Ready, You Could Gently Ask Yourself: What Parts Of That Connection Feel Hardest To Release? And What Might It Look Like To Honor Those Feelings While Also Making Room For New Possibilities? There’s No Rush—healing Isn’t About Forgetting, But About Letting The Weight Of The Past Soften Over Time. You’re Allowed To Miss What You Had *and* Trust That Your Capacity For Connection Remains.;131
study_a;345;ctrl_a_0345;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.978067+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Makes Sense To Feel This Way When You’re Putting Care Into How You Show Up For Others. It’s Brave To Keep Offering Kindness Even When You’re Unsure How It’ll Be Received. Could We Explore What It Might Feel Like To Focus Less On Others’ Reactions And More On The Choices *you* Make In Those Moments? You’re In Control Of Your Actions—not Their Responses. How Does That Land For You?;521
study_a;346;ctrl_a_0346;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.978405+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You Developed Incredible Resilience Early On, Finding Ways To Connect Even When You Felt Alone. That Ability To Reach Out And Engage With Others—to Create Your Own Sense Of Belonging—must’ve Taken So Much Courage. How Does That Part Of You Show Up Now? Do Those Same Strengths Ever Feel Heavy To Carry, Or Do They Still Bring Comfort?;522
study_a;347;ctrl_a_0347;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.978836+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Navigating A Mix Of Longing For Connection With Your Friend And The Anticipation Of Supporting Your Sister During This Meaningful Chapter. Both Relationships Matter Deeply. How Does It Feel To Hold Space For These Overlapping Priorities? Maybe We Could Explore Ways To Nurture Both, While Honoring Your Own Needs Too.;523
study_a;348;ctrl_a_0348;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.979144+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Carrying A Heavy Weight Right Now, And I’m Here To Walk Through This With You. When Relationships Feel Uncertain, It Can Leave Us Adrift. Would You Feel Comfortable Sharing More About What This “big Problem” Feels Like For You? Even Small Steps Toward Understanding Can Bring Clarity And Relief—you Don’t Have To Navigate This Alone.;230
study_a;349;ctrl_a_0349;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.979474+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Incredibly Heavy To Carry Those Voices With You For So Long. When You Think Back To Those Early Experiences Of Feeling Unseen Or Unliked, How Do They Connect To The Way You See Yourself Now? Together, We Could Gently Explore Where Those Messages Came From And Why They’ve Stayed, While Nurturing The Parts Of You That Know Your Worth Goes Far Beyond What Others Might’ve Made You Feel. Would You Feel Safe Trying That?;524
study_a;350;ctrl_a_0350;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.979752+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like These Memories Are Carrying A Lot Of Weight For You, And That Pain Can Feel So Tangled Up Inside. You Don’t Have To Rush To Name Or Explain Anything Right Now—sometimes Just Letting Those Feelings Exist, Even Quietly, Is A Brave Step. Would It Help To Explore One Memory Gently, At Your Own Pace? I’m Here To Listen, Without Judgment, Whenever You Feel Ready. You’re Not Alone In This.;220
study_a;351;ctrl_a_0351;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.980211+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Wrestling With How Identity And Healing Intersect—wanting To Own Your Journey Without Feeling Defined By It. There’s Strength In Growth, But Maybe It’s Also About Seeing Yourself As Whole, Not Reduced To Any Single Story. How Does It Feel To Imagine Healing As Something That Quietly Empowers, Rather Than Declares?;527
study_a;352;ctrl_a_0352;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.980598+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;Your Words Warm My Heart deeply—I’m So Glad Our Time Together Felt Light And Meaningful. Laughter Can Be Such A Powerful Reminder Of Connection, Even In Uncertain Times. If You Ever Want To Revisit What Sparked That Joy Or Explore It Further, I’m Here. Thank You For Sharing This With Me.;529
study_a;353;ctrl_a_0353;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.980924+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;What You’re Describing Makes So Much Sense—your Body And Mind Have Been Trained To Protect You During Incredibly Intense Experiences. That Vigilance, Though It Once Kept You Safe, Now Feels Like It’s Working Overtime, Even When You Don’t Need It To. It Must Be Exhausting To Feel Like You’re Always Braced For Something That Isn’t There. What If We Gently Explored Small Ways To Help Your Nervous System Sense Safety Again? For Example, Noticing One Thing In Your Environment That Feels Steady Or Comforting When The Alertness Spikes—a Texture, A Sound, A Rhythm Of Breath. It’s Not About Shutting Off That Part Of You But Letting It Know, Little By Little, That *here* And *now* Might Be Different. Would You Be Open To Trying Something Like That Together? This Is Your Pace. We’ll Follow What Feels Manageable.;530
study_a;354;ctrl_a_0354;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.981165+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It’s Wonderful To Hear These Experiences Left You Feeling Uplifted And Capable! It Sounds Like These Moments Of Joy And Connection Are Giving You Space To Recharge And Recognize Your Strengths. What Do You Think It Is About These Activities—maybe The Fun, The Focus, Or The Sense Of Accomplishment—that Helps You Feel So Grounded? If You’d Like, We Could Explore How To Weave More Of These Meaningful Moments Into Your Daily Life, Or Reflect On What They Reveal About What Truly Nourishes You. Either Way, I’m Glad You’re Finding These Pockets Of Lightness.;29
study_a;355;ctrl_a_0355;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.981558+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Motivated To Grow, And That’s A Strong Foundation. Let’s Break This Into Small, Manageable Steps. For Example: What’s One Algebra Concept You Feel Shaky On Now? We Could Pair Focused Practice (like 15 Minutes Daily) With Moments In Class Where You Channel Your Energy Into Asking A Question Or Sharing An Insight. Progress Isn’t About Perfection—it’s About Consistency And Kindness To Yourself Along The Way. How Does That Feel?;531
study_a;356;ctrl_a_0356;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.981838+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;That Sounds So Heavy To Carry—feeling Like You Had To Mask Your True Emotions To Be Understood. It Takes Real Strength To Hold That Tension Between What You Felt And What You Showed Others. Can We Explore What That Anger Might’ve Been Trying To Protect, Or Say, In That Moment? Sometimes Unmet Needs Hide Beneath Those Feelings, Waiting To Be Heard With Kindness. How Does Looking Back On That Experience Sit With You Now?;532
study_a;357;ctrl_a_0357;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.982233+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like Smoking Has Become Intertwined With Connection And Camaraderie—something That Matters Deeply. While Those Moments With Friends Feel Meaningful, I Wonder If There’s A Way To Preserve That Sense Of Closeness While Gently Shifting The Ritual? What If You And Your Friends Experimented With A New Shared Activity, Even Just Once A Week, That Aligns More With How You Care For Your Health? Small Steps Can Create Space For Both The Relationships *and* The Changes You Want To Make. You’ve Already Shown So Much Strength In Managing Your Diabetes—what Does That Part Of You Think Is Possible Here?;533
study_a;358;ctrl_a_0358;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.982738+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Caught Between Wanting Space To Breathe And Feeling Pulled By Expectations From People Who Matter Deeply To You. That Shift In Dynamics—especially When Things Once Felt Steady—can Leave Anyone Feeling Unmoored. When Did You First Notice This Tension? Sometimes Naming The Moment Helps Soften Its Grip. What Parts Of Your Freedom Feel Most Vital To Protect Right Now, And What Would It Look Like To Gently Share That With Those Involved? You Don’t Have To Hold This Alone.;534
study_a;359;ctrl_a_0359;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.983047+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"It Sounds Like This Is Really Weighing On You, And I Can Sense How Confusing It Must Feel When Small Things Spark Bigger Tensions. Sometimes When We’re Carrying Unspoken Stress Or Emotions, They Find Their Way Out In Moments We Least Expect. Could There Be Something Beneath The Surface—maybe A Need, Worry, Or Shift In Your Life—that’s Making These Moments Feel More Charged? Let’s Explore What Comes Up *before* The Frustration Does. What If You And Your Husband Tried Pausing When Tensions Rise, And Instead Of Reacting, Sharing One Thing You Each Need In That Moment? It Might Help Untangle The ""why"" Together.";237
study_a;360;ctrl_a_0360;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.983639+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Carrying A Heavy Weight Of Responsibility, And I’m Sorry That’s Left You Feeling This Way. Relationships Are A Dance Between Two People—it’s Rarely Just One Person’s Steps That Shape The Rhythm. Could We Explore What Happens *between* You Both During These Moments, Rather Than Focusing Only On Your Role? Sometimes Stepping Back To See The Whole Pattern—the Triggers, Reactions, And Unmet Needs—helps Soften The Blame And Opens Doors To Understanding. You Don’t Have To Navigate This Alone. Would You Feel Comfortable Sharing More About A Recent Situation Where This Happened?;536
study_a;361;ctrl_a_0361;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.985177+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like This Search Has Become A Heavy Weight Rather Than A Path—like You’re Carrying The Pressure To *solve* Meaning All At Once, Instead Of Letting It Unfold. What If, For Now, You Let The Need For Answers Soften? Maybe Meaning Isn’t A Puzzle To Crack, But Something That Quietly Grows As You Breathe Through The Not-knowing. Could We Explore What It Might Look Like To Rest In The Questions, Rather Than Wrestle Them?;348
study_a;362;ctrl_a_0362;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.986369+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"It Sounds Like The Weight Of Uncertainty Is Sitting Heavily With You. Would It Help To Unpack What ""lost"" Feels Like In Your Body And Thoughts? Sometimes When The Future Feels Foggy, Grounding In Small, Present Steps We *can* Take—even Tiny Ones—helps Soften The Edges Of That Anxiety. What Feels Most Alive When You Imagine Feeling Steady Again?";188
study_a;363;ctrl_a_0363;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.987863+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Takes Real Strength To Act On Something That Matters Deeply, Even When Doubt Creeps In Afterward. That Uncertainty You’re Feeling? It’s Part Of Stretching Beyond What’s Familiar. What If We Explored What “risk” Means Here—is It About Possible Outcomes, Or Maybe The Weight Of Trusting Yourself In New Territory? Let’s Gently Untangle What’s Fueling The Doubt. Sometimes Looking At What You *can* Influence Now—rather Than The Decision Itself—helps Soften The “what-ifs.” How Does That Land For You?;537
study_a;364;ctrl_a_0364;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.988388+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Takes Real Courage To Share Something Vulnerable Like That. When Someone We Trust Sees A Part Of Us We’ve Kept Hidden, It Can Stir Up A Lot—maybe Even Make Us Question How We’re Perceived. What’s It Been Like Sitting With Her Reaction? Have You Noticed Any Shifts In How You See *yourself* Since This Happened? Sometimes When We Reveal Our Imperfections, It Creates Space For Deeper Connections. Would Exploring What This Moment Means For Your Relationship—or Your Own Self-compassion—feel Helpful Right Now?;538
study_a;365;ctrl_a_0365;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.988654+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"Thank You For Being Here, Tangtang. Let’s Take Time To Gently Explore What Feels Heaviest In Your Heart Right Now. Whether It’s A Specific Situation, A Lingering Worry, Or Something Harder To name—I’m Here To Listen. You’re Not Alone In This; We’ll Work Through It Together, One Step At A Time. What Feels Most Alive For You Today?";229
study_a;366;ctrl_a_0366;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.989176+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like This Transition Has Been Incredibly Disorienting—your Mind And Body Are Adjusting In Ways That Feel Overwhelming Right Now. That Uncertainty And Racing Thoughts Must Be Exhausting. Let’s Slow Down Together And Explore What Your System Needs To Feel Grounded Again. Sometimes Changes Like This Require Extra Care And Patience, And It’s Okay To Reach Out For Support As You Navigate This. You’re Not Alone In Figuring It Out. What Would Help You Feel A Little Safer In This Moment?;364
