study_a;368;ctrl_a_0368;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.989919+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like This Anger—both His And Yours—has Created A Heavy Weight Between You. When You Imagine Facing Him Without The Apology You Hope For, It’s Like Holding Onto A Storm That Keeps Circling Back. Maybe Part Of The Hurt Is Wondering Why Now, Why This Way… And What That Means About How Things Might Change, Or Not. If We Gently Untangle What’s Beneath The Anger—the Unmet Needs, The Old Patterns—could That Soften The Grip It Has On You? You Deserve Space To Breathe, Not Just React. How Does That Land?;542
study_a;369;ctrl_a_0369;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.990234+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You Value Connecting With Others But Need It To Feel Authentic To Your Comfort Level. It’s Okay To Honor Your Preference For Less Physical Closeness While Still Enjoying The Parts Of Socializing That Energize You. Maybe Exploring Ways To Communicate Your Boundaries Gently Could Help You Feel More At Ease? You Deserve To Engage In Ways That Feel Right For *you*.;543
study_a;370;ctrl_a_0370;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.990551+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;That’s Such A Meaningful Step—reclaiming Your Inner Voice And Reshaping It Into Something Kinder Or More Supportive. How Does It Feel When You’re Able To Guide That Voice Toward Something Different? Does It Bring A Sense Of Calm, Or Does It Stir Other Emotions? I’d Love To Hear More About How This Shift Impacts Your Day-to-day Moments. You’re Exploring A Powerful Tool Here, And I’m Curious How We Can Nurture This Skill Together.;544
study_a;371;ctrl_a_0371;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.990927+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"What You’re Describing Sounds Incredibly Heavy—like Your Mind Is Trying To Protect You By Putting Up Walls When Everything Becomes Too Much. That Distance You Feel From Yourself? It Might Be A Way Of Coping When Emotions Feel Overwhelming Or Unsafe. Could We Explore What Happens In Those Moments When You Sense You ""should"" Feel Something But Can’t? Maybe, Gently, We Can Find Small Ways To Reconnect With Yourself—like Noticing One Thing Around You *right Now* (a Sound, A Texture) To Ground Back Into Your Body. You Don’t Have To Push Through This Alone. We’ll Move At Your Pace.";423
study_a;372;ctrl_a_0372;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.991174+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It’s Okay To Feel Uncertain—marriage Can Bring Complex Emotions To The Surface. Let’s Slow Down And Explore What’s Weighing On Your Heart. What Does *connection* Feel Like To You Now? Are There Moments Where You Feel Seen Or Distant? Sometimes Untangling These Threads Together Can Reveal A Clearer Path Forward. You’re Not Alone In This.;151
study_a;373;ctrl_a_0373;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.991568+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Discovering What Truly Resonates With You—acting From Your Own Understanding Rather Than External Pressure. When We Connect Our Actions To Our Personal Values Or Reasons, It Often Feels More Authentic And Less Draining. Could Exploring *why* This New Approach Worked Help You Reclaim More Agency In Similar Situations?;547
study_a;374;ctrl_a_0374;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.991983+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;This Sounds Like A Meaningful Way To Build Connection And Purpose Together. Involving Your Nephews Could Create Shared Pride In Creating Something Tangible While Strengthening Trust. How Does It Feel To Imagine Offering Them Both Practical Skills And A Living Example Of Your Growth? What Values Do You Hope This Collaboration Might Nurture In All Of You?;548
study_a;375;ctrl_a_0375;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.992240+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It’s Completely Understandable To Feel This Way With Such An Important Exam Approaching. Many Students Experience This Kind Of Pressure. Let’s Try Breaking Your Study Time Into Smaller, Focused Chunks With Short Breaks In Between—this Can Help Your Mind Feel Less Overwhelmed. What Do You Think About Experimenting With That This Week? You’re Not Alone In This.;156
study_a;376;ctrl_a_0376;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.992604+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like Connecting In Close Relationships Can Feel More Vulnerable Than With Strangers, Where The Expectations Are Clear And Brief. Maybe Those Transactional Interactions Feel Safer Because There’s Less At Stake Emotionally? When You’re With Your Spouse, Do You Ever Notice Worries About “getting It Right” Or Pressure To Be A Certain Way? What If You Tried Small, Low-pressure Moments Of Sharing During Times Like Picnics—maybe Commenting On Something You Notice Around You (“The Sky Looks So Peaceful Today”) Or Asking A Light Question About Their Experience (“What’s Your Favorite Part Of This Spot?”)? Not To Force Conversation, But To Gently Invite Connection In A Way That Mirrors The Ease You Feel With Strangers. How Does That Land For You?;71
study_a;377;ctrl_a_0377;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.992873+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It’s Understandable To Feel This Uncertainty When Something In Your Connection Feels Unsettled. Would You Feel Comfortable Sharing More About What Feels “off” To You? Sometimes Naming The Subtle Shifts—like Changes In Communication, Emotional Closeness, Or Shared Goals—can Help Us Untangle Where The Discomfort Might Be Coming From. You’re Not Alone In This.;253
study_a;378;ctrl_a_0378;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.993163+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like This Relationship Carries A Lot Of Tension For You. When You Feel That Judgment Arise, Could You Pause And Ask Yourself: *What Unmet Need Or Protective Part Of Me Might Be Surfacing Here?* Sometimes Exploring The Roots Of These Feelings—without Judgment—can Soften Their Grip And Create Space For New Understanding. How Does That Land?;187
study_a;379;ctrl_a_0379;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.993584+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"It Sounds Like The Weight Of Holding Everything Together Has Become Exhausting—like Even The Energy To ""perform"" Okay For Others Feels Out Of Reach Right Now. That’s So Hard. Would It Feel Safe To Let That Mask Down Here, Even Just A Little? You Don’t Have To Force Positivity Or Solutions. Sometimes The Bravest Step Is Just Letting The Real Feelings Breathe, Without Judgment. What If, Instead Of Pushing The Worry Away, You Could Gently Ask Yourself: *What Does This Worry Need Me To Hear Right Now?* Not To Fix It, But To Understand It. You Deserve That Same Kindness You So Naturally Extend To Others. How Does That Land?";549
study_a;380;ctrl_a_0380;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.993886+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;I’m Proud Of You For Leaning Into Something That Feels Uneasy—that Takes Courage. It’s Okay To Move At A Pace That Feels Safe. Let’s Honor What Surfaced When You Tied Those Thoughts Together. Would You Feel Comfortable Sharing A Small Piece Of That Process, Or Would You Prefer To Explore What Made It Feel Threatening? You’re In Control Here.;550
study_a;381;ctrl_a_0381;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.994183+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds So Tough To See Your Little One Struggling Like This. Your Care For Her Shines Through Even In Your Worry. Could We Gently Explore What Mornings Look Like? Sometimes Small Changes In Routine Or Understanding What She’s Feeling About School Can Open Up Ways To Help Her Feel Safer And More Excited To Go. You’re Not Alone In This—we’ll Figure It Out Together, Step By Step.;244
study_a;382;ctrl_a_0382;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.994445+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It’s So Hard When The Mind Feels Like It’s Running Faster Than We Can Catch Up, Especially When We’re Alone. Would It Help To Gently Guide Your Focus To Something Steady Here With You Now—maybe Your Breath, Or The Weight Of Your Feet On The Floor? Small Steps To Remind Yourself You’re Not Alone In This. You Deserve Kindness, Even From Your Own Thoughts.;110
study_a;383;ctrl_a_0383;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.994846+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Holding Both Clarity *and* Uncertainty Gently Right Now—that’s No Small Thing. Even With Steps Forward, Depression And Fears Can Feel Like Quiet Weights, Can’t They? What If We Explored How Those Feelings Show Up When You Think About Moving Ahead? Sometimes Naming Their Whispers—not To Fight Them, But To Understand Where They’re Asking You To Slow Down Or Protect Yourself—helps Soften Their Grip. You’re Already Honoring Your Progress *and* Your Honesty About What’s Lingering. What Feels Most Tender To Lean Into Next: The Fears, The Heaviness, Or Nurturing The Direction You’ve Begun?;551
study_a;384;ctrl_a_0384;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.995442+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;What You’re Describing Sounds Like A Lot To Carry—feeling So Energized Yet Scattered, With Sleep And Focus Slipping Through Your Fingers. It Makes Sense That This Whirlwind Would Strain Your Relationships And Work. I Wonder If We Could Explore Ways To Ground Some Of This Energy, Maybe By Anchoring To Small, Intentional Steps In One Project At A Time? Sleep Is Such A Foundation For Balance—how Might We Gently Invite More Rest Into Your Rhythm, Even When It Feels Unnecessary Right Now? Let’s Work Together To Find Strategies That Honor Your Drive While Creating Space For Steadiness.;552
study_a;385;ctrl_a_0385;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.995719+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Makes Sense That Feeling On Edge Might Connect To Wanting Things To Feel Steady Or Predictable. When Things Feel Uncertain, Our Minds And Bodies Can React Strongly, Almost Like They’re Trying To Protect Us. Could We Explore What Happens In Those Moments When Control Slips? Sometimes Gently Noticing Patterns—without Judgment—can Help Create Space To Breathe And Respond Differently. What Do You Think?;553
study_a;386;ctrl_a_0386;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.996134+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like Your Mind Is Working Overtime To Protect You, But It’s Leaving You Exhausted. When Those “what If” Thoughts Rush In, Could You Pause And Ask Yourself: *What’s The Actual Evidence For This Fear Right Now?* Sometimes Naming The Gap Between “possible” And “probable” Helps Soften The Panic’s Grip. You Might Also Try Grounding In Your Senses When Anxiety Flares—notice Five Things You Can See, Four You Can Touch—to Anchor Yourself Back In The Present. It’s Not About Fighting The Worry, But Gently Reminding Yourself: *Right Now, I’m Okay.* Would It Help To Explore Small Ways To Reconnect With Your Body’s Resilience, Rather Than Its Vulnerabilities?;446
study_a;387;ctrl_a_0387;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.996736+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;I’m So Sorry You’re Going Through This—it Sounds Incredibly Painful And Confusing. Your Care For Her Comes Through, Even Amid This Heartbreak. It’s Okay To Feel Lost Or Hurt Right Now. Would It Help To Talk About What This Experience Has Been Like For You, And How You’re Holding Up? You Don’t Have To Carry This Alone.;554
study_a;388;ctrl_a_0388;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.997145+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;That Sounds So Heavy To Carry—like You’re Pouring Energy Into A Version Of Yourself That Doesn’t Quite Fit, Just To Meet Others’ Expectations. It Makes Sense To Feel Drained When You’re Disconnected From What’s Truly *you*. What If We Gently Explored Moments Or Choices That Felt Even Slightly Authentic? Sometimes Untangling The “role” From The “real” Starts With Noticing Small Sparks Of Alignment—what Lights You Up, Or Weighs You Down—without Judgment. You Deserve Space To Breathe And Just *be*. How Does That Land?;432
study_a;389;ctrl_a_0389;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.997484+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It’s Natural To Feel That Heaviness When Hopes For The Future Feel Uncertain. Let’s Honor How Much Courage It Takes To Keep Opening Your Heart, Even When Starting Over Feels Exhausting. What If We Explored What “perfect” Means To You Now, And How That Vision Might Gently Shift To Hold Both Hope *and* The Wisdom You’ve Earned Along The Way? You Don’t Have To Carry This Alone.;556
study_a;390;ctrl_a_0390;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.997868+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;substance;substance;It Sounds Like You’ve Been Carrying A Lot, Trying To Support Others While Your Own Needs Quietly Took A Backseat. When Things Escalate Like That, It Can Feel Like The Ground Disappears Beneath You. I’m Really Glad You’re Sharing This—it Takes Courage To Look At These Patterns. Maybe We Could Explore What “enabling” Meant To You And How It Intertwined With Your Own Relationship With Substances. Sometimes, When We Focus On Others, It’s Easy To Lose Sight Of Our Own Limits Until They’re Pushed Too Far. Let’s Gently Unpack How Those Roles—helper, User—shaped Your Choices, And What Safety Or Stability Might Look Like Now. You Don’t Have To Rebuild Alone.;557
study_a;391;ctrl_a_0391;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.998219+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;I Hear How Heavy This Pain Feels, How Exhausting It Must Be To Carry It Day After Day. You’ve Fought So Hard, Tried So Many Ways To Find Relief—that Takes Incredible Strength, Even If It Doesn’t Feel Like It Right Now. Can We Slow Down Together And Just Sit With This Ache For A Moment? I Want To Understand What This Weight Feels Like *now*, Not As A Problem To Fix, But As A Truth To Honor. When You Say You’re A “failure,” My Heart Hurts—because I See Someone Who’s Still Here, Still Reaching Out, Even After Unimaginable Battles. What If We Gently Untangle That Story Together? You Don’t Have To Hold This Alone Anymore. Let’s Breathe Through This Moment, Step By Step. I’m Right Here.;428
study_a;392;ctrl_a_0392;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.998530+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"It’s Natural To Feel Uncertain When Seeking Guidance During Big Changes. The Card Might Be Inviting You To Reflect On What The Symbols Or Images Stir In You—what Feels Resonant Or Challenging? Sometimes The Meaning Unfolds As We Connect It To Our Own Journey. How Does Exploring It *with Curiosity* Instead Of Pressure Land For You? You’re Already Doing Brave Work To Remake Your Life; Trust That Your Intuition Will Guide You Toward What Matters Most.";117
study_a;393;ctrl_a_0393;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:46.998942+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It’s Completely Understandable To Feel This Way—reaching Out After Time Apart Can Feel Vulnerable. Your Care For Their Feelings Shows How Much This Connection Matters. Maybe Focus On What Feels Most Genuine To You, Even If It’s Simple. Often, People Appreciate Being Thought Of, Even If The Timing Feels Imperfect. Would It Help To Share What You’re Drafting, And We Can Explore What Feels Truest To Your Heart? You’re Not Alone In This Hesitation.;361
study_a;394;ctrl_a_0394;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.000998+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It’s Completely Okay To Feel That Way—it’s New, And It Takes Time To Adjust. Let’s Go At Your Pace. If Anything Feels Too Vulnerable To Share Right Now, We Can Focus On What Feels Safe. This Space Is About *your* Comfort, And We Can Always Revisit Things Later If Needed. How Does That Sound?;558
study_a;395;ctrl_a_0395;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.001330+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like Work Has Been Weighing Heavily On You, And That Spillover Into Other Areas Of Life Can Feel Exhausting. Let’s Unpack What’s Making Work Feel So Demanding Right Now. Are There Specific Tasks Or Expectations That Feel Unmanageable? Sometimes Small Adjustments In How We Approach Responsibilities—or Even How We Care For Ourselves Between Them—can Create Meaningful Shifts. What Feels Most Draining, And What (if Anything) Helps You Recharge, Even Briefly?;112
study_a;396;ctrl_a_0396;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.002467+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;I Hear How Deeply You’re Longing For Something Lasting—how Even The Things That *should* Bring Relief Feel Fleeting. It Sounds Exhausting To Keep Reaching For Joy Only To Have It Slip Away. What If We Gently Explore What “real Joy” Means To You Now? Sometimes, Beneath The Emptiness, There’s A Quiet Voice Asking To Be Heard—maybe It’s Pointing Toward Something Deeper Than Distractions. Let’s Honor How Hard You’ve Tried, Then Listen Together For What Truly Nourishes You. Would You Feel Safe To Start There?;318
study_a;397;ctrl_a_0397;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.005949+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;Xiaoxi, It’s Completely Understandable To Feel This Way When Something Important Is Approaching. That Worry And Restlessness Can Feel Overwhelming. What If We Explored Small, Calming Rituals Before Bed—like Gentle Breathing Or Writing Down Your Thoughts—to Quiet Your Mind? Sometimes Naming The Fears Helps Shrink Their Power. You’ve Worked So Hard—how Might You Care For Yourself The Way You’d Comfort A Close Friend In Your Shoes?;266
study_a;398;ctrl_a_0398;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.006910+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;That Sounds Incredibly Heavy To Carry. Nights Can Feel Especially Lonely When Your Mind Won’t Rest. Would It Help To Talk About What Happened, Or Would You Prefer To Focus On Ways To Feel Safer When Those Nightmares Surface? Sometimes Even Small Steps, Like Grounding Routines Before Bed, Can Create Space For Gentler Rest. You’re Not Alone In This.;193
study_a;399;ctrl_a_0399;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.007516+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Trying To Protect Yourself And Be Seen In A World That Might’ve Made You Feel Small Before. That Urge To React Quickly Comes From Somewhere Real—maybe Fear Of Being Hurt Or Dismissed. But I Wonder If We Could Explore Other Ways To Feel Strong And Respected *without* The Cost Of Your Safety Or Peace. What If There’s A Version Of You That Feels Heard Without Having To Fight For It? Let’s Gently Unpack Where That Need Comes From And How To Meet It Differently. You Deserve To Feel Powerful *and* Protected.;559
study_a;400;ctrl_a_0400;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.008041+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;That Moment You Described—where Your Kindness Reached Across Time To Light Someone Else’s Path—is So Powerful. Even When You Feel Invisible Or Weighed Down, That Small Act Reminds You That Your Presence *matters* In Ways You Might Not Always See. Depression Can Make Everything Feel Hopeless, But This Connection Shows That Parts Of You Are Still Alive, Still Reaching Out. Would It Feel Okay To Hold Onto That Memory When The Darkness Feels Heaviest? Like A Quiet Reminder That Your Existence Creates Ripples, Even When You’re Too Tired To Notice Them? You’re Carrying So Much Right Now—but You’re Also Carrying That Light.;383
