study_a;404;ctrl_a_0404;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.009234+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;Moving To A New Environment Can Stir Up So Much—it Makes Sense To Feel Unsettled. Nights Can Feel Especially Heavy When Our Minds Replay Worries. Would You Feel Comfortable Sharing What Thoughts Or Feelings Come Up When You’re Trying To Rest? Sometimes Naming Them Quietly, Or Writing Them Down, Can Soften Their Grip. Small, Calming Routines Before Bed—like Breathing Slowly Or Listening To Gentle Sounds—might Also Help Your Body Ease Into Rest. You’re Not Alone In This. How Does That Land For You?;163
