study_a;406;ctrl_a_0406;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.010307+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Putting Real Effort Into Building A Healthier Routine, And Cutting Back On Snoozing Is A Meaningful Step—even If It Didn’t Go As Planned This Time. Mornings Can Feel Rushed, Especially When Unexpected Tasks Pop Up. Would It Help To Explore Ways To Simplify Your Routine Or Prepare Ahead For Those Tasks That Tend To Slow You Down? Small Adjustments Can Add Up, And It’s Okay To Experiment Until You Find What Works. You’re Clearly Committed To Improving—that’s Something To Feel Proud Of.;562
study_a;407;ctrl_a_0407;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.010741+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like This Tension Is Really Draining For You. When Values Clash Like This, It Can Feel Like No One’s Being Heard. What If You Tried Sharing *why* Stepping Back From School Matters To You—not To Convince Them, But To Help Them Understand? Sometimes Pausing The Debate To Just Listen To Each Other’s Fears And Hopes Can Soften The Edges. What Do They Worry Might Happen If You Wait? What Do *you* Fear Might Happen If You Rush Into Something? Small Steps Toward Mutual Understanding Might Ease The Cycle Of Arguments.;564
