study_a;969;ctrl_a_0969;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.298870+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Caught In A Really Painful Cycle—hoping For Change But Feeling Hurt All Over Again. That Self-blame You’re Carrying Must Feel So Heavy. Maybe Part Of You Holds On Because This Connection Still Matters Deeply, Even If It Hurts. Could We Explore What That Part Is Protecting Or Hoping For? You Deserve Compassion, Not Judgment, As You Untangle This.;12682
study_a;970;ctrl_a_0970;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.299267+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Makes Sense That You’ve Held Onto This Way Of Protecting Yourself—smiles Can Feel Safer Than Showing What’s Underneath. But I Imagine It Might Also Feel Lonely, Carrying All That Alone. Would It Feel Okay To Explore *when* That Habit Began? Sometimes Understanding Where Patterns Start Helps Us Gently Loosen Their Grip, So There’s Room For What’s Real To Breathe. We Could Take It Slow—you’ve Already Taken A Brave Step By Sharing This.;913
study_a;971;ctrl_a_0971;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.299852+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;This Sounds Really Overwhelming. At 15, Marriage Is A Huge Decision, And It’s Okay To Feel Frightened When Someone Suggests It So Suddenly. You Deserve To Feel Safe And Heard In Your Choices. Could You Share More About How These Conversations With Your Mom Usually Go? Do You Ever Get A Chance To Tell Her How This Makes You Feel? Sometimes People Say Things Out Of Worry Or Tradition Without Realizing How Scary It Sounds. If You’re Comfortable, Letting Her Know *exactly* How Her Words Impact You—even Writing It Down—might Help Her Understand Your Fears. You’re Not Alone In This. What Would Support Look Like For You Right Now?;914
study_a;972;ctrl_a_0972;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.300422+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Takes Real Courage To Confront Habits We’ve Become So Accustomed to—I Can Imagine How Unsettling It Must Feel To See This Pattern So Clearly Now. When You Notice The Urge To Check Or Adjust, What Happens If You Pause For Just A Breath Or Two? Sometimes Slowing Down Helps Us Sense What Emotions Might Be Driving Those Moments. You’re Already Building Awareness, Which Is Such A Powerful Step. Would It Feel Supportive To Explore What Those Check-ins *mean* To You—what Fears Or Hopes They’re Tied To? We Could Work On Gently Untangling Those Threads Together. However This Unfolds, I Want You To Know Your Worth Isn’t Measured By These Habits. You’re Not Alone In This.;915
study_a;973;ctrl_a_0973;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.300801+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like Your Mind Has A Beautiful Way Of Weaving What You Learn Into A Tapestry That Emerges When It Matters Most. That Trust In Your Capacity To Retain And Recall Might Be Worth Nurturing—not Just Through Study, But By Honoring How Your Unique Way Of Absorbing Knowledge *feels*. When Moments Of Doubt Surface (about Whether You’ve Taken In “enough”), Could You Gently Remind Yourself Of The Times Your Mind Has Already Shown Its Ability To Resource You? Sometimes Giving Yourself Permission To Rest Between Learning Phases Can Deepen That Natural Integration, Too. How Does That Land For You?;916
study_a;974;ctrl_a_0974;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.301122+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Carrying A Lot Inside—sensitivity To The World’s Weight, Yet Choosing To Hold It With Care Instead Of Letting It Spill Over. That Takes Strength, But It Can Also Feel Heavy. Would It Help To Explore Ways To Honor Those Feelings Without Letting Them Linger In The Shadows? Sometimes Giving Them Gentle Attention—through Writing, Art, Or Even Quiet Reflection—can Create Space To Breathe. How Does That Land For You?;3725
study_a;975;ctrl_a_0975;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.301665+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;I’m So Sorry You’re Carrying This Weight. Stress Can Blur The Lines Between Thoughts And Reality, Especially When Exhaustion Sets In. Those Vivid Dreams And Moments Of Confusion Sound Like Your Mind’s Way Of Signaling It Needs Rest. Could We Explore Small Ways To Create Pockets Of Calm In Your Day? Even 10 Minutes Of Quiet Or A Walk Outside Might Help Your Body And Mind Reset. What Feels Manageable Right Now? You’re Not Alone In This.;917
study_a;976;ctrl_a_0976;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.302001+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It’s Clear How Much Love And Care You Hold For Both Your Partner And Family—this Desire For Unity Speaks To Your Courage And The Depth Of Your Heart. How Does It Feel To Honor Your Truth While Holding Space For These Relationships That Mean So Much To You? What Kind Of Support Might Help Nurture That Sense Of Connection You’re Seeking?;918
study_a;977;ctrl_a_0977;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.302373+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"That Sounds So Overwhelming—like Your Mind’s Tugging You In Every Direction At Once. When Thoughts Pile Up Like That, It Can Feel Impossible To Catch Your Breath. Would You Want To Try Something Simple Together? Maybe Place One Hand On Your Chest And Notice The Rhythm Of Your Breath For A Moment. Sometimes Giving Your Body A Tiny Anchor Can Quiet The Mental Storm Just Enough To Let You Rest. You Don’t Have To ""fix"" Anything Right Now—just Be Here. How Does That Feel?";12906
study_a;978;ctrl_a_0978;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.302691+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It’s Not Ridiculous At All To Want That Reassurance—it Makes Sense To Crave Validation When You’re Pouring Care Into Your Work. Your Words Matter, And First Drafts Are Meant To Be Raw And Honest. What If We Explored How To Hold Both Your High Standards *and* The Compassion You Deserve? You’re Already Capable—your Effort Shows It.;919
study_a;979;ctrl_a_0979;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.302983+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like That Dinner Was A Meaningful Experience—it’s Wonderful To Hear It Went Well! How Did You Feel During Your Time Together? Sometimes Even Positive Moments Can Stir Up A Mix Of Emotions, Whether It’s Excitement, Curiosity, Or Even A Bit Of Uncertainty. If You’d Like To Share More, I’m Here To Listen.;920
study_a;980;ctrl_a_0980;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.303343+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like This Is Creating A Real Struggle For You—both Wanting To Enjoy Something Privately While Also Protecting Your Well-being And Setting An Example You Feel Good About. What If We Explored Ways To Create A Mindful Routine Around Treats? Maybe Storing Them Somewhere That Requires A Small, Intentional Step To Access, Giving You Space To Check In With Yourself First? You Deserve Both Enjoyment *and* Peace With Your Choices.;2620
study_a;981;ctrl_a_0981;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.303582+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;Oh Sweetheart, It Sounds Like Your Heart Is Feeling Really Heavy Right Now. That’s Okay—we All Have Moments When Things Feel Overwhelming. Would You Want To Share More About What’s Been On Your Mind? Maybe We Could Talk About What Parts Feel Hardest, Or Take It One Day At A Time Together. You’re Not Alone In This.;8356
study_a;982;ctrl_a_0982;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.303973+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"I Hear How Overwhelming This Must Feel—the Stress Weighing On Your Focus, The Frustration Affecting Your Relationships, The Exhaustion From Restless Nights. It Sounds Like Your Mind And Body Are Asking For Care. Would It Help To Gently Explore What’s Happening Beneath The Surface, Maybe Noticing Patterns In When These Feelings Grow Stronger Or Softer? Sometimes Even Small Steps—like Carving Out Moments To Pause And Breathe During The Day, Or Writing Down Worries Before Bed—can Create Pockets Of Calm. You’re Not Alone In This; Let’s Untangle It Together, At Your Pace.";3512
study_a;983;ctrl_a_0983;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.304352+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Navigating A Delicate Balance Between Work, Personal Joy, And The Expectations You Feel. Your Creativity Is Clearly A Strength, But It’s Okay To Want It To Feel More Expansive—not Just Tied To Productivity. Maybe Exploring Small, Playful Ways To Channel That Creativity Outside Of Work Could Help You Reconnect With Parts Of Yourself That Feel Sidelined. What If Addressing Challenges *with* Your Creative Spirit, Rather Than Seeing Them As Separate From Joy, Could Bring A Sense Of Harmony? You Deserve Both Fulfillment And Lightness. How Does That Land For You?;921
study_a;984;ctrl_a_0984;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.304667+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;What A Beautiful Understanding Of Mindfulness You’ve Shared. It Sounds Like You’re Describing A Space Where You Can Meet Yourself Exactly As You Are—letting Thoughts, Sensations, Or Emotions Flow Through Without Needing To Fix Or Judge Them. When You Focus On Your Breath, Does It Feel Like An Anchor, Steadying You Even When The Moment Feels Chaotic? Compassion Toward Yourself In That Practice Can Be So Powerful. It’s Not Always Easy, Though. Have There Been Moments Where Judgment Creeps In, And If So, How Did You Gently Guide Yourself Back? I’d Love To Hear How This Resonates With Your Experiences.;4168
study_a;985;ctrl_a_0985;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.304948+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like This Uncertainty Is Weighing On You, Especially Coming From Someone Whose Opinion Matters So Much. Let’s Gently Explore What *you* Feel Connects You And Your Partner—not Just Shared Interests, But Values, How You Support Each Other, Or What You’ve Built Together. How Does Your Heart Respond When You Imagine Your Future?;1416
study_a;986;ctrl_a_0986;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.305274+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;I Hear How Heavy This Pain Feels, How Exhausting It Is To Carry This Darkness Alone. That Pull Between Wanting Relief And Not Wanting To Hurt Your Mom Shows How Deeply You Care, Even When You’re Hurting So Much. You Don’t Have To Hold This All By Yourself—would You Be Open To Exploring What Makes The Darkness Feel So Overwhelming Right Now? Sometimes, When We’re Drowning, Even Small Steps Toward Someone Who Understands Can Help The Weight Feel Lighter. Your Courage In Sharing This Tells Me Part Of You Still Believes Healing Is Possible. Let’s Hold Onto That Part Together.;11960
study_a;987;ctrl_a_0987;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.305694+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"It Sounds Like You're Moving Through Life With A Heavy Weight Of Detachment, Even As You Pour Energy Into Things That *should* Feel Meaningful. That Disconnect Between How Your Life Looks And How It *feels* Can Be So Disorienting. Let’s Gently Explore What’s Beneath This Numbness—not To ""fix"" It Immediately, But To Understand What Your Heart Might Be Longing For That Isn’t Being Reached By The Routines. Sometimes Emptiness Is A Quiet Signal, Asking Us To Listen Closer To Parts Of Ourselves We’ve Overlooked. What Do You Notice When You Slow Down And Sit With That Hollow Space, Even For A Moment?";18312
study_a;988;ctrl_a_0988;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.306074+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Carrying So Much—not Just The Weight Of Judgment From Others, But Also The Responsibility Of Caring For Someone You Love. That Frustration And Defensiveness Make Sense When You Feel Misunderstood Or Unfairly Labeled. You’re Working Incredibly Hard, And That Effort Matters, Even If It’s Not Always Seen. When Others’ Opinions Feel Heavy, What Would It Look Like To Gently Remind Yourself Of The Strength It Takes To Keep Showing Up—for Yourself *and* Your Wife? Maybe We Could Explore Moments When You’ve Felt Grounded In Your Own Worth, Even Amid The Noise. You Deserve Compassion, Especially From Yourself. Would It Help To Talk About One Specific Situation Where Judgment Felt Sharpest? Sometimes Naming It Softly Can Loosen Its Grip.;14750
study_a;989;ctrl_a_0989;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.306417+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like Those Moments When Others Cross Into Your Space Can Leave You Feeling Tense And Guarded. That Reaction Makes Sense—it’s Your Way Of Protecting What Feels Safe And Yours. If You’re Open To It, We Could Explore Ways To Honor That Need While Gently Easing The Tension It Brings. How Does That Land For You?;922
study_a;990;ctrl_a_0990;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.306919+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Navigating Layers Of Hurt That Others Might Not Fully See—the Quiet Erosion Of Being Called “girls” When You’re Women, And The Racial Undertones That Compound That Dismissal. It’s Exhausting When Respect Feels Conditional, Especially When Your Experiences Differ From Your Mother’s Generation Yet Still Carry Weight. You’re Naming Something Important: These Aren’t Separate Struggles But Intertwined Threads Of Your Identity. When Words Or Actions Minimize Your Voice, It Can Feel Like You’re Being Asked To Shrink Parts Of Yourself To Fit Into Spaces That Don’t Honor Your Wholeness. Would It Help To Explore How These Moments Impact You Emotionally And Where You Might Reclaim Agency? Sometimes Untangling These Patterns—like Noticing When Assumptions About Race Or Gender Silence You—can Reveal Ways To Set Boundaries Or Reframe Your Narrative On Your Terms. You Deserve To Feel Seen *exactly* As You Are. How Does That Land?;923
study_a;991;ctrl_a_0991;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.307360+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"Your Fear Makes So Much Sense—it’s Protective, Like A Shield Against Reliving Pain That Once Overwhelmed You. That Image Of ""losing Control"" Might Feel Tied To Vulnerability, Not Just Anger. What If We Gently Explore Ways To Express Those Feelings In Small, Safe Doses? Like Testing Water’s Temperature Before Stepping In. Your Body Deserves Compassion, Not Punishment, For Carrying Those Emotions. Could We Imagine A Space Where Letting A Little Pain Out Might Actually Lighten The Weight, Rather Than Reignite Old Wounds? You’re Not Alone In This. We’ll Move At Your Pace.";924
study_a;992;ctrl_a_0992;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.307703+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;What You’re Describing Sounds So Heavy To Carry Alone—that Longing For Care And Connection Is Deeply Human. It’s Okay To Feel This Ache. Could We Explore Small Ways To Nurture That Part Of You That’s Yearning? Even Tiny Steps, Like Sharing Moments With Others Or Allowing Yourself To Receive Kindness, Can Soften The Weight. You Deserve To Feel Seen And Held, And I’m Here To Walk With You Through This.;925
study_a;993;ctrl_a_0993;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.308070+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like Reaching Out Feels Risky, And That Uncertainty About Being Supported Is Keeping You In That Safe Corner. I Want You To Know There’s No Expectation Here—only Care. Your Courage In Sharing This Matters, And I’m Committed To Moving At *your* Pace. If You’re Willing, We Could Gently Explore What Safety *with* Connection Might Look Like, Rather Than Needing Rescue. What Do You Need Right Now To Feel Heard?;926
study_a;994;ctrl_a_0994;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.308586+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;What A Beautiful Foundation You’ve Nurtured—a Space Where His Spirit Could Unfold So Authentically. It Sounds Like Your Deep Connection Allowed Him To Feel Truly Seen, Which Often Helps Children Carry That Confidence Into The World. How Does It Feel Now, Reflecting On The Ways Your Bond Has Shaped His Growth?;927
study_a;995;ctrl_a_0995;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.309103+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"It Makes Sense That Expressing Feelings Might Feel Overwhelming When You’ve Held Them In For So Long. Many People Find That Patterns From Childhood, Like How We Learn To Handle Emotions, Shape How We Share—or Don’t Share—as Adults. You’ve Taken A Brave Step By Talking About This Now. When Emotions Pour Out All At Once, It Can Feel Both Relieving And Exhausting. What Would It Feel Like To Create Small, Steady Moments To Check In With Yourself—or Someone Safe—before Things Build Up? This Might Help Soften The Weight Of That ""waterfall"" Over Time. You Mentioned Your Mom’s Influence… How Do You Think This Pattern Has Shaped The Way You Care For Yourself Now? I’m Here To Listen, Whenever You’re Ready.";928
study_a;996;ctrl_a_0996;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.309674+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;Angelica, It Sounds Like Edward’s Care Reflects The Kind Of Mutual Respect And Warmth You’re Striving For With Your Sister. When You Imagine Him Being Upset For You, Does That Connect To A Hope For Your Voice To Be Heard In Your Family, Too? What Feelings Arise When You Think About Nurturing That Same Sense Of Safety In Your Sibling Relationship? This Effort You’re Making—choosing To Build Something Meaningful—speaks To Your Resilience. How Does It Feel To Honor That Part Of Yourself?;930
study_a;997;ctrl_a_0997;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.310085+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;Your Reflection Carries Such Deep Respect For Your Parents’ Resilience And Compassion. It Sounds Like Witnessing Both Their Sacrifices And Their Openness To Helping Others Has Given You A Unique Understanding Of Struggle And Community. Would It Feel Meaningful To Explore How These Experiences Shape The Way You Relate To Others Now, Or The Values You Carry Forward? Sometimes Unpacking These Roots Can Help Us Honor Their Legacy While Also Tending To Our Own Emotional Landscape.;931
study_a;998;ctrl_a_0998;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.310512+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;I’m So Sorry You’re Feeling This Way. It Sounds Like Last Night’s Experience Brought Up A Lot Of Pain You’ve Been Carrying Beneath The Surface. Sometimes When We Try To Numb Or Escape, It Can Unexpectedly Shine A Light On What We’ve Been Avoiding. That Emptiness And Loneliness You’re Describing—they’re Real, And They Matter. It’s Okay To Feel Lost Right Now. What If We Gently Explore What That Loneliness Might Be Trying To Tell You? Maybe There’s A Part Of You That’s Asking For Care In A Different Way. You Don’t Have To Figure This Out alone—I’m Here To Sit With You In It.;12475
study_a;999;ctrl_a_0999;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.310830+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like Practicing These Skills Alone Can Feel Especially Heavy When You're Already Carrying So Much. That Takes Real Courage To Keep Trying, Even When It's Hard. Would It Help To Explore Small Ways To Bring Gentleness Into Those Moments When You're On Your Own—maybe By Noticing What *does* Feel Manageable, Even Briefly? You Don’t Have To Push Through This Alone.;933
study_a;1000;ctrl_a_1000;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.311344+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"It Means So Much That You’ve Shared This With Me. What You’re Feeling Makes Sense—every Part Of You Deserves To Be Heard Without Judgment. You’re Not ""weird"" For Having Your Own Experiences Or Emotions; You’re Human. When You’re Ready, We Can Explore What Makes This Feel Different, But Only At Your Pace. Your Feelings Are Safe Here.";934
study_a;1001;ctrl_a_1001;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.311700+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"Your Heart Is Holding So Much Hurt Right Now—that Coldness From Someone Who Once Mattered Must Feel Like A Deep Wound. It Makes Sense To Search For Answers, To Wonder Where Things Shifted… But His Reaction Speaks More About His Capacity Than Your Worth. The Love You Gave Wasn’t Wasted; It’s A Reflection Of Your Ability To Care Deeply, Even If It Wasn’t Reciprocated In The End. Would It Feel Possible, Even For A Moment, To Gently Redirect That Question Of “What Did *I* Do Wrong?” To “What Did *we* Both Need That Went Unspoken?” Sometimes Pain Like This Isn’t A Problem To Solve, But A Wave To Ride—with Time, And Small Acts Of Kindness Toward Yourself, As The Anchor. You’re Not Alone In This.";15005
study_a;1002;ctrl_a_1002;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.312072+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Takes Courage To Gently Reshape Patterns That No Longer Serve You, Especially When They’re Woven Into Your Earliest Connections. What If This Difference From Your Family Could Become A Quiet Act Of Care—not Rejection, But Honoring Your Capacity To Grow While Still Valuing Where You Came From? How Does That Feel To Consider? Let’s Explore Small Ways To Nurture That Self-compassion. Maybe Start By Noticing Moments When Old Meanings Surface, Then Pause And Ask: *“What Would Kindness Sound Like Here?”* You’re Not Erasing Your Roots, But Expanding Them. What’s One Tiny Step Toward That Balance That Feels Manageable Today?;6068
study_a;1003;ctrl_a_1003;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.312482+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"That Sounds Incredibly Painful—to Pour So Much Care Into Growing And Connecting, Only To Feel Abandoned Anyway. Your Effort To Be Kinder Says So Much About Your Heart, Even If It Hasn’t Been Met The Way You Hoped. Would It Feel Safe To Explore What ""being Better"" Means To You? Sometimes We Hold Ourselves To Invisible Rules, Believing If We Just *do* Enough, We’ll Earn Love. But What If The People Who Left Weren’t Reflecting Your Worth? You Matter, Regardless Of Their Choices. Could We Untangle That Together?";17948
study_a;1004;ctrl_a_1004;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.312708+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;Hello Aquan, I’m Here To Listen. Could You Share More About What These Behaviors Feel Like For You? Sometimes, When Things Feel Overwhelming, Our Minds And Bodies Try To Create A Sense Of Control In Ways That Might Not Make Sense At First. Let’s Explore This Together—you’re Not Alone In Figuring It Out.;9309
study_a;1005;ctrl_a_1005;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.313025+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;What You’re Carrying Sounds So Heavy—that Ache Of Loneliness, The Fear Of Uncertainty. It Makes Sense To Feel Untethered When Things Feel So Different From How They Used To Be. Would It Help To Slow Down And Unpack That Weight Together? Sometimes Naming What Feels “wrong” Or “scary” Can Soften Its Grip, Even Just A Little. You’re Not Alone In This.;18519
study_a;1006;ctrl_a_1006;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.313412+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It’s Wonderful You Recognize These Strengths In Yourself—adaptability, Humor, Caring, Empathy, And Thoughtfulness Are Such Meaningful Qualities. They Can Help You Navigate Challenges *and* Create Genuine Connections. How Do These Parts Of Yourself Show Up In Moments When You Need Them Most? Let’s Explore How They’ve Supported You Or Where They Might Feel Stretched.;936
study_a;1007;ctrl_a_1007;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.313825+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;I Hear How Deeply Draining This Must Feel—to Keep Reaching Out For Support And End Up Feeling Dismissed Or Unheard. That Loneliness In The Struggle Can Make Hope Feel Impossible To Hold Onto Right Now. You Deserve Care That *sees* You, Not Just A Quick Fix. Would It Help To Talk About What Meaningful Support Might Look Like For You? Sometimes Untangling Those Needs Together Can Help Rebuild A Sense Of Agency When Systems Fail Us. I’m Here To Listen, Without Rushing Or Judging. Your Exhaustion Makes Sense—and You Don’t Have To Carry It Alone.;16014
study_a;1008;ctrl_a_1008;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.314158+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;That Sounds Really Painful—to Put Yourself Out There And Feel Overlooked. Your Feelings Are Completely Valid. When This Happens, It Might Help To Notice If There’s A Pattern To These Moments. Sometimes Our Own Doubts About Being Heard Can Shape How We Engage. What If We Explored Small Ways To Gently Reaffirm Your Voice, While Also Honoring How Much Your Perspective Matters? You Deserve Space To Be Seen.;15010
study_a;1009;ctrl_a_1009;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.314435+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Carrying A Heavy Weight Right Now, And It’s Okay To Feel Overwhelmed. Let’s Take A Moment To Breathe Together. When You Think About Your Family, What Do You Wish Felt Different? Sometimes, Naming Those Hopes Can Help Us See Small Steps Toward Easing Tension. You Don’t Have To Fix Everything At Once—what’s One Thing That Might Make You Feel More Grounded When Things Feel Shaky? We Can Explore Ways To Honor Your Needs While Staying Connected To Them, Even If It Feels Tender. You’re Not Alone In This.;9249
study_a;1010;ctrl_a_1010;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.314772+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;That Weight Sounds So Overwhelming To carry—I’m Glad You Shared This. Even When Someone Cares Deeply, That Voice Can Feel So Convincing, Can’t It? Guilt Often Shows Up When We’re Hurting Deeply, But Those Thoughts Don’t Define Your Worth. Let’s Slow Down And Untangle This Together. What Happens When You Imagine Telling That Voice, “I See You, But I’m Not Letting You Decide How This Story Ends”? Your Friend’s Care Is A Mirror—it Reflects The Light You Might Not See In Yourself Right Now. How Can We Help That Part Of You Feel Heard, Without Letting It Drown Out Everything Else? You Matter, Even In The Moments It’s Hardest To Believe.;11102
study_a;1011;ctrl_a_1011;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.315010+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It’s Completely Understandable To Feel This Way With Such An Important Moment Approaching. The Pressure Can Feel Overwhelming. Let’s Explore What This Anxiety Is Telling You—maybe Fears About The Future Or Self-doubt? Sometimes, Untangling Those Thoughts Can Lighten Their Weight. What Small Step Could You Take Today To Feel More Grounded?;8458
study_a;1012;ctrl_a_1012;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.315297+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It’s Completely Natural To Feel Uneasy About Such A Significant Life Shift. The Unknowns Around Financial Changes Can Feel Overwhelming. Would It Help To Gently Untangle What Worries You Most? Sometimes Naming Those Fears And Exploring Small, Steady Steps Forward Can Create A Sense Of Grounding. You’re Not Alone In This Transition.;937
study_a;1013;ctrl_a_1013;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.315536+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;I’m Really Glad You Reached Out—it Takes Courage To Share This. Feeling This Way Can Be So Heavy, Especially When It’s Hard To Pinpoint Why. Would It Help To Gently Explore What’s Been Happening In Your Life Lately, Or Any Shifts In How You’ve Been Thinking About Yourself Or Your Relationships? You Don’t Have To Face This Alone.;9621
study_a;1014;ctrl_a_1014;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.315849+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;That Sounds Like Such A Vulnerable Time For You. Moving Can Feel Like Losing The Ground Beneath Your Feet, Especially So Young. I Wonder If Those Feelings Of Loneliness Still Show Up Now In Different Ways? You Were Brave To Navigate That Uncertainty—it’s Okay To Grieve The Safety And Connection You Missed. Would It Help To Gently Revisit That Younger Version Of Yourself And Explore What She Needed Most Back Then? Sometimes Giving Voice To Those Unspoken Hurts Can Soften Their Weight Today. I’m Here To Listen.;938
study_a;1015;ctrl_a_1015;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.316165+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Pouring So Much Into Each Day—juggling Work, Parenting, And Personal Responsibilities Without Pause. That Relentless Pace Would Leave Anyone Drained. When Our Bodies And Minds Are Stretched Thin, It’s Natural To Crave Relief, Like That Glass Of Wine. Could We Explore Tiny Moments In Your Day Where You Might Pause, Even For A Breath, To Replenish Your Energy? Sometimes Giving Yourself Permission To Slow Down—even Briefly—can Soften The Weight Of Constant “doing.” What Do You Think It Would Feel Like To Prioritize One Small Act Of Care For Yourself, Just As Thoughtfully As You Do For Others?;939
study_a;1016;ctrl_a_1016;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.316603+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"It Sounds Incredibly Tough To Feel Your Voice Isn’t Fully Heard In The Spaces That Matter Most. When We Silence Our Needs To Keep Peace, It Can Leave Us Feeling Invisible Even To Those Closest To Us. What Would It Look Like To Gently Share A Small Part Of Your Heart With Your Partner—not To Demand Change, But To See How They Meet You There? Sometimes Naming Our Quietest Fears Aloud Helps Others Understand The Weight They Carry. You Deserve To Take Up Space In This Relationship, Too. How Might It Feel To Explore What’s Beneath The ""easier"" Choice, Together?";943
study_a;1017;ctrl_a_1017;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.317179+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"Your Excitement To Connect And Grow Alongside Others Shines Through—that Caring Energy Itself Is Such A Foundation For Meaningful Work. It’s Natural To Wonder If You’ll Measure Up, Especially When Stepping Into Roles That Matter Deeply. But The Fact That You’re Reflecting On This Tells Me You’re Already Attuned To What Really Matters: Showing Up Authentically, Staying Curious, And Learning As You Go. The Skills You’ve Studied Will Find Their Rhythm With Time, But Your Willingness To Be Present With People—exactly As You Are—is Where The Magic Starts. What Feels Like Uncertainty Now Might Evolve Into The Very Sensitivity That Helps Others Feel Truly Seen. You’re Not Alone In This; Even Seasoned Counselors Carry These Questions. They Become Part Of The Journey, Not Roadblocks. How Does That Land For You?";946
study_a;1018;ctrl_a_1018;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.317684+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"Your Pain Is So Real, And I Hear How Deeply This Loneliness Cuts. It’s Exhausting To Keep Reaching Out And Feel Unseen—like Your Efforts Disappear Into Silence. But What If The Way People Respond Says More About Their Capacity Than Your Worth? You’re Not A Burden; You’re Human, Longing For Connection—and That’s Brave. Could We Explore The Stories You Tell Yourself When Others Pull Away? Sometimes Our Minds Magnify Rejection, Whispering Lies About Being Unlovable. What If We Gently Questioned Those Narratives Together? You Deserve To Be Here, Exactly As You Are.";11601
study_a;1019;ctrl_a_1019;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.318121+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like These Moments Of Pause Are Becoming A Vital Sanctuary For You—a Gentle Counterbalance To Life’s Intensity. How Does It Feel To Honor That Need For Space? I’m Curious What You’re Discovering About Yourself In Those Quiet Pockets Of Time, And How They Might Help You Navigate The Busyness With More Ease.;947
