study_a;1021;ctrl_a_1021;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.318897+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"I Hear How Heavy That Numbness Must Feel—like Life Is Happening At A Distance, Muffled And Muted. It Takes So Much Strength Just To Keep Moving When Everything Feels Colorless. Would It Help To Gently Explore What’s On The Other Side Of That Glass Together? Sometimes Even Naming The Quietest Flicker Of Emotion—a Hint Of Frustration, A Wisp Of Longing—can Begin To Soften The Walls. You Don’t Have To Push Or ""fix"" Anything Right Now. I’m Here, Walking Beside You In This Space.";11206
study_a;1022;ctrl_a_1022;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.319251+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;That Sounds Deeply Painful—to Carry That Memory Of Fighting So Hard Just To Feel Seen, And To Still Feel That Ache Of Not Quite Belonging. It Makes Sense That Those Early Experiences Might Shape How You Move Through The World Now. Part Of You Learned To Protect Your Place Fiercely, Even As A Child. I Wonder How That Protective Part Shows Up Today, And What It Might Need To Feel Safe Enough To Soften? You Deserve Spaces Where You Can Simply Exist, Without Having To Fight For Your Worth. Would It Feel Helpful To Explore Ways To Reconnect With That Younger Version Of Yourself—to Offer Them The Compassion And Belonging They Craved Back Then?;6268
study_a;1023;ctrl_a_1023;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.319562+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;I Hear How Heavy This Pain Feels, And I’m So Glad You’re Sharing It. You’re Not Alone In Carrying This. When Hopelessness Clouds Everything, Even Small Steps Forward Can Feel Impossible—but Your Feelings Matter, And So Does Your Presence Here. Could We Explore What Might Help Lighten This Weight, Even Just A Little? You Don’t Have To Hold It All By Yourself.;16805
