study_a;1033;ctrl_a_1033;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.323392+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"It Sounds Like That Fear Feels Heavy To Carry, Especially When Past Experiences Make It Feel So Real. Many People Find That Looking Closely At Those ""mistakes"" With Curiosity—rather Than Judgment—helps Soften Their Grip. What If We Gently Explored What Those Moments Taught You About Your Strengths, Not Just The Struggle?";2956
study_a;1034;ctrl_a_1034;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.323687+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;This Sounds Incredibly Painful—feeling Unsupported In A Relationship Can Leave You Torn Between Love And Uncertainty. Have You And Your Boyfriend Shared How This Tension Affects Each Of You? Sometimes, Exploring What You *both* Need To Feel Secure—and What Boundaries Could Protect Your Connection—helps Clarity Emerge. You Deserve To Feel Valued, Both By Him And Within This Dynamic. How Does That Land For You?;8321
study_a;1035;ctrl_a_1035;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.324176+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Incredibly Frustrating To Feel So Unheard, Especially When You’re Trying To Connect Honestly. You’ve Shown Courage In Sharing Your Truth, Even When Met With Anger Or Dismissal. Would It Help To Explore Ways To Express Yourself That Might Feel Safer For You, While Also Protecting Your Peace? Sometimes Small Steps—like Writing Down Your Thoughts First Or Choosing Moments When Emotions Are Calm—can Create Space For Understanding, Even If It Takes Time. You Deserve To Feel Seen, And It’s Okay To Seek Support From Others Who Can Hold Space For You When Family Struggles To Listen. How Does That Land With You?;957
study_a;1036;ctrl_a_1036;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.324508+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Carrying A Lot Of Care For Fairness And Understanding, And It’s Painful When Others Don’t Meet That. I Wonder If Stepping Back From Trying To “fight” Their Views Could Help? Maybe Asking Gentle Questions To Uncover *why* They Feel So Strongly—sometimes People Soften When They Feel Heard First. What Do You Think?;958
