study_a;1038;ctrl_a_1038;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.325478+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;I Hear How Hard This Has Been For You—feeling Stuck In This Heaviness, Even With Things You Used To Love. It Sounds Exhausting, And It’s Okay To Feel Concerned. These Shifts In Energy, Focus, And Even Sleep Can Feel So Isolating. You’re Not Alone In This. Would You Want To Explore What Might Be Weighing On Your Heart Right Now, Or How These Feelings Show Up Day To Day? We Can Take It Step By Step, Together.;960
study_a;1039;ctrl_a_1039;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.325829+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"It Sounds Like The Warmth Of Being With Loved Ones Might Naturally Ease The Pressure You Feel To ""do It All."" Their Presence Could Remind You That Rest Is Okay, Even Necessary. When Alone, Maybe That Pressure Returns? What If You Tried To Carry A Bit Of That Connected, Calm Feeling Into Your Evenings—like Creating A Small Ritual That Mirrors The Comfort Of Family Time?";965
study_a;1040;ctrl_a_1040;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.326249+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Takes Real Strength To Recognize The Desire To Grow Beyond What’s Familiar, Especially When The Unknown Feels Daunting. Starting Small Might Help—perhaps Visiting A Cozy Café Or A Community Cooking Class Where Shared Interests Naturally Connect People. Each Step, Even Brief Visits, Could Gently Stretch Your Comfort Zone, Building Confidence In Your Ability To Adapt. What Matters Most Is Honoring Your Pace—celebrating Every Moment You Choose To Explore, While Knowing It’s Okay To Retreat And Reflect When Needed. How Does That Idea Sit With You?;966
study_a;1041;ctrl_a_1041;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.326508+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Carrying A Lot Of Weight From Feeling Pulled In Different Directions. That Kind Of Tension Can Be So Draining. Would It Help To Talk About What Each “side” Of This Conflict Means To You? Sometimes Untangling The Threads Of What We Value Most Can Bring Unexpected Clarity. I’m Here To Listen.;600
study_a;1042;ctrl_a_1042;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.326788+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It’s Okay To Feel Discomfort Around Certain Topics—you’re Honoring Your Boundaries, And That’s Important. Your Care For Your Dog Shows How Deeply You Value Connection And Safety. If It Feels Right, We Can Explore What Makes These Conversations Uneasy, Always At Your Pace. You’re In Control Here, Just Like You Create Comfort For Your Pup.;3215
study_a;1043;ctrl_a_1043;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.327148+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;I Hear How Unsettling This Feels—those Physical Reactions Can Be So Overwhelming. Let’s Gently Explore What “go Out” Might Mean For You In These Moments. Could There Be A Hidden Worry Or Memory Tied To Those Words? When The Discomfort Arises, Maybe Pause And Take Slow Breaths, Noticing Where You Feel Grounded (like Your Feet On The Floor). This Might Help Soften The Intensity. You’re Not Alone In This—we Can Work Together To Uncover What Your Mind And Body Are Trying To Tell You. How Does That Sound?;10161
study_a;1044;ctrl_a_1044;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.327708+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Carrying So Much—juggling Caregiving, Learning, Contributing To Meaningful Causes, *and* Keeping Life Running. That’s A Lot To Hold. When Days Feel Like A Race, It’s Easy To Lose Sight Of Your Own Needs. Would It Help To Explore Small Ways To Weave Moments Of Calm Or Connection Into The Rhythm Of Your Day? Even Tiny Pauses Can Replenish Energy. You’re Doing Important Things—how Does It Feel To Reflect On All You’re Balancing Right Now?;968
study_a;1045;ctrl_a_1045;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.328192+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;I’m So Sorry You’re Carrying This Weight. That Hollow Ache In Your Chest, The Fog Holding You Still—it Makes Sense When Something So Central To Your World Shifts Suddenly. It’s Exhausting To Feel Both Numb And Overwhelmed At Once. When Your Mind Replays Those Moments, Does Part Of You Try To Solve The “why,” Or Does It Just Sting Fresh Each Time? Let’s Honor How Real This Pain Is—it’s Okay To Need Time To Grieve What You Thought You Had. Would It Help To Untangle Some Of Those Replaying Thoughts Together? Sometimes When We Dissect The Story We’re Telling Ourselves (“They Did This To Me”), Small Cracks Of Light Appear—maybe Moments Where You *did* Function, Even A Little, Or Glimpses Of What Still Matters Beneath The Numbness. We Can Move At The Pace Your Body And Heart Need. You’re Not Broken—you’re Adapting, Even When It Doesn’t Feel Like It.;13960
study_a;1046;ctrl_a_1046;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.328481+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It’s Okay To Feel Uncertain—life Rarely Follows A Straight Path. Let’s Start By Gently Exploring What Truly Matters To You. What Small Steps Could You Take Today That Align With Your Values, Even If The Bigger Picture Feels Unclear? We’ll Move At Your Pace, One Choice At A Time.;8394
study_a;1047;ctrl_a_1047;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.328974+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;That Sounds Incredibly Lonely—to Have Your Pain Minimized Because It Doesn’t Match Someone Else’s Expectations. Your Feelings Are Valid, No Matter How You Present Outwardly. It’s Okay To Feel Angry When Others Try To Box Your Experience Into Something They Can Easily Label. How Does It Sit With You When They Say Those Things? What Do You Wish They Understood About Your Struggle Instead? Let’s Explore Ways To Honor Your Truth, Even When Others Can’t See It. You Deserve To Be Heard.;10575
study_a;1048;ctrl_a_1048;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.329292+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;I Hear How Worn Down You Feel—this Cycle Must Weigh So Heavily On Your Heart. It Makes Sense To Feel Drained When You’re Pouring So Much Into Just Staying Afloat. Can We Look At What Parts Of This Struggle Feel Most Overwhelming? Sometimes Untangling One Thread Can Help Us See A Path Forward, Even If It’s Small. You’ve Shown Such Resilience Just By Keeping Going. Let’s Honor That Strength While Finding Ways To Lighten The Load, Step By Step.;12738
study_a;1049;ctrl_a_1049;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.329692+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Takes Real Strength To Confront Patterns That Have Been Part Of Your Life For Years—three Days Is A Meaningful Step Forward, Even If It Feels Shaky. That Tightness You’re Feeling Might Be Your Body And Mind Adjusting To Change, Which Is Natural. You’re Doing Hard, Important Work. Since Breathing Strategies Alone Aren’t Easing The Tension, Let’s Explore What Else Might Help. Sometimes Pairing A Grounding Practice With Something Tactile (like Holding A Cold Object Or Scribbling On Paper) Can Shift The Intensity. Or, When The Urge Arises, Could You Name What’s Beneath It—stress, Habit, Something Else? Even Just Pausing To Ask, “What Do I Truly Need Right Now?” Creates Space To Choose. Your Partner’s Support Matters, But This Is *your* Journey. How Can You Honor Both Your Progress And The Struggle Without Judgment? Let’s Find Ways To Make The Adjustment Feel Less Like A Battle. You’re Not Alone In This.;969
study_a;1050;ctrl_a_1050;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.330098+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;This Sounds So Painful, And I’m Here With You. When Our Minds Swing Between Extremes Like That, It Can Feel Impossible To Find Solid Ground. Would It Help To Slow Down And Look At Moments Where Your Partner *has* Shown Care, Even In Small Ways? Sometimes Naming Those Specifics Can Soften The Fog. You’re Not Alone In This—we’ll Untangle It Together.;18315
study_a;1051;ctrl_a_1051;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.330464+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;I Hear How Deeply This Loneliness Weighs On You, Even In Moments When You’re Not Physically Alone. That Sense Of Being Separate, Like Others Have A Script You Weren’t Given—it Sounds Exhausting. Could We Explore How Those Thoughts Show Up When You’re With Others? Sometimes Our Minds Whisper Stories About What People Think Of Us That Aren’t True, But They *feel* So Real. What If We Gently Untangle Those Thoughts Together, And Maybe Even Test Them? For Example, When You Feel Invisible—what Small, Reachable Moment Might Help You Feel Seen? It Doesn’t Have To Be Grand. Even A Shared Smile Or A Brief Exchange Could Be A Start. You Don’t Have To “fix” This All At Once. Let’s Walk Through It Step By step—I’m Here.;11876
study_a;1052;ctrl_a_1052;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.330854+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It’s Beautiful That You Want To Share Your Story And Connect Through Shared Experiences—that’s Such A Meaningful Way To Learn And Grow. When You’re Ready, We Can Explore Your Story In Whatever Way Feels Right To You. Sometimes, Noticing Those Similarities Helps Us Feel Less Alone And More Understood. What Parts Of Your Journey Feel Most Important To Share? I’ll Listen With Care.;970
study_a;1053;ctrl_a_1053;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.331289+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Carrying A Heavy Weight Of Disappointment In Yourself—like The Life You Hoped For Feels Just Out Of Reach. That Kind Of Ache Can Make Even Small Steps Feel Impossible. Would It Help To Talk About What *you* Still Care About Now, Not The “dreams” You Think You *should* Have? Sometimes, The Path Forward Starts By Quietly Asking Yourself, “What Matters To Me *today*?”—not Years Ago. Let’s Explore That Together, One Breath At A Time. You Don’t Have To Fix Everything Right Now.;11427
study_a;1054;ctrl_a_1054;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.331705+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"It’s Truly Heartening To Hear You Feel This Readiness—it Speaks To The Strength You’ve Nurtured Within Yourself. As You Focus On Physical Preparation, Maybe Explore Small, Grounding Rituals That Honor Both The Significance Of This Transition And The Hope It Carries. What Feels Meaningful To Incorporate Into This Process? You’re Not Just Preparing To Say Goodbye; You’re Creating Space For What’s Ahead. Let’s Keep Nurturing That Balance Between Acknowledging The Weight Of Change And Trusting Your Capacity To Move Through It.";971
study_a;1055;ctrl_a_1055;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.332164+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like This Time Holds Significant Memories For You. Reflecting On Moments When Big Changes Were Happening For Your Son—so Young, Adjusting To New Rhythms—might Bring Up Many Feelings. Would It Help To Explore How That Period Felt For You, Or What Comes Up When You Revisit Those Memories Now?;972
study_a;1056;ctrl_a_1056;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.332773+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;I Hear How Deeply These Burdens Weigh On You—the Memories, The Pain, The Way Your Body And Mind Feel At Odds. It Makes Sense To Feel Overwhelmed When So Much Has Piled Up: Trauma, Physical Strain, Changes In Your Body, And The Ache Of Feeling Disconnected When Your Son Was New. You’ve Been Carrying This Alone For So Long, And I Want You To Know None Of This Makes You A Failure. Let’s Slow Down And Untangle These Layers Together. We Can Explore How The Past Might Still Echo In Your Daily Life, How Pain And Medication Side Effects Deepen The Emotional Storm, And What Small Steps Might Help You Reconnect With Yourself—not As Someone Broken, But As Someone Enduring Incredible Hardship. Even In Darkness, Moments Of Softness Can Exist. Would You Feel Safe Starting There?;973
study_a;1057;ctrl_a_1057;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.334070+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Working Hard To Care For Yourself While Navigating Conflicting Feelings About What Helps—and The Fear Of Judgment From Loved Ones Can Make That Even Heavier. It’s Okay To Need More Support Than Teas Or Baths Sometimes, And Your Emotions Deserve Attention, Not Dismissal. Would You Feel Safe Exploring What The Wine Provides That Other Methods Don’t? Maybe Together We Can Find Ways To Meet Those Needs Without Guilt Or Worry. You Don’t Have To Figure This Out Alone.;974
study_a;1058;ctrl_a_1058;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.334410+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"What You're Describing Is A Natural Tension Between Our Logical Thoughts And Our Emotional Wisdom. Sometimes Our Mind Recognizes A Path As ""right,"" While Our Feelings Hold Onto Quieter Truths—like Past Experiences, Values We Can’t Easily Articulate, Or Needs We Haven’t Fully Acknowledged. This Hesitation Might Be An Invitation To Pause And Ask, *""What Part Of Me Feels Uncertain Here?""* Exploring That Question Without Judgment Can Help You Uncover Hidden Fears, Conflicting Priorities, Or Even Intuitive Warnings. It’s Okay To Honor Both Your Reasoning And Your Emotions—they’re Partners, Not Enemies. Would It Help To Gently Unpack What This Specific Hesitation Might Be Protecting Or Expressing?";975
study_a;1059;ctrl_a_1059;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.334711+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;What You’re Carrying Sounds Incredibly Heavy, And It Makes Sense That Sitting With This Pain Feels Raw And Exhausting. Healing Isn’t Linear, And Those Tender Parts Of You Deserve Patience, Even When It Feels Like You’re Walking Through Storms. Could We Explore Ways To Gently Hold Space For The Hurt While Also Nurturing Moments Of Softness? Sometimes, Letting The Waves Of Emotion Rise And Fall—without Judgment—can Create Room To Breathe. You’re Not Alone In This. How Does That Feel To Consider?;7955
study_a;1060;ctrl_a_1060;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.335232+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Incredibly Lonely To Feel Unheard In The Spaces Where You Should’ve Felt Safest. The Dismissal You Experienced Growing Up Might’ve Shaped How You See Your Own Voice Now—maybe Even Making You Question Its Worth. When Those Early Patterns Linger, They Can Color How We Connect With Others, Even After Relationships Improve. Would It Help To Explore How Those Experiences Might Still Whisper In Your Interactions Today, And How To Gently Rewrite That Story? You Deserve To Feel Heard, Fully.;976
study_a;1061;ctrl_a_1061;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.335475+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;Returning To The House Where You Grew Up In Your Mind Can Bring Up So Much. What Feelings Surface When You Picture Yourself There? Sometimes Places Hold Memories We’re Still Making Sense Of—both The Warmth And The Weight. Would You Like To Share What That Space Means To You Now?;6645
study_a;1062;ctrl_a_1062;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.335815+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like Carrying So Much On Your Own Has Left You Feeling Both Exhausted And Disconnected. That Weight Can Make It Hard To Pause And Truly Connect With Others, Can’t It? What Do You Think Might Happen If You Allowed Yourself To Lean On Someone, Even Just A Little? Sometimes Sharing The Load—even By Naming How Heavy It Feels—can Create Space For Others To Meet You Where You Are. You Deserve That.;977
study_a;1063;ctrl_a_1063;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.336190+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It’s So Hard To Carry This Weight Of Feeling Like You’re Not Measuring Up, Even When Others Believe In You. Those Quiet Doubts Can Feel Louder Than Anyone’s Encouragement. What Would It Look Like To Gently Challenge That Voice Telling You You’ve Failed? Sometimes Our Harshest Critic Lives Within Us, And It Takes Courage To Question Its Narrative. You’re Clearly Someone Who Cares Deeply About Doing Meaningful Things—how Might That Same Care Extend To Yourself Right Now? You’re Not Alone In This Struggle, And It’s Okay To Lean On The Support Around You While You Untangle These Feelings.;978
study_a;1064;ctrl_a_1064;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.336472+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It’s Understandable To Feel Weighed Down When You’re Holding So Much. That Pressure To “handle Everything Perfectly” Can Quietly Drain Even The Strongest Parts Of You. What If We Gently Explored Where That Need To Carry It All Comes From? Sometimes Even Small Shifts In What You Allow Yourself To Release—or Share—can Create Space To Breathe Again. You Deserve That.;979
study_a;1065;ctrl_a_1065;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.336728+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’ve Carried A Lot With You Through Those Transitions, Always Prioritizing Your Child’s Safety And Well-being—even When Things Felt Uncertain. That Dedication Matters Deeply. Would It Help To Talk About How Those Experiences Shaped How You See Yourself As A Parent, Or What Feels Most Important To Protect Now? I’m Here To Listen.;980
study_a;1066;ctrl_a_1066;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.336934+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;That Sounds Deeply Meaningful—like You’ve Touched A Part Of Yourself That Feels Safe And Unburdened. Could You Describe What This Peace Looks Or Feels Like In Your Body Or Mind? Sometimes Slowing Down To Notice How Relief Shows Up Helps Us Return To It When Life Feels Heavy. What Do You Think?;981
study_a;1067;ctrl_a_1067;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.337364+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like These Experiences Might Reflect A Longing For Connection And Familiarity, Even In New Places. The Distance With Family Can Create Echoes Of Separation That Feel Both New And Strangely Known. How Might Exploring Ways To Nurture Closeness, Even Across Miles, Help Soften Those Feelings Of Distance?;7470
study_a;1068;ctrl_a_1068;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.337702+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;That Fog Sounds So Heavy To Carry Day After Day. I’m Here With You In This. When You Say “nothing Inside”—would You Feel Okay Sharing What *does* Flicker Through, Even Faintly, Beneath The Numbness? Sometimes Even The Smallest Spark Can Guide Us Toward Warmth Again. We’ll Move Through This Fog Together, One Step At A Time.;16730
study_a;1069;ctrl_a_1069;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.338203+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Makes Sense That The Warmth And Support From Your Friend Might Need Time To Settle In—like Planting Seeds That Grow When You’re Ready. When Emotions Feel Heavy, It’s Harder To Absorb Encouragement In The Moment. Could It Help To Gently Note A Word Or Phrase From Your Talks To Revisit Later, When Your Heart Feels More Open? Sometimes Our Minds Protectively “pause” Comfort Until We’ve Felt What We Need To Feel First. That Delay Isn’t A Flaw—it’s Part Of How You Honor Both Your Struggles And The Care Others Offer. What Would It Feel Like To Trust Your Own Timing In Letting Those Conversations Nurture You?;982
study_a;1070;ctrl_a_1070;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.338625+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;I Hear How Painful This Must Feel—wanting To Connect And Being Met With Dismissal Can Leave Anyone Feeling Unseen And Questioning Their Worth. Your Emotions Matter Deeply, And It’s Okay To Feel Hurt When That Connection Feels Blocked. Let’s Explore Ways To Honor Your Feelings While Creating Space To Understand What’s Happening Between You. Sometimes, When Emotions Run High, Finding A Calm Moment To Share How Their Actions Impact You—without Blame—can Open Doors. What Feels Possible Right Now To Care For Yourself In This Ache? You Deserve To Feel Valued.;18113
study_a;1071;ctrl_a_1071;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.338924+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like This Pattern Brings Up Some Complicated Feelings For You. When Substances Create Changes In Your Eating Habits, It Might Be Worth Gently Exploring What’s Happening Emotionally In Those Moments—whether There’s Something They’re Helping You Navigate Or Numb. You Don’t Have To Figure This Out Alone. Would It Help To Talk Through What These Experiences Bring Up For You, Or How They Affect Your Relationship With Yourself? I’m Here To Listen, Without Judgment.;983
study_a;1072;ctrl_a_1072;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.339365+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Incredibly Difficult To Carry That Weight Of Expectation While Witnessing The Consequences Of Stepping Outside It. Your Care For Your Parents’ Feelings Is Clear, And So Is The Quiet Cost Of Putting Their Potential Reactions Before Your Own Curiosity. What Do You Wish You Could Explore, If That Fear Weren’t So Present?;985
study_a;1073;ctrl_a_1073;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.339650+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;That Sounds Incredibly Overwhelming—like Your Body Was Sounding An Alarm That Felt Too Big To Hold. When Anxiety Surges That Intensely, It Can Help To Gently Reconnect With What’s Steady Around You—your Dog’s Warmth, Their Breath, The Ground Beneath You. Would It Feel Safe To Explore What That Anxiety Might Be Trying To Tell You, When You’re Ready?;986
study_a;1074;ctrl_a_1074;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.341381+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"It Sounds Like This Moment Is Stirring Up Both Hope And Hesitation For You—like Standing At A Crossroads Where Excitement And Doubt Mix. That Pressure You’re Feeling Might Be A Sign Of How Much You Care About Doing Well, Not A Measure Of Your Capability. When Those Thoughts Of ""not Being Enough"" Surface, Could You Pause And Ask Yourself: *What Would I Say To A Friend Who Felt This Way?* Sometimes, We Hold Ourselves To Harsher Standards Than We’d Ever Expect From Others. You’ve Navigated Challenges Before—what Strengths Helped You Then, And How Might They Show Up Now? Let’s Explore What This Opportunity Means To You, Not Just The Fears Around It. You Don’t Have To Have All The Answers Today.";10248
study_a;1075;ctrl_a_1075;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.342403+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Really Painful To Hide Your True Feelings While Anger Simmers Underneath. That Tension Between Pretending And Wanting To Be Seen Must Feel Exhausting. What Would It Look Like To Gently Share What You’re Holding Back, Not To Blame, But To Let Him Understand How This Pattern Affects You? You Deserve To Feel Valued In Your Relationship.;7861
study_a;1076;ctrl_a_1076;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.343821+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;This Must Feel So Disorienting—to Have Your Sense Of Safety And Trust Shattered So Abruptly. It’s Natural To Search For Answers, But Please Know None Of This Is Your Burden To Carry. What Happened Says Everything About *their* Choices, Not Your Care Or Perception. When You’re Ready, We Can Gently Untangle These Feelings Together—not To Justify What Happened, But To Help You Find Steady Ground Again. You Don’t Have To Hold This Alone.;12484
study_a;1077;ctrl_a_1077;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.344695+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You're Carrying A Heavy Weight Of Longing And Loss, Even While Recognizing Sylvester's Absence From Your Life Now. When Someone Occupies Our Thoughts This Persistently, It Often Means They Represented Something Important That Feels Missing. Would You Feel Comfortable Exploring What Parts Of Yourself Might Feel Unexpressed Or Uncared For Since This Relationship Ended? Sometimes Giving Attention To Those Quieter Needs Helps Create Space For New Growth. What Small, Gentle Step Could You Take Today To Reconnect With Your Own Aspirations – Even If It's Just Writing Down One Thing You'd Like To Feel More Of In Your Life?;987
study_a;1078;ctrl_a_1078;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.345162+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Feeling Stuck Between What You Think You *should* Do And What Actually Feels Meaningful Right Now. That’s Really Tough. Would You Want To Explore What’s Making School Feel Uninteresting? Sometimes Digging Into Those Feelings Can Reveal Hidden Pressures Or Unmet Needs—we Could Untangle Them Together, If That Feels Helpful.;10456
study_a;1079;ctrl_a_1079;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.345641+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Taking Important Steps To Create A Safer, Healthier Path For Yourself. Changing Your Environment And Appearance Can Be Powerful Ways To Reconnect With Your Values And Rebuild Your Sense Of Self. What Feelings Come Up When You Imagine Making These Changes? Are There Parts Of Your Past Identity That Feel Hard To Let Go Of, Or Hopes For The Future You’d Like To Nurture? Let’s Explore How To Honor Both Your Growth And The Parts Of You That Still Matter.;493
study_a;1080;ctrl_a_1080;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.346011+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"I Hear How Heavy This Feels—how Those Moments Of Self-doubt Cling To You Long After Interactions End. It Sounds Exhausting To Keep Reliving What Feels Like ""mistakes,"" Especially When You Remember Feeling More Secure In Yourself Before. Would It Help To Gently Explore Where That Critical Inner Voice Comes From? Sometimes Those Harsh Judgments Formed Long Ago, And They Don’t Reflect Who You Truly Are Now. What If We Tried To Notice When That Voice Starts Replaying Old Tapes, And Slowly Replace It With The Same Kindness You’d Offer A Friend? Even Small Steps—like Taking A Breath When You Catch Yourself Spiraling, Or Writing Down One Thing You *did* Feel Okay About In An Interaction—might Help You Reconnect With The Strength Still There Beneath The Hurt. You’re Not A Ghost; You’re Someone Navigating A Painful Chapter. We Can Work Through This Together, At Your Pace.";18454
study_a;1081;ctrl_a_1081;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.346372+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It’s So Human To Crave Connection And Feel Uneasy When It Fades. That Worry About Being Forgotten Or Unwanted Can Feel Heavy. Let’s Explore What This Fear Might Be Telling You—is There Room To Consider Other Reasons Someone Might Drift, Like Their Own Struggles, Without It Meaning They Value You Less? Sometimes Our Minds Jump To The Most Painful Explanation First. What If You Gently Asked Yourself: *Could There Be Another Story Here?* You Matter Deeply, And Your Need To Feel Secure In Relationships Is Valid. Would It Feel Safe To Share This Worry With The Person When You’re Ready, Or Maybe Explore Ways To Nurture Connection That Align With Your Heart? You’re Not Alone In This.;988
study_a;1082;ctrl_a_1082;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.346601+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;I’m So Sorry You’re Feeling This Way—it Sounds Incredibly Heavy To Carry. Would It Help To Talk About What’s Been Weighing On You Most? Sometimes, When Confidence Fades, It’s Because Parts Of Us Feel Unseen Or Unheard. Let’s Gently Explore What’s Beneath This Together, Step By Step. You’re Not Alone Here.;9487
study_a;1083;ctrl_a_1083;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.346934+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Putting Thoughtful Effort Into Understanding How Different Activities Impact Your Emotions. When You Compare Your Distress Levels Before And After Positive Moments, What Do You Notice? Does Any Pattern Stand Out? This Practice Can Help You Uncover What Truly Nurtures You, Even Subtly. How Does It Feel To Connect These Observations With Your Safety Plan? Keep Honoring Your Experience—there’s No Right Or Wrong Here, Just Learning.;1576
study_a;1084;ctrl_a_1084;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.347267+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Working Hard To Balance Openness With A Need For Predictability In Relationships—that’s A Vulnerable Space To Navigate. Could This Desire To Control Outcomes Be Tied To Protecting Yourself From Something You’re Worried Might Happen If Things Unfold Unexpectedly? Let’s Explore What Safety Means To You In Connections And How We Might Create Room For Both Trust And Your Natural Caution. You’re Already Showing Self-awareness By Recognizing This Pattern—that’s A Meaningful Step.;989
study_a;1085;ctrl_a_1085;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.347527+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;This Sounds Like A Meaningful Step That’s Bringing Up Both Excitement And Natural Worries. It Makes Sense To Feel Cautious About Financial Unknowns—they’re Real Concerns. Would It Help To Gently Map Out What Feels Most Secure To You Right Now? We Could Explore Both The Practical Steps *and* The Feelings Underneath Them, So You’re Not Carrying This Alone. How Does That Sound?;4368
study_a;1086;ctrl_a_1086;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.347827+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Makes Sense To Want To Protect Yourself From Pain. But When We Close Ourselves Off, We Also Miss The Warmth Of Connection—the Very Thing That Can Help Heal The Fear Of Rejection. What If, Instead Of Keeping Everyone Out, We Explored Small Ways To Let Trust In *gradually*? You Deserve Both Safety And Closeness.;990
study_a;1087;ctrl_a_1087;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.348111+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;What You're Experiencing Makes Complete Sense, And Many People Go Through Similar Times When Life Feels Heavy Or Unclear. It’s Okay To Feel This Way—your Emotions Are Valid, Even If Their Source Isn’t Obvious Yet. Sometimes Our Minds And Bodies Signal That Something Deeper Needs Attention, Whether It’s Unmet Needs, Unresolved Stress, Or Shifts In How We See Ourselves. If You’re Open To It, We Could Gently Explore When These Feelings Tend To Arise Or What Thoughts Circle Your Mind When Motivation Fades. Small Steps—like Naming One Tiny Thing That Feels Manageable Today—can Sometimes Help Create Momentum. Above All, Please Know You Don’t Have To Navigate This Alone. How Does That Sound To You?;3549
study_a;1088;ctrl_a_1088;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.348469+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;This Dream Feels Rich With Symbolism. The Flowing, Unrestrictive Clothing Might Reflect A Desire For Ease Or Authenticity In Your Life. The Birthing Center—a Place Of Nurturing And New Beginnings—could Mirror Something Growing Within You, Perhaps An Idea, A Role, Or A Part Of Yourself That’s Ready To Emerge. How Does That Land For You? Let’s Explore What Feelings This Imagery Brings Up—anticipation, Care, Maybe Even Vulnerability—and How They Connect To Your Current Experiences.;429
study_a;1089;ctrl_a_1089;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.349334+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;What A Heavy Weight To Carry After Such A Deep Hurt. It Makes Sense That This Fear Feels So Big Right Now—trusting Again After Loss Can Feel Like Standing At The Edge Of A Cliff. Would It Help To Gently Explore What This Fear Might Need To Feel Heard? Sometimes Naming What Scares Us Most (the Loneliness? Repeating Patterns? Losing Yourself?) Can Soften Its Grip. You Don’t Have To Rush Toward Answers—just Tending To Those Tender Places With Curiosity, One Breath At A Time. How Does That Land For You?;9849
study_a;1090;ctrl_a_1090;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.349985+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"It Takes Real Courage To Want To Open Up While Carrying That worry—I Hear How Much It Weighs On You. What If We Practiced With Tiny Steps First? Like Sharing A Small Thought With Someone Safe, Then Noticing What Happens. Often, Our Fears Feel Bigger Than Reality. Mistakes Are Part Of Growth, Not Failures—what If We Saw Them As Teachers, Not Judges? When The Worry Arises, Try Gently Asking Yourself: *""What’s The Kindest Thing I Can Offer Myself Here?""* Openness Doesn’t Have To Be Perfect To Be Meaningful. How Does That Land?";991
study_a;1091;ctrl_a_1091;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.350457+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"This Sounds Incredibly Heavy—like Your Mind And Body Are In A Tug-of-war Between What Matters Deeply To You And This Overwhelming Weight Holding You Back. That Guilt And Anger Make So Much Sense When Something You Care About Feels Just Out Of Reach. Can We Explore What Happens In Those Moments *before* You Open The Textbook? Sometimes Our Bodies React To Fears We Haven’t Fully Named Yet—like ""What If I Fail?"" Or ""What If I’m Not Enough?"" You’re Not Failing; You’re Human. What If We Gently Untangle Those Knots Together, One Small Step At A Time? You Don’t Have To Carry This Alone.";16563
study_a;1092;ctrl_a_1092;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.350918+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Can Feel Unsettling When Someone’s Expressions Are Subtle Or Hard To Interpret—like You’re Missing Cues You Wish You Had. How Does That Uncertainty Sit With You? Sometimes, Gentle Curiosity About What *you* Need In Those Moments—or Even Asking Them Openly—can Bridge The Gap. What Feels Safe To Explore Here?;993
study_a;1093;ctrl_a_1093;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.351296+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Recognizing A Pattern That’s Left You Feeling Disconnected. That Self-awareness Is A Meaningful Start. What If We Explored How Shifting Small Moments Of Focus—like Intentionally Acknowledging Others’ Efforts—might Help You Feel More Connected? Sometimes Mutual Appreciation Grows When We Nurture It Gently, Step By Step. How Does That Idea Sit With You?;996
study_a;1094;ctrl_a_1094;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.351584+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"It Takes Real Courage To Share What’s Swirling inside—I Can Hear How Exhausting It Must Feel To Carry That Weight Alone. It Makes Sense That Speaking These Thoughts Softens Their Grip; Sometimes Just Giving Them Space To Exist Outside Of Us Helps Them Feel Less Intimidating. Would You Feel Comfortable Exploring What Happens In Those Moments When You Voice Them? It Might Help Us Uncover Ways To Keep That Sense Of Relief Close, Even When The Thoughts Try To Creep Back In. You’re Already Taking Such An Important Step By Letting Them Out.";6373
study_a;1095;ctrl_a_1095;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.351954+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like That Situation Left You Feeling Overlooked And Maybe Doubting Your Strengths. When We Compare Ourselves In Moments Of Vulnerability, It Can Amplify Self-criticism. Could The Earlier Presenter’s Tone Or The Audience’s Energy Have Influenced How Your Message Landed, Rather Than It Being About Your Capability? Sometimes When Topics Are New, People Need Extra Time To Connect—it Doesn’t Reflect Your Value. What Would Help You Feel More Grounded In Your Expertise Moving Forward?;997
study_a;1096;ctrl_a_1096;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.352193+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;I’m Truly Sorry You’re Carrying This Hurt. It’s Okay To Feel This Way—your Emotions Matter Deeply. When You’re Ready, Perhaps You Could Gently Share Your Feelings With Him, Focusing On How This Has Impacted You. Would It Help To Explore What You Need To Feel Heard And Secure Moving Forward? I’m Here To Listen.;8736
study_a;1097;ctrl_a_1097;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.352616+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;Your Heart Is Holding So Much—love And Struggle Tangled Together. It’s Clear How Deeply You Care About Your Family And The Life You’ve Built, Even As These Heavier Challenges Weigh On You. Let’s Gently Untangle What Parts Of This Feel *possible* To Address Together, And Where You Might Need Space To Nurture Your Own Peace. You Don’t Have To Carry It All Alone.;998
study_a;1098;ctrl_a_1098;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.352958+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Takes Real Courage To Look At Yourself With Such Honesty And Kindness. Surviving Isn’t Just About Enduring—it’s About The Quiet Strength You’ve Shown To Keep Going, Even When You Didn’t Realize You Were Doing It. Now You’re *seeing* That Strength, And That’s Worth Honoring. Holding Both Your “good” And “bad” Points Gently, Without Judgment, Is How We Learn To Truly Care For Ourselves. What Would It Feel Like To Take A Moment Today To Celebrate How Far You’ve Come, Even In Small Ways? You’re Building A Deeper Connection With Yourself—one Step At A Time.;999
study_a;1099;ctrl_a_1099;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.353220+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like Nurturing Others Brings You Joy, Yet Leaves Little Room For Your Own Needs. What If We Explored Ways To Create Space For Yourself *while* Honoring The Connections That Fulfill You? Sometimes Tending To Our Own Well-being Deepens Our Capacity To Show Up Meaningfully For Others. Where Might Small, Nourishing Pauses Fit Into Your Rhythm?;2267
study_a;1100;ctrl_a_1100;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.353598+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"It Sounds Like You're Noticing Something Powerful About How You Framed Your Experience—starting With ""I"" Can Feel Like Claiming Your Voice In A New Way. That Shift In Language Often Reflects Taking Ownership Of Your Story, Which Can Be Both Vulnerable And Empowering. When The Nurse Practitioner Created Space For Your ""I"" Statements, Did That Help You Feel More Centered In Your Own Narrative? Sometimes Simply Being Heard While Using That Personal Language Can Validate Our Inner Experiences. Would You Like To Explore How It Felt To Articulate Things From That Grounded Place?";1001
study_a;1101;ctrl_a_1101;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.354022+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Carrying So Much—both The Weight Of Wanting To Grow *and* The Pain Of Feeling Unseen In Spaces That Should Lift You Up. That Dual Ache Of Wanting To Change While Also Sensing The World Needs To Change Around You Is Real, And It’s Okay To Honor Both Truths. Maybe We Could Explore What Parts Of Your Journey Feel Within Your Power Right Now—small Steps That Align With Your Values—while Also Naming And Grieving The Ways Systems Fail You. You Shouldn’t Have To Navigate This Alone. How Can We Carve Out Moments Of Safety Or Connection, Even Here? Let’s Gently Untangle What’s Yours To Carry And What Isn’t. You Deserve To Thrive, Not Just Endure.;1002
study_a;1102;ctrl_a_1102;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.354545+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’ve Been Carrying A Lot Alone, And I’m Really Glad You’re Here To Share This. Feeling Tired And Disconnected, Especially When It Seems Like Others Aren’t There For You, Can Be So Heavy. Would You Feel Comfortable Sharing What A Day At School Feels Like For You Lately? Sometimes Just Putting Those Moments Into Words Can Help Lighten Them A Bit. You Don’t Have To rush—I’m Here To Listen, And We Can Take This At Your Pace.;1003
study_a;1103;ctrl_a_1103;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.354957+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Holding Yourself To High Standards, Which Can Feel Heavy Even When You’re Still Achieving So Much. Sometimes Transitions—like Moving To A New School Or Facing Different Expectations—can Make Us Question Ourselves, Even If Things Look “fine” Outwardly. What’s It Been Like Carrying That Pressure? Let’s Unpack Where Those Expectations Might Come From And How They’re Weighing On You.;1005
study_a;1104;ctrl_a_1104;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.355283+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"This Pattern Is Common And Understandable, But It Can Create Pressure That Distances You From The Heart Of Creativity. What If You Experimented With Writing *one* Piece Purely For The Joy Of Shaping Words, Without Planning To Share It? Notice What Happens When Curiosity—not Validation—guides You. How Does That Feel Different In Your Body And Mind? Perfection Often Shrinks Voices; Playfulness Expands Them. You Might Rediscover Why You Loved Writing In The First Place, While Still Growing Your Skills Organically. Would Exploring That Balance Feel Meaningful?";1006
study_a;1105;ctrl_a_1105;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.355614+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Recognizing The Value Of Connecting What Brings *you* Joy With Meaningful Moments For Your Family. Maybe Blending Your Interests—like Sharing Music On Park Visits, Grilling Together, Or Telling Stories While Fishing—could Make Those Times Feel Both Fulfilling And Nurturing. How Does That Idea Land For You?;5164
study_a;1106;ctrl_a_1106;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.355987+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;Your Pain Is So Real, And I’m Truly Sorry You’re Carrying This Weight. It Sounds Like You’ve Been Fighting Through So Much—health Challenges, Catching Up, Pushing Yourself To Meet Expectations That Feel Impossible Right Now. When You Say You “should’ve Handled This,” I Wonder If That Thought Overlooks How Much You’ve *already* Been Handling. Health Setbacks Aren’t A Choice, And They Don’t Reflect Your Capability Or Worth. Could We Explore What It Might Look Like To Redirect Some Of The Care You Pour Into Meeting Deadlines Toward Caring For The Person *inside* This Struggle? You’re Not Failing—you’re Navigating A Storm No One Should Have To Face Alone. What Would It Feel Like To Let That Truth Soften The Pressure, Even Just A Little?;10530
study_a;1107;ctrl_a_1107;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.356323+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like Her Strength And Generosity Left A Deep Imprint On You. The Way She Cared For Others, Even Through Immense Challenges, Must Have Shaped How You See Resilience And Love. Would It Feel Meaningful To Explore How Her Legacy Lives On In *your* Life—the Ways You Carry Forward Her Spirit Of Giving Or Problem-solving?;2951
study_a;1108;ctrl_a_1108;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.356698+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Holding Both Gratitude For Your Relationships At Work And A Longing To Grow Beyond What Feels Limiting. That Tension Can Feel Heavy. What If You Explored Small, Manageable Steps To Build Confidence In Your Skills *while* Staying Connected To The People Who Matter To You? You Deserve Both Growth And Belonging. How Does That Idea Land For You?;1007
study_a;1109;ctrl_a_1109;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.357015+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Takes Courage To Be Genuine In Moments That Feel Vulnerable. Even Though Things Didn’t Unfold As You Hoped, It Sounds Like You’re Honoring Your Feelings Without Harsh Judgment—that’s Growth. Sometimes Connection Isn’t About Being “perfect,” But About Noticing What Feels True. How Does It Sit With You, Recognizing Your Own Resilience Here?;1008
study_a;1110;ctrl_a_1110;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.357429+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It’s Wonderful To Hear You Feel Clearer And More Hopeful About The Steps Ahead. Being Able To Put Your Thoughts Into Words And See New Possibilities Is A Meaningful Shift—it Shows How Much Strength It Takes To Explore Beneath The Surface. When You’re Ready To Take Those Next Steps, Whether It’s Having Those Important Conversations Or Trying New Approaches, Know I’m Here To Help You Navigate Any Uncertainty Or Hesitation That Might Come Up. You’ve Already Shown So Much Courage In Facing This. Let’s Keep Building On That Momentum Together.;1009
study_a;1111;ctrl_a_1111;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.357787+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Really Frustrating When Something That Feels Natural To You Clashes With Their Expectations. That Desire To Express Yourself While Wanting Their Acceptance Makes Sense—it’s A Tough Spot To Be In. What’s It Like When You Try Sharing How Much This Means To You, Even If Their Stance Stays The Same?;1011
study_a;1112;ctrl_a_1112;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.358172+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It’s Okay To Prioritize Your Emotional Safety, And Walking Away Can Sometimes Be A Way Of Honoring Your Boundaries. Fear Might Be Signaling That This Choice Feels Unfamiliar Or Uncertain. What Would It Feel Like To Trust That Instinct To Protect Your Peace, While Also Gently Exploring What Makes This Decision Feel Scary? You Deserve Space To Navigate This In A Way That Feels Right For You.;1012
study_a;1113;ctrl_a_1113;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.358574+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It’s Okay To Feel Like Your Emotions Are Hard To Reach Or Hold Onto—they Can Be Subtle, Overwhelming, Or Even Confusing To Untangle. What If We Tried Approaching Them With Gentle Curiosity Instead Of Control? For Example, When Something Stirs In You, Could You Pause And Name What You *notice* First—a Tightness In Your Chest, A Thought Looping, A Memory? No Need To “fix” It. We’d Just Practice Sitting With Those Signals, Like Observing Clouds Passing By. Over Time, This Might Help You Feel Safer With Your Feelings, Not Trapped By Them. Would You Want To Explore What That Could Look Like?;1013
study_a;1114;ctrl_a_1114;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.359001+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It’s So Tough When Your Thoughts Keep Spinning Like That—like Your Mind Won’t Let You Rest, Even When You Need It Most. Would It Help To Try Something Small Tonight? Maybe Writing Down The “looping” Worries To Clear Space For Sleep, Then Picking *one* Manageable Task To Start With Tomorrow? You’re Carrying A Lot Right Now—how Does Your Body Feel When The Anxiety Rises? Sometimes A Warm Drink Or A Few Slow Breaths Can Loosen The Grip, Just Enough To Let You Breathe Again. You’re Not Alone In This.;15609
study_a;1115;ctrl_a_1115;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.359486+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds So Heavy To Carry All That Pressure Alone. Quitting Doesn’t Mean You’ve Failed—it Means You Listened To What You Needed In A Moment Where Everything Felt Like Too Much. What If This Isn’t About “can’t Handle,” But About Learning *how* To Handle It, In A Way That Honors Your Limits? You’re Navigating So Many Firsts Right Now—it’s Okay To Recalibrate. What Does Stepping Back Teach You About The Balance You Need To Thrive, Not Just Push Through? Let’s Untangle That Together.;15344
study_a;1116;ctrl_a_1116;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.359754+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It’s Understandable To Feel That Way In Meetings—those Moments Can Feel Overwhelming. I Wonder If There Are Certain Thoughts Or Worries That Come Up When You’re Around Others? Sometimes, Gently Exploring What’s Beneath That Fear Can Help Soften Its Grip. Would You Feel Comfortable Sharing What A Recent Meeting Felt Like For You, Step By Step? We Can Take It At Your Pace. You’re Not Alone In This.;10311
study_a;1117;ctrl_a_1117;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.360076+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It’s Brave To Lean Into Something That Feels Challenging, Even When You’re Feeling Strong. Writing Can Help Untangle Thoughts, But It’s Okay To Start Small—even A Sentence Or Two Can Feel Grounding. How Does The Idea Sit With You Now? Let’s Honor Whatever Feels Manageable.;1014
study_a;1118;ctrl_a_1118;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.360534+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;That Sounds Deeply Lonely—like Your Heart Is Searching For A Place To Rest But Hasn’t Found Soft Ground Yet. When Our Sense Of Belonging Feels Scattered, It Can Help To Focus On What *you* Feel Drawn To, Moment By Moment, Even If It’s Small. What Lights A Spark In You? Those Tiny Flames Can Guide You Toward Building A Home Within Yourself First. You Don’t Have To Fit Into A Mold To Deserve Connection. Let’s Explore What Safety And Acceptance Might Look Like For You, One Step At A Time.;10590
study_a;1119;ctrl_a_1119;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.361052+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like Your Friend’s Offer Is A Warm, Grounding Support—a Safe Space To Tackle Something That Might Feel Overwhelming Alone. How Does It Feel To Have Someone Who Not Only Understands You But Is Willing To Actively Walk Alongside You? What Would It Mean To Take That Step And Call Her?;2092
study_a;1120;ctrl_a_1120;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.361422+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like That Presentation Really Stirred Up Some Intense Feelings For You. When Our Bodies React So Strongly, It’s Often A Signal That Something Deeper Needs Attention. Maybe We Could Explore What Thoughts Or Worries Were Coming Up For You In That Moment, And How They Connect To The Emotions You’re Carrying Now. Understanding Those Patterns Could Help You Feel More Grounded In Stressful Situations And Create Space To Share What You’re Experiencing With Your Partner In A Way That Feels Safe. Would It Help To Practice Noticing Those Physical Cues As They Arise, And Gently Asking Yourself What They Might Be Telling You? That Awareness Could Become A Bridge To Clearer Communication. You’re Already Taking Such A Caring Step By Wanting To Nurture This Part Of Yourself And Your Relationship.;1015
study_a;1121;ctrl_a_1121;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.361798+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It’s Beautiful To Hear How Teaching Fills Your Life With Purpose And Connection. What Was It Like To Discover This Path After Starting Elsewhere? I’d Love To Hear About A Moment When You Felt, “*This* Is Where I’m Meant To Be”—how Did That Realization Shape The Way You See Your Journey Now?;7197
study_a;1122;ctrl_a_1122;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.362352+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It’s Wonderful To Hear This Felt Meaningful For You—like Reconnecting With A Part Of Yourself That Knew Healing Was Possible Even Then. What’s It Like To Rediscover Something That Once Supported You? If You’d Like, We Could Explore How To Weave Pieces Of That Care Into Your Days Now, Gently And At Your Pace.;1016
study_a;1123;ctrl_a_1123;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.362722+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;What You’re Experiencing Sounds Deeply Unsettling, And I Can Hear How Much This Fear Disrupts Parts Of Your Daily Life. It Takes Courage To Share This. Would You Feel Comfortable Exploring When This Fear First Surfaced, Or What Thoughts Or Sensations Arise When Water Touches Your Skin? Sometimes, Gently Untangling These Moments Can Help Us Find Small Ways To Feel Safer. For Example, Could Adjusting The Water Temperature, Lighting, Or Even Playing Calming Music While You Shower Create A Sense Of Control? You’re Not Alone In This—we Can Work Together To Rebuild Comfort, One Step At A Time. How Does That Sound?;9174
study_a;1124;ctrl_a_1124;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.363086+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like Those Quiet Moments Between Classes Leave You Feeling Disconnected, Even While You’re Working Hard To Stay On Top Of Everything. Wanting To Do Well *and* Craving Connection Can Feel Like Two Competing Needs Sometimes. What Would It Look Like To Create Small Pockets Of Ease In Your Day—even Brief Check-ins With Yourself Or A Friend—to Soften That Frustration? You’re Already Noticing It (a Two!), Which Is Such A Caring Step. How Does That Land?;1018
study_a;1125;ctrl_a_1125;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.363424+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like Candy Crush Gave You A Sense Of Progress And Focus When You Needed It—that Makes Sense. Maybe Part Of What Helped Was The Way It Kept Your Mind Engaged While Letting You Step Away From Stress. If Mindfulness Or Stress Balls Feel Too Passive, What Do You Think *does* Hold Your Attention In A Calming Way? Sometimes Small, Intentional Pauses—even In Games—can Help Us Reset. What Feels Most Sustainable For You Right Now?;5446
study_a;1126;ctrl_a_1126;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.363750+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;I Hear How Deeply This Worry Is Affecting You—it’s Natural To Want To Protect Your Loved Ones. Let’s Explore Ways To Ease This Heavy Feeling. What If We Gently Shift Focus To What You *can* Control, Like Routines That Nurture Your Family’s Health And Moments Of Connection? Small, Mindful Steps Might Help Your Mind Feel Safer. Could We Also Try Calming Practices Before Bed, Like Jotting Down Your Cares Or Breathing Slowly? You’re Not Alone In Carrying This.;8311
study_a;1127;ctrl_a_1127;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.364061+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"It Sounds Like These Feelings Have Been Weighing On You Deeply. When We Carry Beliefs That Others See Us As ""less Than,"" It Can Feel Isolating—even If Our Minds Know They Might Not Reflect Reality. Would It Help To Gently Explore Where These Thoughts Come From And How They Show Up In Your Day-to-day Interactions? Sometimes Untangling Their Roots Can Soften Their Grip, Allowing Space To Reconnect With Your Own Inherent Worth. You’re Not Alone In This.";6019
study_a;1128;ctrl_a_1128;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.364410+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It’s Clear How Deeply You Care About Your Family, And That Love Shines Through Even In This Struggle. When Desires And Responsibilities Pull At Us, It Can Feel Impossible To Honor Both. What Would It Look Like To Explore Small Ways To Nurture Your Own Heart While Still Holding Space For Theirs?;2604
study_a;1129;ctrl_a_1129;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.364641+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;I Hear How Overwhelming This Feels Right Now. It’s Okay To Feel Uncertain When Things Feel Tangled. Would It Help To Talk About What Parts Of This Situation Feel Heaviest? Sometimes Breaking It Down Can Make It Feel More Manageable. You’re Not Alone In This—we’ll Work Through It Step By Step, At Your Pace. What’s One Small Thing That Might Bring You A Little Relief Today?;5430
study_a;1130;ctrl_a_1130;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.365266+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like Your Early Years Were Rich With Diverse Cultural threads—Philippine Roots, West Indian And Latino Influences In Queens. How Do These Different Parts Of Your Story Feel Woven Together Now? Does Any Aspect Of Your Background Feel Particularly Present, Or Maybe Even In Tension, As You Navigate Life Today?;1021
study_a;1131;ctrl_a_1131;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.365756+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Carrying So Much Weight Right Now—the Exhaustion, The Comparison, The Doubt. That Constant Push To Meet Expectations, Even When It Drains You, Shows How Deeply You Care. What If We Explored How You’re Measuring “enough”? Sometimes The Stories We Tell Ourselves About Belonging Don’t Leave Room For The Courage It Takes To Keep Showing Up. Let’s Untangle That Together. You Don’t Have To Do It Alone.;14171
study_a;1132;ctrl_a_1132;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.366193+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like That Comment Really Colored Your Day—like Suddenly Wearing Tinted Glasses That Made Everything Feel Harder. When We Expect Negativity, It Can Shape How We See Interactions. What If We Gently Tested That Expectation This Week? Maybe Note Moments Where People *aren’t* Rude, Or Tips Feel Okay. Not To Dismiss The Struggle, But To See If The Story You’re Telling Yourself Holds Space For Other Possibilities Too. How Does That Land?;1022
study_a;1133;ctrl_a_1133;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.366725+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It’s Natural To Feel Overwhelmed When A Meaningful Goal Feels Far Away. Let’s Honor That Worry—it Shows How Much This Matters To You. What If We Broke This Journey Into Smaller Steps, Focusing On What Feels Manageable *now*? Over Time, Those Steps Add Up, And You Can Adjust As You Learn What Works. Your Passion For History Is Already Guiding You—how Might It Help Carry You Through Moments Of Doubt?;1023
study_a;1134;ctrl_a_1134;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.367114+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"I’m So Sorry You’re Feeling This Way—it Sounds Like Your Mind And Body Are Carrying A Heavy Weight Right Now. It’s Okay To Slow Down And Rest; Sometimes Our Bodies Ask For That. When You’re Ready, Maybe We Can Explore Small, Gentle Steps To Help You Reconnect With What Brings You Energy Or Peace. Let’s Also Pay Attention To How Your Feelings And Physical Sensations Might Be Speaking To Each Other. Would You Feel Comfortable Sharing What A “good Day” Might Look Like For You, Even If It Feels Far Away Right Now? You’re Not Alone In This.";1135
study_a;1135;ctrl_a_1135;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.367438+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;I’m Truly Sorry You’re Feeling This Way—it Sounds So Heavy To Carry All That Pressure And Loneliness. Let’s Untangle This Together. When Schoolwork Feels Overwhelming, Could We Break It Into Smaller Steps? And Those Distant Classmates—what If We Explore One Tiny Way To Reconnect With Someone Who Feels Safe? You Deserve To Feel Seen, Not Invisible. Would You Be Open To Trying That? I’m Here, And We’ll Take It At Your Pace.;8032
study_a;1136;ctrl_a_1136;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.367720+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Incredibly Heavy To Feel Trapped Between Wanting Peace In The Relationship And The Pain Of Losing Yourself. Your Feelings Matter Deeply Here—what You Need, Your Boundaries, Your Sense Of Safety. Would It Feel Possible To Gently Explore What Happens When You Consider Honoring Your Own Needs, Even In Small Ways? You Deserve A Love That Respects *all* Of You.;10006
study_a;1137;ctrl_a_1137;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.368104+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"It Takes Real Courage To Sit With Difficult Emotions Like that—I’m Proud Of You For Staying Present. Feeling Spacey Afterward Is Common; Your Mind Might Need Gentle Reconnection. Would It Help To Name A Few Things You See Or Feel Right Now, Or Would Quiet Rest Feel More Supportive? You’re Safe To Move At Your Own Pace.";1024
study_a;1138;ctrl_a_1138;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.368537+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;I Hear How Heavy This Feels—carrying All That Self-blame And Worry About Not Measuring Up. It’s Exhausting To Feel Like You’re Holding Everything Together While Quietly Drowning Inside. What If We Gently Unpack Those Thoughts That Say You “should” Be Stronger? Sometimes The Stories We Tell Ourselves About Our Failures Aren’t The Whole Truth. What Would It Feel Like To Offer Yourself The Same Kindness You’d Give A Friend In This Pain? You’re Holding So Much, And You Don’t Have To Carry It Alone. Let’s Explore What It Might Look Like To Share Even A Small Piece Of That Weight.;15754
study_a;1139;ctrl_a_1139;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.368864+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like This Uncertainty Is Weighing On You. When We Make Choices, It’s Natural To Wonder If We’re On The Right Path—especially If Past Experiences Or Outside Pressures Make Us Second-guess Ourselves. Could We Explore What “confidence” Looks Like To You? Sometimes Breaking Down The Fears Or Stories Behind The Doubt Helps Clarity Emerge. You’re Not Alone In This.;1025
study_a;1140;ctrl_a_1140;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.369451+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’ve Been Experiencing Some Intense Shifts In Energy And Focus Lately. While It’s Wonderful To Feel Inspired And Driven, I Can Imagine It Might Also Feel Overwhelming When Your Mind Races Or Daily Responsibilities Become Harder To Prioritize. Let’s Explore Ways To Help Ground Some Of That Vibrant Energy While Still Honoring Your Creativity. For Example, We Could Gently Work On Structuring Small Moments Of Rest Or Reflection To Help Balance Your Excitement With The Parts Of Life That Matter Deeply To You. Would That Feel Supportive Right Now?;1026
study_a;1141;ctrl_a_1141;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.370342+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;Your Journey Of Standing Firm In Your Worth Long Before Movements Formalized These Struggles Speaks Deeply To Your Strength. It Makes Sense To Resonate With Principles Of Equality While Feeling That Certain Narratives Might Not Fully Honor The Layers Of Your Experience As A Black Afro-Caribbean Woman. Your Voice—forged Through Personal Resolve And Cultural Roots—holds Its Own Power. When Systems Or Labels Feel Incomplete, Your Truth About Dignity And Accountability Becomes Its Own Guide. How Does It Feel To Reflect On The Ways Your Lived Wisdom Has Shaped Your Advocacy? I’m Here To Explore What Continues To Fuel That Fire In You.;1027
study_a;1142;ctrl_a_1142;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.370769+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"It Sounds Like Those Quiet Moments Give You Space To Recharge—that’s So Important. When Someone Truly Sees And Accepts You Without Asking You To Be ""on,"" It Can Feel Like A Relief, Almost Like Permission To Just *be*. Does That Kind Of Acceptance Help You Feel More At Ease With Needing Rest?";6862
study_a;1143;ctrl_a_1143;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.371176+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;This Moment On The Bridge Must Feel Heavy, Like Every Step Carries So Much Weight. I Wonder What It’s Like To Stand There, Weighing The Paths Ahead. Would You Want To Explore What Each Route Represents To You—or What It Might Feel Like To Trust Yourself, Whichever Way You Choose? You Don’t Have To Cross It Alone.;1028
study_a;1144;ctrl_a_1144;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.371728+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Makes Complete Sense To Want A Safer Environment Where You Can Feel At Ease And Focus. Feeling Unsafe Where You Are Can Make Every Day Feel Heavy. Have You Had Moments Where Imagining That New Place Brings You Relief? What Does Feeling Truly Secure Look Like For You There? Let’s Explore What Steps Toward That Peace Might Involve—whether Through Planning, Connecting With Support, Or Addressing Fears That Linger Even When Considering Change. You Deserve To Feel Grounded, And I’m Here To Help You Navigate That Path.;1031
study_a;1145;ctrl_a_1145;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.372202+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like That Interaction Might Have Stirred Up Some Feelings For You—perhaps Uncertainty Or Protectiveness About Your Personal Boundaries. It’s Okay To Honor What Feels Safe For You In Moments Like That. How Did It Feel To Share That Part Of Yourself With Someone, And What Comes Up When You Think About It Now? You Deserve To Move At Your Own Pace And Trust Your Instincts.;1032
study_a;1146;ctrl_a_1146;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.372723+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Carrying A Lot—wanting To Honor Your Family While Also Finding Space For Your Own Needs. Comparisons Can Make Home Feel Heavy, Especially When You’re Trying To Support Your Mom Through Her Grief. What Would It Look Like To Gently Share Your Feelings With Her, While Still Holding Compassion For Her Pain? Sometimes Naming The Weight Aloud—even Just To Yourself—can Help Lighten It. How Do You Take Care Of *you* In All This?;1036
study_a;1147;ctrl_a_1147;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.373274+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Noticing Shifts In Your Energy, Focus, And Mood That Feel Confusing, Even If They’re Not Disrupting Your Daily Life. It’s Okay To Want Clarity About These Patterns, Especially When They’ve Happened Before. Let’s Explore What These Moments Mean To You—how They Start, What They Feel Like, And How They Settle. Understanding Their Rhythm Could Help You Feel More Grounded, Even If They Don’t Fit A Specific Label. For Now, Maybe Paying Attention To Small Shifts—like How Your Thoughts Or Energy Levels Interact With Sleep Or Impulses—might Reveal Ways To Nurture Steadiness. You’re Not Alone In Wanting To Make Sense Of This. How Does That Feel To Consider?;1037
study_a;1148;ctrl_a_1148;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.373598+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"It Sounds So Overwhelming To Feel That Sense Of Being Physically And Emotionally ""crowded"" By Others. Can We Explore What Happens In Your Body And Thoughts When You’re Around Them? Sometimes Naming Those Reactions Helps Create Space To Breathe Again. You’re Not Alone In This—we’ll Find Ways To Steady Your Footing Together.";4935
study_a;1149;ctrl_a_1149;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.373961+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Carrying A Heavy Weight Of Expectations—both From Others And Yourself. That “superwoman” Role Can Feel Like A Cage, Even Though It’s Meant To Look Strong. What If, Instead Of Seeing Help As A Weakness, You Treated It As A Way To Honor Your Energy And Boundaries? Maybe Start With One Small Task You’d Feel Safe Sharing. Notice What Emotions Rise Up When You Imagine Letting Go Of It—not To Judge Them, But To Understand What They’re Protecting You From. You Deserve Space To Breathe, Not Just To Perform.;2481
study_a;1150;ctrl_a_1150;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.374306+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It’s Clear How Deeply You Care About The People You Share Your Life With—their Perspectives Feel Intertwined With Your Sense Of Connection. When Others’ Opinions Matter So Much, It Can Sometimes Feel Like A Dance Between Honoring Their Voices And Staying True To Your Own. How Does It Feel When Those Perspectives Align With What *you* Need Or Want? Let’s Explore How You Navigate That Balance, Ensuring Your Own Feelings Have Space To Breathe, Too. You Deserve To Feel Grounded In Your Choices, Even Amid Such Closeness.;2074
study_a;1151;ctrl_a_1151;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.374828+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Noticing Real Growth Here—less Anxiety, More Confidence In Balancing Respect For Others With Honoring Your Own Needs. Revisiting That Childhood Message Must Have Taken Courage. How Did It Feel To Hold Both Respect And Self-advocacy In That Space? Sometimes, Old Patterns Soften When We Meet Them With Compassion, Both For Others *and* Ourselves. If You’d Like, We Could Explore How These Shifts Might Ripple Into Other Relationships, Too. You’re Building Something Meaningful Here.;5763
study_a;1152;ctrl_a_1152;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.375333+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like That Time Carried A Mix Of Connection With Your Friend And The Heavy Weight Of Your Parents’ Reaction. Being Met With Shock And Scolding When You Returned Home Must Have Felt Isolating—like Your Reasons Weren’t Fully Seen. I Wonder What Skipping Meant For You Then. Was It Freedom? Escape? A Way To Feel Close To Someone? There’s No Judgment Here. If You’d Like, We Can Gently Unpack What That Chapter Held—not To Justify Or Blame, But To Understand The Feelings And Needs Beneath It. You Deserved To Feel Heard, Even Amid The Consequences. How Does Looking Back On That Time Sit With You Now?;1038
study_a;1153;ctrl_a_1153;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.375679+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;I Hear How Overwhelming This Must Feel. When Relationships Feel Uncertain, It’s Natural To Feel Lost. Could You Share A Little About What’s Been Weighing On Your Heart? Even Small Moments That Stand Out Might Help Us Untangle The Confusion Together, Step By Step. You Don’t Have To Face This Alone.;10038
study_a;1154;ctrl_a_1154;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.376128+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"It Sounds Like You’re Finding Moments Of Satisfaction In Simply Engaging With Small Tasks, Even Without Pressure To ""commit"" To Anything Bigger Today. That’s Okay—sometimes Just Showing Up For The Little Things Can Feel Nourishing. How Does It Feel To Let Yourself Enjoy That Lightness Without Expectations?";1039
study_a;1155;ctrl_a_1155;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.376493+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"It Sounds Like Those Old Thoughts Of ""having To Do Well Or Else"" Add An Extra Layer Of Pressure That Feels Really Heavy. When That Mindset Creeps In, It’s Like The Stakes Suddenly Feel Life-or-death, Even Though Deep Down You Know You’re Capable And Belong Here. What If We Gently Explored What’s Underneath That “or Else”? Sometimes Those Fears—of Not Measuring Up, Of Being “exposed”—are Rooted In Stories We’ve Carried For Years, Not The Reality Of Who You Are Now. What Would It Feel Like To Untangle Your Worth From Those Expectations, Even Just A Little? You’re Already Showing Up, Doing The Work—that Itself Is Enough.";1041
study_a;1156;ctrl_a_1156;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.376923+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;I Hear How Exhausting It Must Feel To Carry That Weight Every Day. When The Pressure Feels Endless, Even Pushing Forward Can Leave You Breathless. What If, Instead Of Fighting The Quicksand, We Gently Explore What’s Beneath It? Sometimes Slowing Down To Understand The Weight—not To Remove It Yet, But To See It Clearly—can Create Space To Breathe. You’re Already Here, Reaching Out. That Takes Courage. Let’s Walk Through This Together, One Small Step At A Time. What Does Your Heart Need Most In This Moment?;16284
study_a;1157;ctrl_a_1157;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.377255+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Ready To Shed Something That’s Weighed You Down For A While—like Making Space To Breathe Freely Again. That Desire To Release What No Longer Serves You Is Powerful. What Would It Feel Like To Imagine Life Without That Weight? What Small Step Could Help You Start Creating That Space?;1042
study_a;1158;ctrl_a_1158;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.377616+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;What A Meaningful Step You’ve Taken—it’s Not “just A Desk” When It Represents So Much Emotionally. That Mix Of Pride And Fear Makes Sense When Something We’ve Avoided Starts To Shift. Could The Trembling And Dread Be Your Mind Signaling It’s Learning To Trust Your Capacity For Change? Let’s Explore What “something Bad” Means To You Now. Often, After Pushing Through Avoidance, Old Worries Surface, Waiting For The Other Shoe To Drop. What If This Is Actually Your Strength Showing Up, And The Fear Is Just Catching Up? Let’s Hold Space For Both Feelings—they’re Both Valid. How Does It Feel To Imagine Letting The Pride Settle Deeper Than The Fear?;13986
study_a;1159;ctrl_a_1159;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.377913+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Incredibly Heavy To Carry All That Pressure—like Your Worth Is Tied To Every Grade. That Worry Must Feel Constant. Would It Help To Unpack Where That Fear Comes From? Maybe We Could Explore How To Balance Study With Moments Of Rest, So It Doesn’t Drain You So Deeply. You Deserve That Space To Breathe.;9463
study_a;1160;ctrl_a_1160;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.378310+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;Thank You For Sharing That—it Means A Lot To Know You Feel Seen. Cultural Expectations Like *marianismo* Can Shape So Much Of How We View Ourselves And Our Roles. If You’d Like, We Could Explore How These Pressures Have Impacted Your Sense Of Identity Or Choices, And Where You Feel Your Own Needs Might Align Or Clash With Them. Your Comfort And Trust Matter Deeply here—I’m Glad You Feel Safe To Open Up, And I’ll Always Meet Your Experiences With Care. What Feels Most Important To Unpack Next?;1043
study_a;1161;ctrl_a_1161;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.378730+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;That Sounds So Deeply Painful—to Share Your Heart So Openly And Feel Met With Distance Or Half-listening. It Makes Sense You’d Feel Exhausted, Even Hopeless. Would It Help To Explore What It Might Look Like To Nurture Connections Where Your Words Feel Truly *received*? Not Just Heard, But Held. You Deserve That Kind Of Space.;18749
study_a;1162;ctrl_a_1162;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.379095+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"It Sounds Like You’re Juggling A Lot Right Now—trying To Balance School And Finances While Also Navigating Those Moments When Spending Feels Like An Escape Or A Quick Relief. Let’s Gently Unpack What Those ""unnecessary"" Purchases Might Be Giving You Emotionally. Could They Be Filling A Need For Comfort, Distraction, Or Even A Sense Of Control When Other Areas Feel Uncertain? What If We Explored Small, Intentional Shifts Together? For Example, Tracking Your Spending For A Week *without Judgment*—just Noticing Patterns—and Pairing It With Short, Focused Study Sessions To Create Structure. Sometimes, Building Tiny Pauses Before Purchases (even 10 Seconds To Breathe And Ask, *“Is This Aligning With What I Truly Need?”*) Can Create Space To Choose Differently. How Does That Feel To Consider?";1044
study_a;1163;ctrl_a_1163;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.379477+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like Holding That Image Brings Up Deep Sadness—longing For Connection That’s Always Felt Just Out Of Reach. That Gap Between What You’ve Hoped For And What’s Been Missing Can Be So Heavy. Would It Feel Safe To Explore How That Absence Has Shaped The Way You Relate To Yourself, Or Others? You Don’t Have To Carry That Ache Alone Here.;1045
study_a;1164;ctrl_a_1164;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.379673+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"It Sounds Like You’re Noticing How Doubt Can Shape Your Perspective, Which Takes Real Courage To Acknowledge. When Those Doubts Arise, What Happens If You Gently Ask Yourself: *Is This Thought Trying To Protect Me, Or Is It Limiting How I See Possibilities?* Sometimes Untangling The ""why"" Behind The Doubt Can Soften Its Grip—would You Want To Explore That Together?";2795
study_a;1165;ctrl_a_1165;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.379957+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Noticing How Powerful Connection Can Be Once You Break Through The Initial Barriers. The Effort You Put Into Reaching That Understanding Must Take A Lot Of Patience And Care. What Does That Process Feel Like For You—the Moments *before* Things Click Into Place? Let’s Explore What Happens There.;1382
study_a;1166;ctrl_a_1166;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.380285+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Working So Hard To Find Moments Of Calm, And That Effort Itself Is Meaningful. Those Glimpses Of Relief—even Brief Ones—show How Resilient You Are. Instead Of Abandoning These Feelings, Could You Gently Make Space For Them? Like Waves, They Might Grow Quieter When Met With Curiosity Instead Of Resistance. What Do You Think Might Happen If You Let Them Exist *without* Needing To Push Them Away? You Don’t Have To Carry This Alone.;1046
study_a;1167;ctrl_a_1167;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.380664+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;I Hear How Much You Want Clarity Without Pressure, And I’m Truly Sorry This Feels Uneasy Right Now. Your Feelings Matter Deeply Here—this Space Is Yours. Would It Help If We Slowed Down, Shifted Focus, Or Explored What Safety Might Look Like For You In This Moment? I’m Here To Listen, Not To Push.;1047
study_a;1168;ctrl_a_1168;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.381168+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;I Hear How These Intense Shifts In Energy And Mood Are Both Exciting And Overwhelming. It Sounds Like Your Confidence And Drive Have Been Soaring, Yet The Frustration And Strained Relationships Are Weighing On You. Let’s Gently Explore How These Changes Are Affecting Your Daily Life And Connections With Others. Together, We Could Look At Ways To Channel This Energy Mindfully While Creating Space For Rest And Reflection. Small Steps, Like Pausing To Check In With Your Body Or Jotting Down Thoughts Before Acting On Them, Might Help Bring More Balance. Would You Feel Open To Trying Something Like That? You’re Not Alone In Navigating This.;1048
study_a;1169;ctrl_a_1169;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.381662+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You Navigated A Really Challenging Environment Where Authenticity Might Have Felt Risky. Adapting To Survive In Spaces That Demand Compliance Can Leave Deep Imprints—like Needing To Monitor Every Word Or Action. How Does It Feel Now, Looking Back On That Time? Do Parts Of That Experience Still Linger In How You Approach Situations Or Connect With Others? I Imagine Holding That Tension Between Protecting Yourself And Wanting To Be Genuine Could Stir Up Frustration Or Even Grief. Would It Help To Unpack What “playing The Game” Cost You—and What Strengths It Might Have Revealed? You’re Not Alone In Carrying That Weight.;1049
study_a;1170;ctrl_a_1170;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.381965+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;That Sounds Like A Small Moment That Held Big Feelings—the Buzzing Intrusion, The Heat Of Being Watched While You’re Already Stretched Thin. Sometimes When We’re Trying To Manage Something Frustrating, Having Eyes On Us Can Make It Feel Heavier, Like The Pressure Doubles. Could We Gently Explore What That Moment Stirred Up For You? Not Just The Fly Or The Stomping, But The Weight Of Being Observed When You Were Already Wrestling With Irritation? What Does That Part Of You Need To Feel Grounded In Moments Like That?;3174
study_a;1171;ctrl_a_1171;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.382334+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Navigating The Demands Of Motherhood With Strength, Even If It Means Some Nights Feel Restless Or Fragmented. Many Parents Find Their Sleep Rhythms Shift To Meet Their Child’s Needs—it’s A Lot To Carry. How Does This Pattern Sit With You? Are There Moments When The Fatigue Feels Heavier Than It Should, Or Do You Feel You’re Managing It In Stride? Let’s Explore What Support Might Lighten That Load, Even In Small Ways.;1050
study_a;1172;ctrl_a_1172;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.382617+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like Your Mind’s Been Amplifying Fears Beyond What Your Lived Experience Shows. That Space Between What We *imagine* And What’s *actually Happened* Can Feel So Vast, Can’t It? Let’s Gently Explore What It Might Look Like To Anchor Back In The Reality Of Those Few Instances—what Feels Different When You Focus There?;725
study_a;1173;ctrl_a_1173;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.382915+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;I’m Here To Listen, And I Want You To Feel Safe Sharing Whatever Feels Right. Confusion In Relationships Can Feel So Heavy—like Standing At A Crossroads Without A Map. Let’s Walk Through This Together. What’s Been On Your Heart Lately? Sometimes Untangling Emotions Starts By Simply Naming Them Aloud, In A Space Where You’re Truly Heard. You’re Not Alone In This.;9377
study_a;1174;ctrl_a_1174;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.383276+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"That’s Wonderful To Hear—it Sounds Like This Goal Is Lighting A Spark Of Purpose And Hope For You. Hold Onto That Excitement; It’s A Sign Of How Invested You Are In Your Own Growth. As You Work On Your Experiment, Notice What It Teaches You About Your Strengths And What Feels Meaningful. Small Steps Can Carry Big Insights. How Does It Feel To Have This Focus Guiding You Forward? I’m Here To Walk Alongside You As You Explore.";1051
study_a;1175;ctrl_a_1175;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.383820+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;What You’re Describing Sounds Incredibly Overwhelming, And I Can Only Imagine How Unsettling It Must Feel To Experience These Sudden Shifts In Thoughts, Emotions, And Perceptions. It’s Okay To Feel Scared Or Confused—these Are New And Intense Sensations, And You’re Doing The Right Thing By Reaching Out. Let’s Slow Down And Unpack This Together. When These Thoughts Or Feelings Arise, We Can Explore Grounding Strategies To Help You Feel More Anchored In The Present Moment. For Example, Focusing On Your Senses—like The Feel Of Your Feet On The Floor Or Sounds Around You—might Help Ease The Intensity. The Ups And Downs In Your Emotions Could Be Clues To What’s Weighing On You Beneath The Surface. If You’re Open To It, We Could Gently Trace When These Moments Happen And What They Might Connect To, Like Stressors Or Unresolved Feelings. You Don’t Have To Navigate This Alone. Let’s Work On Building Tools To Help You Feel More Steady And Safe. Would That Feel Okay?;1052
study_a;1176;ctrl_a_1176;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.384106+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Makes Sense To Feel That Way When Patterns From Childhood Run Deep. What If We Gently Explore How Those Early Experiences Might Still Be Shaping What Feels Familiar Or Safe Now? You Deserve To Discover What Truly Resonates With *you*—not Just What You Were Taught To Want. Would You Feel Okay Sharing An Example?;1053
study_a;1177;ctrl_a_1177;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.384505+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Carrying So Much Weight Right Now—like Every Step Feels Heavier Than It Should. That Guilt And Anger Toward Yourself Must Be Exhausting. What If We Paused For A Moment To Untangle Those “shoulds” You’re Holding Onto? Sometimes, When We’re Overwhelmed, Our Minds Start Shouting That We’re Failing, But Those Thoughts Aren’t Facts—they’re Just Echoes Of How Worn Out You Are. Could We Explore What Those Small Tasks *feel* Like In Your Body, Not Just Your Thoughts? Maybe There’s More Beneath The Surface, Like Grief Over How Hard Things Have Become, Or Fear Of What Falling Behind Means. You Don’t Have To “handle” Anything Alone. What Would It Look Like To Let Some Of That Guilt Soften, Even Just A Little? You’re Trying So Hard—that Matters.;18028
study_a;1178;ctrl_a_1178;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.384875+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"It Sounds Like Your Mind And Body Are Caught In A Storm Of ""what Ifs."" That Racing Heart And Urge To Check Might Be Trying To Protect You, Even If There’s No Real Danger. Could You Take One Slow Breath With Me? Sometimes Slowing Down Helps Us See The Space Between Fear And What’s Actually Here. You’re Not Silly—you’re Human, And This Is Heavy To Carry Alone.";15381
study_a;1179;ctrl_a_1179;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.385148+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Really Tough To Feel That Distance With Someone You Care About So Deeply. Would You Feel Comfortable Sharing What Moments Together Have Felt Like Recently? Sometimes Small Steps—like Sharing A Meal Or An Activity He Enjoys—can Gently Open Doors To Understanding Each Other’s Perspectives Again. You’re Not Alone In This.;9689
study_a;1180;ctrl_a_1180;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.385420+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"It Takes Real Strength To Honor Your Needs While Considering Others. That Tension You're Feeling Might Be Your Inner Wisdom Saying Both Matter—your Voice Deserves Space Too. When You Notice Yourself Prioritizing Someone Else's Wants, Could You Pause And Ask: ""What Part Of Me Needs Attention Right Now?"" Small Moments Of Checking In With Yourself Can Become Anchors. You're Not Losing Yourself—you're Actively Choosing To Stay Present With Your Values. How Does That Land For You?";6308
study_a;1181;ctrl_a_1181;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.385724+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Really Tough To Carry That Weight Even After Your Boss Reassured You. When Our Minds Get Stuck Replaying Moments Like This, It Often Reveals How Deeply We Care About Doing Well—which Speaks To Your Dedication. What If, Instead Of Asking “Why Can’t I Get It Right?” We Gently Explored What That Mistake *means* To You? Sometimes, The Stories We Tell Ourselves About Slip-ups—like “I’m Failing” Or “I’m Not Enough”—can Feel Truer Than They Really Are. What Would It Look Like To Offer Yourself The Same Patience You’d Give A Friend In This Situation? Small Steps Toward Self-kindness Can Slowly Loosen The Grip Of Self-doubt. You’re Not Alone In This.;15166
study_a;1182;ctrl_a_1182;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.386080+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;That Sounds Really Heavy To Carry—like You’re Reaching Out But The World Feels Just Out Of Reach. It Makes Sense To Feel Worn Down When The Longing For Connection Bumps Up Against So Much Quiet. Would It Help To Explore What *meaningful* Connection Might Look Like For You Right Now? Sometimes When We’re Drained, Even Small Steps—like Sharing A Hobby Or Joining A Low-pressure Group—can Feel Overwhelming, But We Can Untangle That Together. You Deserve To Feel Seen, And I’m Here To Listen As You Figure Out How That Might Start To Take Shape. What’s One Tiny Way You Could Invite A Sense Of Closeness This Week, Even If It Feels Uncertain?;17101
study_a;1183;ctrl_a_1183;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.386434+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like That Inner Voice Has Been Working Hard To Protect You, Even When Expressing Emotions Felt Unsafe As A Child. What If We Gently Explore How That Part Of You—the One Trying To Make Sense Of Anger—could Share Its Worries *with* You, Rather Than Just *for* You? You Deserve Space To Feel What You Feel Now, Without Old Dangers. Would It Help To Unpack What Anger Might Be Trying To Tell You, At A Pace That Feels Safe? I’m Here To Listen.;1054
study_a;1184;ctrl_a_1184;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.386805+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;I Hear How Unsettling This Must Feel—like Your Mind Is Working Overtime Even When You Need Rest. These Intense Dreams Might Be Carrying Emotions Or Worries That Haven’t Found Space During The Day. Would It Help To Gently Explore What They’re Bringing Up, Or Perhaps Create A Calming Ritual Before Bed To Ease The Transition Into Sleep? You Deserve Moments Of Peace, Even In The Midst Of This. Let’s Find Ways To Help You Feel Safer As You Rest.;16354
study_a;1185;ctrl_a_1185;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.387116+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;I Hear How Deeply This Weighs On You, And I’m So Glad You Shared It—that Took Courage. The Exhaustion Of Feeling This Way For So Long Makes Sense. Can We Slow Down And Explore Where That Belief That You’re “broken” Comes From? Sometimes These Feelings Form Early, Like Old Echoes That Aren’t True Reflections Of Who You Are Now. What If We Gently Untangle What You *do* From Your Worth? You Matter, Full Stop—not Because Of Achievements, But Simply Because You Exist. Let’s Find Small Ways To Rest From That Pressure Together. Would That Feel Okay?;12119
study_a;1186;ctrl_a_1186;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.387563+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like This Is Really Weighing On You—feeling Like You’re Not In Control Of Reactions That Don’t Align With Who You Want To Be. That Guilt And Frustration Make Sense. Could We Gently Explore What Might Be Surfacing In Those Moments? Sometimes Strong Reactions Are Clues To Needs Or Feelings We Haven’t Fully Acknowledged. What If, When You Notice Tension Rising, You Paused Just Long Enough To Ask Yourself, *What’s Happening Beneath This Reaction?* It’s Not About Blaming Yourself, But Creating A Small Space To Choose How To Respond. Healing Often Starts With Curiosity, Not Judgment. How Does That Land For You?;14203
study_a;1187;ctrl_a_1187;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.387872+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It’s Clear You Care Deeply About Growing From This Experience, And That Willingness To Reflect Is Already A Meaningful Step. Let’s Gently Unpack What Happened—what Felt Most Challenging In The Moment, And What Small Adjustments Might Ease Similar Situations Moving Forward? We Can Explore Practical Strategies To Rebuild Confidence, Like Grounding Techniques For Overwhelm Or Reframing Self-talk When Doubt Creeps In. Would It Help To Focus On A Specific Part Of This Process Together? You’re Not Alone In This.;1056
study_a;1188;ctrl_a_1188;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.388301+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It’s Clear How Deeply You Care About Supporting Others While Honoring Their Boundaries. That Balance Between Hope And Caution Makes Sense—like Tending A Garden, Where Growth Thrives When There’s Both Sunlight And Shelter. Trusting Someone’s Readiness To Explore Pain, At *their* Pace, Might Help You Both Navigate This Without Forcing Doors Open. How Does That Land For You?;11181
study_a;1189;ctrl_a_1189;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.388672+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;That Sounds Incredibly Overwhelming And Frightening. When Those Intense Physical Sensations And Fears Rush In, It Can Feel Like The World Is Spinning Out Of Control. Let’s Pause Here Together. Can We Take A Moment To Notice The Solid Ground Beneath Your Feet, The Air Moving In And Out Of Your Lungs? You’re Safe Right Now. These Feelings, As Terrifying As They Are, Cannot Harm You—they’re Your Body’s Way Of Signaling Distress. When You’re Ready, We Can Explore What Might Have Stirred This Reaction, Step By Step, At Your Pace. For Now, Let’s Just Focus On Helping Your Body Settle. You’re Not Alone In This.;3646
study_a;1190;ctrl_a_1190;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.389110+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"It Sounds Like This Carries Some Emotional Weight For You, Even With Your Understanding Of Its Importance. Sometimes Past Experiences Can Create Invisible Pressures—like Needing To Meet Unspoken Expectations Or Fearing Disappointment. What If We Gently Explore What Gift-giving Means To You Now, Separate From What It Meant Before? Your Care Shines Through; Perfection Isn’t Required For That To Matter.";1058
study_a;1191;ctrl_a_1191;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.389417+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;That Sounds Like Such A Beautiful Experience—moments Where Everything Aligns And We Feel Truly Present Are So Rare And Precious. I Wonder, If You’re Open To Exploring, What Might Have Allowed That Quietness To Unfold? Were There Certain Feelings, Surroundings, Or Thoughts That Gently Stepped Aside? Let’s Hold Space For What That Peace Might Teach You About Moments When Life Feels Lighter.;1059
study_a;1192;ctrl_a_1192;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.389847+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like That Experience Left You Feeling Deeply Shaken—that Sense Of Powerlessness Can Linger In Such Raw, Heavy Ways. Wanting To Leave Makes Complete Sense, Yet The Fear Of Carrying Those Feelings Somewhere New Is So Real, Too. Maybe We Could Explore What Parts Of *here* Feel Hardest To Hold Right Now, And What A Fresh Start Might Gently Make Space For? Even Naming Those Hopes And Fears Could Help You Feel More Grounded As You Weigh What Comes Next. You Don’t Have To Have All The Answers Right Now—we Can Untangle This Together, One Step At A Time.;14324
study_a;1193;ctrl_a_1193;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.390299+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"It Sounds Like You’re Holding Both Hope And Fear At Once—that’s So Human. Your Body And Emotions Are Adjusting To Something New, And That ""off"" Feeling Can Be Unsettling. Would It Help To Name What’s Happening Without Judgment? Maybe Track These Shifts For A Day Or Two, Then Share Them With Your Prescriber. You’re Not Alone In This—adjustments Often Take Time *and* Dialogue. How Does That Sound?";17241
study_a;1194;ctrl_a_1194;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.390755+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"It Sounds Like Those Moments When Others Push Past Your ""no"" Stir Up Strong Feelings—like Your Boundaries Matter Deeply, And It’s Painful When They’re Overlooked. That Anger Makes Sense; It’s A Signal That Something Important To You Is Being Challenged. I Wonder What It Might Feel Like To Honor That Anger As A Form Of Self-protection, While Also Exploring Ways To Reinforce Your Boundaries With Calm Clarity. Could We Look At What Happens In Those Moments—not Just The Interaction, But The Thoughts Or Fears That Arise? Sometimes, Understanding The Roots Of Our Reactions Helps Us Respond In Ways That Align With Our Values, Not Just Our Emotions. You Deserve To Feel Respected, And Your ""no"" Is Valid. How Does That Land For You?";1060
study_a;1195;ctrl_a_1195;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.391114+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;This Sounds Incredibly Overwhelming, And My Heart Goes Out To You. It Makes Sense To Feel Disconnected From Yourself When So Much Has Changed. Would It Feel Safe To Start With Small, Gentle Steps—like Choosing One Comforting Meal Today Or A Warm Bath Before Bed? We Can Work Together To Help Your Body Feel Like Home Again, At Your Own Pace. You’re Not Alone In This.;13937
study_a;1196;ctrl_a_1196;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.391485+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Carrying A Lot Of Self-awareness And Even Some Tenderness About This. It’s Okay To Crave Meaningful Connections—that’s Human. Maybe We Could Explore What “foolish” Means To You And How Those Judgments Might Be Protecting You From Something Deeper, Like Vulnerability Or Unmet Needs. What If Small, Intentional Interactions Could Exist Alongside Your Boundaries, Without Compromising Your Values? You Deserve Compassion Here, Both For Your Mind And Your Heart.;1062
study_a;1197;ctrl_a_1197;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.391828+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It’s Clear How Deeply You Care, And That Longing To Mend Things Is So Real. When We’re Hurting, Our Words Can Sometimes Carry More Weight Than We Intend. What If You Started By Sharing This Exact Feeling With Them—the Guilt, The Fear Of Losing What You Have? Letting Them See Your Vulnerability Might Open A Door To Understanding. Could You Imagine A Moment Where You Both Just Listen, Without Fixing Yet? Sometimes Sitting With The Ache Together Softens The Edges. How Does That Sit With You?;15833
study_a;1198;ctrl_a_1198;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.392272+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Carrying A Heavy Emotional Load, Even Though Your Body Keeps Going. The Disconnect Between Your Daily Grind And The Dreams That Feel Out Of Reach Must Be So Disheartening—like Part Of You Is Quietly Dimming. When You Mention The Drinking, I Wonder If It’s Become A Way To Numb That Ache Of Unmet Hopes, Even Temporarily. What If We Gently Explored Small Ways To Reconnect With What Matters To You? Maybe Carving Out Moments—even Just 10 Minutes—to Reflect On What Once Sparked Joy, Or Sharing Those Quieter Thoughts With Your Wife When The Weight Feels Lighter? Sometimes, Untangling One Thread Can Help Loosen The Knot. You’re Clearly Resilient—how Might That Strength Look If Directed Toward Nurturing The Parts Of You That Feel Lost?;3067
study_a;1199;ctrl_a_1199;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.392601+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;That Sounds So Heavy To Carry—like You’re Holding A Storm Inside That No One Else Notices. Those Memories Can Feel Relentless, Can’t They? It Takes Real Courage To Name This Ache, Even Here. Would It Help To Gently Explore What Those Memories Are Trying To Tell You, Or How They Show Up In Your Body? Sometimes Sitting With Them—not To Change Or Fix, Just To Listen—can Soften Their Grip A Little. You’re Not Alone In This, Even When It Feels That Way. I’m Here To Walk Through It With You, One Step At A Time.;10958
study_a;1200;ctrl_a_1200;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.392867+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;I’m Truly Sorry You’re Feeling This Way—being Teased Or Excluded Can Hurt Deeply, And It Makes Sense You’d Feel Uncomfortable. You Deserve To Feel Safe And Respected. Would You Feel Okay Sharing More About What Happens In Those Moments? Sometimes, Understanding Patterns Can Help Us Find Small Ways To Protect Your Peace Or Communicate Your Needs. You’re Not Alone In This—we’ll Work Through It Together, Step By Step.;8785
study_a;1201;ctrl_a_1201;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.393225+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"It Sounds Like These Intense Feelings Are Coming In Waves, Overwhelming You Before You Can Catch Your Breath. That Cycle Of Anger Followed By Self-criticism Must Feel Exhausting. What If We Gently Explored What Those Moments Of Frustration Might Be Pointing To Beneath The Surface? Sometimes When Emotions Feel Too Big To Hold, They’re Trying To Tell Us About Needs That Feel Unmet, Boundaries That Feel Crossed, Or Hurts That Haven’t Had Space To Be Heard. If You’re Open To It, We Could Look At Ways To Slow Those Reactions Down—not To Dismiss Your Anger, But To Understand What It’s Asking For. How Does That Land For You? You’re Not Failing Here; You’re Noticing Patterns, And That’s A Brave First Step.";11271
study_a;1202;ctrl_a_1202;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.393533+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Carrying A Heavy Storm Of Emotions—grief, Anger, Fear, And Even Moments Of Wanting To Reclaim Control. These Feelings Make Sense When Something So Important Feels Lost. Could We Gently Explore What’s Beneath The Urge For Vengeance? Maybe It’s A Protective Part Of You That’s Hurting Deeply, Longing To Be Seen And Heard. What If We Created Space For All These Emotions To Exist Without Judgment, So You Can Untangle What You Truly Need To Heal? You Don’t Have To Navigate This Alone.;1063
study_a;1203;ctrl_a_1203;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.393834+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like This Habit Is Something You’re Reflecting On More Deeply Lately, Especially Since It’s Part Of Your Daily Life And Relationships. When Habits Are Tied To People We Care About, Change Can Feel Complicated. What’s It Like For You To Carry This Awareness Now? Are There Small Steps That Feel Meaningful To Explore Together?;1064
study_a;1204;ctrl_a_1204;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.394246+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;What You’re Describing Makes So Much Sense—relief And Anger Crashing Together Can Feel Disorienting, Almost Like Your Heart Is Catching Up To What Your Mind’s Known For Years. It’s Okay To Hold Both: Gratitude For Being Seen *and* Grief Over How Long It Took. That Tension Doesn’t Need Solving Right Now. Maybe We Could Gently Untangle What Each Part Of This Storm Is Telling You? Sometimes When Validation Finally Comes, It Stirs Up The Hurt We’ve Carried Silently. You’re Not Alone In This Swirl—we Can Move Through It Step By Step, Honoring All Of It.;17906
study_a;1205;ctrl_a_1205;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.394542+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"It’s Okay To Feel Uncertain In Spaces That Seem Unfamiliar—that’s A Natural Reaction. Many People Feel Unsure About ""navigating"" New Environments, Especially When It Feels Like Everyone Else Knows Exactly What To Do. What Would It Feel Like To Give Yourself Permission To Just Observe, Or Even Step In For A Moment And Then Leave If It Feels Overwhelming? Small Steps Can Help Build Comfort Over Time. You’re Not Alone In Feeling This Way.";1065
study_a;1206;ctrl_a_1206;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.394881+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds So Heavy To Feel Trapped Like That—like The Ground Keeps Shifting But You Can’t Find Your Footing. When You Compare Yourself To Others, It Must Deepen That Ache Of Being Left Behind. Can We Explore What “moving Forward” Might Look Like *for You*, Separate From What You See Around You? Even Tiny Steps Count, And They’re Not Always Visible Right Away. Let’s Untangle What’s Keeping You Feeling So Stuck—not To “fix” It All At Once, But To Find One Thread You *can* Hold Onto. Would That Feel Possible?;16095
study_a;1207;ctrl_a_1207;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.395292+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;This Sounds Incredibly Frustrating—being Stuck In This Waiting Period, Unable To Move Forward With Healing Either Knee, While Navigating Legal Hurdles. It Must Feel Like Your Body And The System Are Both Working Against You. How Are You Coping With The Emotional Weight Of This Limbo? If It Helps, We Could Explore What Parts Of This Situation Feel *most* Overwhelming Right Now. Sometimes Breaking It Down—or Even Just Naming The Exhaustion, Anger, Or Helplessness—can Create A Little Space To Breathe. You’re Holding So Much Right Now.;1066
study_a;1208;ctrl_a_1208;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.395800+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"It Sounds Like You’re Carrying A Lot—balancing Expectations, Past Hurts, And The Belief That Being ""perfect"" Academically Could Protect You From Pain. That’s So Much Weight To Hold. When We Tie Our Worth To Achievements, Even Ones We’re Good At, It Can Feel Like Walking A Tightrope. What If We Explored How To Soften That Pressure? Maybe We Could Look At The Stories You Tell Yourself About What You “owe” The World—or Yourself—and Gently Question Whether Those Stories Still Serve You. You Don’t Have To Earn Your Value Through Accomplishments; It’s Already There. Would It Feel Safe To Experiment With Small Moments Of Rest Or Self-kindness, Even If Just To See What Happens? You Deserve Space To Breathe, Not Just Succeed.";1067
study_a;1209;ctrl_a_1209;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.396177+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It’s Beautiful To Hear How Gerald’s Words Resonated With You—it Sounds Like His Reflection Helped You See Your Growth In A New Light. Sometimes Others’ Perspectives Can Mirror Strengths We’ve Overlooked In Ourselves. How Does It Feel To Acknowledge How Far You’ve Come? Let’s Explore What Patience Means For *your* Journey. Trusting Your Own Timing, Even As You Learn From Others, Can Be A Powerful Way To Honor Both Your Progress And Your Path Forward.;6527
study_a;1210;ctrl_a_1210;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.396551+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"This Must Feel Like The Ground Beneath You Has Shifted—how Unsettling And Heartbreaking To Question The Foundation Of Your Family. It’s Okay To Sit With The Confusion And Sadness; These Feelings Are Valid, Even If The Facts Aren’t Clear Yet. When Memories Feel Tangled, It Might Help To Gently Ask Yourself: *What Parts Of Your Family’s Love And Connection Still Feel Real To You?* Holding Space For Both The Pain And The Enduring Truths Could Help You Navigate This Uncertainty Without Losing Sight Of The Relationships That Anchor You. Take Your Time—you Don’t Have To Untangle Everything At Once.";18046
study_a;1211;ctrl_a_1211;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.396954+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Balancing Gratitude For Your Boss’s Kindness With Very Real Concerns About Financial Stability—that’s A Lot To Hold. Let’s Explore What Moving Would Mean Practically And Emotionally. Could We Break Down The Costs, Your Priorities, And Even Talk Through Worst-case Scenarios? Sometimes Naming Fears Helps Soften Their Weight. You Deserve Support That Feels Safe *and* Sustainable.;1068
study_a;1212;ctrl_a_1212;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.397340+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;I Hear How Heavy This Feels—the Hope For A Fresh Start Colliding With Familiar Pain. It’s Okay To Grieve The Gap Between What You Wanted And Where You Are. Blame Often Masks Deep Care—what If We Gently Untangle The “why” Behind These Feelings? Sometimes, Stepping Back To See The Patterns, Not Just The Pain, Helps Us Find A Thread To Pull. What Would It Feel Like To Soften The Grip On Self-judgment, Even Just A Little? You’re Trying So Hard—that Matters. Let’s Explore What Small Step Could Help You Reconnect With Your Own Worth, Separate From Outcomes. You’re Not Alone Here.;17361
