study_a;1625;ctrl_a_1625;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.563311+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"It Sounds So Draining To Feel Pulled Between Others’ Needs And Your Own—like No Matter What You Choose, Part Of You Ends Up Hurt. That Guilt You Mentioned… Do You Think It Might Be Tied To A Fear Of How Others See You, Or Maybe How You See Yourself When You Say ""no""? What If We Explored What ""selfish"" Really Means Here—could Setting A Kind Boundary *also* Be A Way Of Respecting Both Your Coworker *and* Yourself In The Long Run? Maybe Even Small Steps, Like ""I Need To Check My Plans First,"" Could Help You Practice Honoring Your Energy Without Shutting Down That Caring Part Of You. How Does That Land?";18786
