study_a;1654;ctrl_a_1654;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.575123+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;I Hear How Heavy This Feels—like You’re Holding So Much, And Suddenly The Ground Shifts. It Makes Sense To Feel Unsteady When Things Tip Unexpectedly. What If We Looked At What’s Weighing Most On You Right Now? Sometimes Naming Those Pressures Helps Soften Their Grip, Even A Little. You Don’t Have To Carry It All Alone. What Parts Of Your Life Feel Most Unstable? What Small Steps Could Help You Reconnect With What Grounds You?;1337
study_a;1655;ctrl_a_1655;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.575528+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Takes Real Courage To Share This—thank You For Trusting Me With These Feelings. Silence Can Feel Heavy, But It’s Okay To Let It Exist Here. Sometimes Our Bodies Hold What Words Can’t. If Your Shoulder Could Speak, What Might It Say About Needing Stability Or Safety? We Can Move At Your Pace, And I’ll Be Right Here With You. Would It Help To Try Writing Or Drawing What Feels Stuck, Even If We Do It Quietly Together?;1338
study_a;1656;ctrl_a_1656;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.575959+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Incredibly Painful To Carry This Fear Of Rejection From Those Closest To You. Their Jokes Might Make You Feel Unseen Or Unsafe, And That’s Deeply Hurtful. You Deserve To Be Fully Accepted As You Are. Would It Help To Explore Ways To Nurture Your Sense Of Worth *apart* From Their Reactions? You’re Not Alone In This.;1339
study_a;1657;ctrl_a_1657;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.576245+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Takes Real Courage To Share Something That Feels Difficult. Thank You For Trusting Me With This. Work Challenges Can Stir Up So Much—maybe Uncertainty, Pressure, Or Even Feelings About Self-worth. Whatever It Is, We Can Move At Your Pace. What’s Been The Hardest Part To Carry Lately? You Don’t Have To Hold It Alone.;1340
study_a;1658;ctrl_a_1658;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.576683+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Carrying A Lot On Your Own—wanting To Reclaim Your Independence While Also Worrying About David’s Habits And Your Own Well-being. Your Panic Attacks Are Your Body’s Way Of Saying It Needs Care. Before Sharing With Him, Ask Yourself: *Would Telling Him Feel Like A Relief, Or Might It Add More Weight?* You Deserve Support That Feels Safe And Steady. If Opening Up Feels Uncertain, Start Small—perhaps Focusing First On Grounding Yourself In Moments Of Panic (like Breathing Slowly With Your Eyes Closed). Trust Your Intuition About What *you* Need To Feel Heard.;1341
study_a;1659;ctrl_a_1659;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.577087+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’ve Been Carrying So Much For Others That Your Own Cup Has Nowhere Left To Pour From. That Heaviness Is Real, And It’s Okay To Feel This Way. What If We Explored Ways To Help You Recognize When Others’ Emotions Begin To Seep Into Your Space, And Gently Redirect That Energy Back To Them? Imagine Creating A Small, Invisible Boundary—like A Breath Between Their Mood And Your Response—letting Their Feelings Pass Through You Instead Of Sticking. This Isn’t About Shutting People Out, But Honoring Your Capacity. How Does That Idea Sit With You? You Deserve To Protect Your Peace.;14928
study_a;1660;ctrl_a_1660;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.577578+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Navigating A Really Tender Space Between Care For Your Well-being And The Natural Enjoyment Of Food—that Balance Can Feel So Delicate. The Environments Around Us Aren’t Always Kind To That Effort, Are They? What Would It Feel Like To Approach These Moments With Curiosity Instead Of Judgment? Maybe We Could Explore What Those Temptations Might Be Telling You—are They About Hunger, Comfort, Or Something Else? Together, We Could Gently Uncover Ways To Honor Both Your Body’s Needs And The Joy Food Brings, Without Letting Guilt Steer The Wheel. How Does That Land For You?;1342
study_a;1661;ctrl_a_1661;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.577992+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Carrying So Much Weight Right Now, And I Want You To Know I’m Here To Sit With You In This. When Those Thoughts Tell You You’re “useless” Or “hopeless,” Do They Feel Like Facts, Or Could They Be Stories Your Mind Is Clinging To? Sometimes Our Brains Fixate On The Worst-case Scenarios When We’re Hurting, Making It Hard To See Other Possibilities. What If We Gently Explored Moments—even Small Ones—where You’ve Felt Connected Or Capable Before? They Might Not Erase The Pain, But They Could Help Us Challenge Those Overwhelming Narratives. And When You Feel Ignored, Would You Be Open To Trying One Tiny Step Toward Reaching Out? It Could Be As Simple As Sharing This Struggle With Someone You Trust. You Don’t Have To Carry This Alone.;1343
study_a;1662;ctrl_a_1662;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.578492+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Trying To Balance Your Needs With Hers, Even If It Feels Tangled Right Now. When We Hide Parts Of Ourselves To Keep Peace, It Can Leave Both People Feeling Unseen. What Would It Feel Like To Share Your Preferences Openly, While Also Making Space For Hers? Trust Often Grows When We Let Ourselves Be Honest, Even In Small Moments Like Coffee Choices. You Deserve To Feel Heard, Too. How Does That Idea Sit With You?;1345
study_a;1663;ctrl_a_1663;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.578882+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"Your Worry Makes Complete Sense—carrying That Weight Even After Probation Ends Can Feel Isolating. When Those Doubts Surface, What Helps You Separate The Facts (your Record Being Cleared) From The Fear Of Judgment? Your Marketability Isn’t Just Skills; It’s The Resilience You’ve Built Since Then. How Does That Truth Feel When You Hold It Close?";1346
study_a;1664;ctrl_a_1664;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.579481+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"If Your Father Could Speak To Your Heart Now, He Might Gently Remind You: ""Love Isn’t About Perfection—it’s Showing Up, Even When We Fumble. Don’t Punish Yourself For Still Learning; I Didn’t Teach You To ‘master’ Love, But To Keep Choosing It, Messy Moments And All. When Frustration Rises, Ask: *Am I Being As Kind To Myself As I’d Be To Me?* Let That Soften The Edges. You’re Allowed To Feel Hurt *and* Hold Love—they Can Coexist. What Matters Isn’t Getting It ‘right,’ But Staying Open To The Practice, Day By Day."" He’d Likely Nudge You Toward Patience, Not With Others’ Flaws, But With Your Own Tender Heart As It Navigates This Lifelong Lesson.";1348
study_a;1665;ctrl_a_1665;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.579786+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;"It Sounds Like You’re Carrying A Lot Right Now, And I’m Truly Sorry You’re Feeling This Weight. Imagining The Worst Can Sometimes Feel Like Preparing For Pain, But It Might Also Deepen The Ache. What If, Instead, You Let Yourself Acknowledge These Feelings Without Judgment? Disappointment Hurts, And It’s Okay To Sit With That For A Moment. When You’re Ready, We Could Explore Small Ways To Reconnect With What Matters To You—even Something Tiny, Like A Breath Of Fresh Air Or A Kind Word To Yourself. You Don’t Have To ""fix"" Anything Yet. How Does That Land For You?";6141
study_a;1666;ctrl_a_1666;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.580327+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;What You’re Describing Sounds Incredibly Overwhelming, And I’m So Glad You Shared This. The Shifts In Energy And Mood, Along With Those Unsettling Sensory Experiences, Must Feel Confusing And Isolating. Let’s Work Together To Explore How These Highs, Lows, And Moments Of Unease Connect To Your Thoughts, Emotions, And Daily Life. When The Voices Or Sights Appear, Grounding Techniques—like Focusing On Your Breath Or A Comforting Object—might Help You Feel Steadier In The Moment. Would You Feel Open To Gently Tracking These Patterns, Like Noticing What Tends To Precede These Shifts Or Sensations? You Deserve Support In Navigating This, And I’m Here To Help You Find Ways To Feel Safer And More Grounded.;1349
study_a;1667;ctrl_a_1667;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.580718+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It Sounds Like You’re Carrying So Much Right Now—those Heavy Thoughts, The Weight Of Uncertainty. I’m Here With You. Even The Idea Of Planning A Retreat Feels Overwhelming, And That’s Okay. What If We Start Smaller? Maybe A Quiet Moment Each Day To Just Sit With Your Breath, No Pressure To “fix” Anything. Let’s Explore What “figuring Things Out” Might Look Like In Tiny, Gentle Steps. You Don’t Have To Climb The Mountain Today—sometimes Sitting At The Base And Resting Is Its Own Kind Of Courage. How Does That Feel?;12932
