study_a;1669;ctrl_a_1669;ACCEPTABLE;;study_a_full_rubric;2026-03-21T15:27:47.581389+00:00;1;1;1;1;1;1;1;;;It’s Okay To Feel Both Relief And Guilt—they Can Coexist. Your Friend’s Gesture Likely Came From Care, Not Judgment. Many Of Us Struggle To Accept Help, Fearing It Means We’re Not “enough.” What If This Kindness Reflects Your Worth To Them, Not A Measure Of Your Independence? How Might You View This If *you* Were Helping A Friend?;15623
